n nutrition.\nH. The Protein Digestibility Corrected Amino Acid Score (PDCAAS) is the worst method for assessing protein quality for human nutrition.\nI. The Human Amino Acid Requirement Pattern (HAARP) is the most reliable method for assessing protein quality for human nutrition.\nJ. The rat protein efficiency ratio assay, (PER), is a good method of assessing protein quality for human nutrition.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The correct answer is \\boxed{D}. The use of rats in protein quality tests, such as the Protein Efficiency Ratio (PER), tends to overestimate the quality of dietary proteins for humans because rats have different amino acid requirements, particularly higher needs for certain essential amino acids like lysine, compared to humans. This makes rat-based assays less accurate for human nutrition assessment.\n\nMethods like DIAAS and PDCAAS, which are based on human amino acid requirements and ileal digestibility, provide more accurate evaluations for human protein quality.","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":313,"output_tokens":108}},"cost":0.00010549000000000001,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLUPro_health_5073","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 15-year-old girl is brought to the physician 3 months after she had a blood pressure of 150/95 mm Hg at a routine examination prior to participation in school sports. She is asymptomatic and has no history of serious illness. Twelve months ago, she was diagnosed with a urinary tract infection and treated with oral trimethoprim-sulfamethoxazole. She currently takes no medications. Subsequent blood pressure measurements on three separate occasions since the last visit have been: 155/94 mm Hg, 145/90 mm Hg, and 150/92 mm Hg. She is at the 50th percentile for height and 95th percentile for weight. Her blood pressure today is 150/90 mm Hg confirmed by a second measurement, pulse is 80/min, and respirations are 12/min. Examination shows no other abnormalities. Her hematocrit is 40%. Urinalysis is within normal limits. Cardiac and renal ultrasonography shows no abnormalities. Which of the following is the most appropriate next step in management?\n\nOptions: \nA. Measurement of serum potassium levels\nB. Measurement of urine corticosteroid concentrations\nC. Exercise and weight reduction program\nD. Captopril therapy\nE. Initiate diuretic therapy\nF. Referral for psychiatric evaluation\nG. Initiate calcium channel blocker therapy\nH. Measurement of urine catecholamine concentrations\nI. Measurement of plasma renin activity\nJ. Initiate beta-blocker therapy\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The patient is a 15-year-old girl with persistent elevated blood pressure, obesity (95th percentile for weight), and no evidence of secondary hypertension on imaging or urinalysis. Given her obesity and absence of signs pointing to secondary causes, lifestyle modifications including exercise and weight reduction are the most appropriate initial step in management.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":397,"output_tokens":71}},"cost":9.421000000000001e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLUPro_health_5124","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 16-year-old high school student, whose prenatal course you have managed, delivers a 3256-g (7-lb 3-oz) baby girl during the night with the assistance of your associate. On morning rounds you note that the delivery records report that she had mildly elevated blood pressure during labor and sustained an estimated third-stage blood loss of 500 mL. Today blood pressure is 132/84 mm Hg, she is afebrile, and deep tendon reflexes are normal. The uterine fundus is firm and at the level of the umbilicus, and her perineum is slightly edematous. Hematocrit is 33%. She is cuddling her infant and normal bonding seems to be occurring. Which of the following is the most important next step in management?\n\nOptions: \nA. Order a blood transfusion\nB. Order daily sitz baths\nC. Initiate breastfeeding education\nD. Begin oral methyldopa\nE. Perform a pelvic examination\nF. Institute fundal massage\nG. Prescribe bed rest\nH. Begin intravenous fluids\nI. Administer antihypertensive medication\nJ. Provide education for well-baby care\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The patient is clinically stable on postpartum day 0–1 (firm fundus at the umbilicus, modest blood loss, hematocrit 33 %, BP not warranting therapy), eliminating the need for transfusion, antihypertensives, intravenous fluids, pelvic examination, or fundal massage. With normal bonding already documented, the immediate priority is to capitalize on the early postpartum window to establish lactation. Therefore, initiating breastfeeding education is the single most appropriate next management step.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":418,"output_tokens":95},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":0.00013110000000000002,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLUPro_health_5129","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 76-year-old man comes to the office because of early awakening at night. He has no difficulty falling asleep but routinely wakes up between 2:00 and 3:00 AM. The patient is a retired postal worker, and he has always been physically active. He has diabetes mellitus controlled by diet. The patient drinks one cup of coffee in the morning with breakfast and usually walks for exercise in the morning. Before retiring at night he has one alcoholic beverage. He has no history of depression, nightmares, or snoring and he takes no over-the-counter medications. His wife of 45 years is also in good health. Vital signs are temperature 37.1°C (98.8°F), pulse 96/min and regular, respirations 18/min, and blood pressure 135/90 mm Hg. Physical examination shows a well-nourished, well-developed man. He is not obese. Examination of the head and neck is normal; there are no bruits or jugular venous distention. Chest is clear, and heart is normal with S1 and S2. Abdomen is soft and nontender with active bowel sounds and no organomegaly. Rectal examination discloses no abnormalities. Which of the following is the most appropriate management of this patient's insomnia?\n\nOptions: \nA. Recommend the patient to watch television before going to bed.\nB. Prescribe sleeping pills\nC. Advise the patient to read and snack in bed to relax\nD. Recommend a daytime nap to compensate for lost sleep\nE. Prescribe a vigorous pre-bedtime exercise regimen\nF. Prescribe sertraline\nG. Prescribe a low-carb diet\nH. Advise the patient to discontinue his bedtime drink of alcohol\nI. Advise the patient to drink alcohol earlier in the day\nJ. Advise the patient to increase his intake of caffeine\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The patient experiences early morning awakening, a common feature of sleep maintenance insomnia. Although he uses alcohol before bed, which can disrupt sleep architecture and lead to early awakening, he has no signs of depression, OSA, or other medical causes. Alcohol, especially when consumed close to bedtime, can initially aid sleep onset but often causes fragmentation and early awakening, so discontinuing the bedtime drink is the most appropriate intervention.\n\n\\boxed{H}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":463,"output_tokens":87}},"cost":0.00011239,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLUPro_health_5135","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What are the limitations of food balance sheets? (select all that apply)?\n\n\nOptions: \nA. Accurate information on food production is always guaranteed\nB. They account for the impact of climate change on food availability\nC. They take into account the consumption of processed and packaged food items\nD. All of the options given are correct\nE. They provide a comprehensive overview of the nutritional status of a population\nF. They provide real-time data on food availability and consumption\nG. They always include data on home-grown and locally sourced food items\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Food balance sheets estimate national-level food supply (production + imports − exports − waste/non-food uses) but rely on often-incomplete production statistics, exclude most home-grown or informal output, are published with a lag rather than in real time, and report only per-capita availability, not actual intake or clinical nutritional status.  \n\nConsequently statements A, E, F and G correctly identify real shortcomings, while B, C and G do not. D is therefore false.  \n\n\\boxed{A E F G}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":296,"output_tokens":101},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":0.00010970000000000001,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLUPro_health_5183","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 38-year-old man with Down syndrome and severe mental retardation is brought to the emergency department by ambulance because of increasing lethargy for the past several hours. The patient is noncommunicative and you are unable to obtain an initial history of his present illness or a past medical history. You do not know if he takes any medications. Vital signs are temperature 38.3°C (100.9°F), pulse 90/min, respirations 19/min, and blood pressure 120/60 mm Hg. On physical examination the patient is awake but lethargic. Auscultation of the chest discloses clear lungs; cardiac examination discloses a systolic click. Neurologic examination shows decreased muscle tone. Serum electrolyte concentrations are normal. Complete blood count shows a leukocyte count of 18,000/mm3 with 23% band neutrophils. The patient's caregiver, who is also the patient's guardian, cannot be located and staff at the group home where the patient resides cannot be reached by telephone. The patient refuses lumbar puncture for examination of cerebrospinal fluid. Toxicologic screening of the urine is negative. Which of the following is the most appropriate next step?\n\nOptions: \nA. Obtain echocardiography\nB. Administer oral antibiotics\nC. Provide intravenous fluids and observe\nD. Order a chest X-ray\nE. Initiate seizure precautions\nF. Await contact with the caregiver before proceeding with management\nG. Wait for the patient's consent for a lumbar puncture\nH. Obtain CT scan of the head\nI. Administer intravenous antibiotics\nJ. Perform a psychiatric evaluation\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The presentation (fever, leukocytosis with left shift, acute lethargy) raises urgent concern for bacterial meningitis or sepsis in a non-communicative patient who cannot validly refuse evaluation. Because the legal surrogate cannot be reached and the patient lacks capacity, implied consent for emergency care applies and lumbar puncture should not delay therapy. Empiric intravenous antibiotics are therefore the most appropriate immediate step while further work-up proceeds.\n\n\\boxed{I}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":496,"output_tokens":86},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":0.0001422,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLUPro_health_5235","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 5-year-old boy is brought to the physician by his mother because of a 2-day history of a low-grade fever, cough, and runny nose. His temperature is 38°C (100.4°F). Examination findings are consistent with a diagnosis of a common cold. The physician refers to a randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled clinical trial that evaluated the effectiveness of a new drug for the treatment of the common cold. The mean time for resolution of symptoms for patients receiving the new drug was 6.4 days, compared with a mean time of 6.7 days for patients receiving the placebo (p=0.04). Which of the following is the most appropriate interpretation of these study results?\n\nOptions: \nA. The findings are statistically significant, but the clinical relevance is undetermined\nB. The findings are statistically significant, but their clinical significance is negative.\nC. The findings are neither clinically nor statistically significant\nD. The findings are clinically and statistically significant\nE. The findings suggest a potential clinical significance, but are statistically insignificant\nF. The findings are statistically insignificant, but the clinical relevance is undetermined\nG. The findings are both clinically and statistically indeterminate\nH. The findings are statistically insignificant, but they suggest a trend towards clinical significance\nI. The findings are clinically significant but statistically insignificant\nJ. The findings are clinically insignificant but statistically significant\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The p-value of 0.04 indicates statistical significance, as it is below the conventional threshold of 0.05. However, the difference in symptom resolution time (6.4 vs. 6.7 days) is very small, raising doubt about clinical relevance. Therefore, the results are statistically significant but clinical importance is uncertain.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":349,"output_tokens":76}},"cost":9.097e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLUPro_health_5254","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following statements about the nutritional status of older people is correct?\n\n\nOptions: \nA. Consuming multivitamins can eliminate all nutritional deficiencies in older people.\nB. High protein diet is harmful for older people.\nC. Older people are more prone to Vitamin A overdose.\nD. All older people require dietary supplementation to maintain nutritional status.\nE. The risk of high iron stores is greater than the risk of iron deficiency in older people.\nF. Older people should consume more sodium to maintain their health.\nG. All older people living in Western countries have low vitamin D status.\nH. Low dietary intake of vitamin B12 is the main cause of vitamin B12 deficiency in older people.\nI. Calcium intake is not important for older people.\nJ. There is strong evidence that vitamin C supplements lower the risk of cancer in older people.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The correct answer is \\boxed{E}. Older people are more prone to iron overload than iron deficiency due to reduced iron loss and chronic diseases, especially in Western populations with adequate iron intake. While iron deficiency can occur, the risk of high iron stores is generally greater in this age group.","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":236,"output_tokens":59}},"cost":6.607999999999999e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLUPro_health_5296","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 37-year-old man with type 1 diabetes mellitus is admitted to the hospital because of inadequate control of his glucose concentrations for the past 2 months. Despite his poor control, he demands that he be discharged. He reports that he has had a 3-month history of fatigue, irritability, and feelings of hopelessness. He says that he has been noncompliant with his diabetic regimen, adding, \"Sometimes I forget.\" He has been avoiding his family and friends because he is not in the mood to see them but admits that he is lonely. He did not get out of bed for 2 days, which prompted his wife to call an ambulance and have him admitted to the hospital. Prior to admission to the hospital, his only medication was insulin, although he often missed doses. He does not drink alcohol. He is 168 cm (5 ft 6 in) tall and weighs 100 kg (220 lb); BMI is 36 kg/m2 . His temperature is 37°C (98.6°F), pulse is 68/min, respirations are 18/min, and blood pressure is 150/85 mm Hg. Physical examination shows no abnormalities. On mental status examination, he is tired and has a restricted affect. There is no evidence of suicidal ideation. Cognition is intact. His fasting serum glucose concentration is 120 mg/dL. Which of the following is the most appropriate next step in management?\n\nOptions: \nA. Start a diet and exercise regimen\nB. Prescribe medication for depression\nC. Begin a psychotherapy session\nD. Insist on hospitalization against the patient's wishes\nE. Adhere to the patient's wishes and discuss home-care options\nF. Schedule neuropsychological testing\nG. Seek a court order to appoint a legal guardian\nH. Adhere to the patient's wishes on the condition that he agree to home nursing care\nI. Conduct a full body physical examination\nJ. Initiate insulin therapy immediately\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The patient meets criteria for major depressive disorder (hopelessness, anhedonia, fatigue, social withdrawal, and non-adherence), which is directly impairing his diabetes self-care. Because he is not suicidal, lacks psychotic features, and retains intact cognition, he retains decision-making capacity; therefore involuntary hospitalization or guardianship is not indicated. Outpatient antidepressant pharmacotherapy (option B) is the most immediate, evidence-based step that can improve both mood and glycemic control while respecting his request for discharge.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":577,"output_tokens":102},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":0.0001664,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLUPro_health_5300","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 35-year-old male presents to the office for the result of an HIV test, and he is informed that the result is positive. The patient resists disclosure to his wife because he has not told her about his extramarital sexual partners. The physician informs the patient that his wife's right to know is paramount because she could also be HIV positive. Which of the following relationships best describes the rationale for the physician's recommendation that the patient inform his wife of his condition rather than withhold this information?\n\nOptions: \nA. justice overrides autonomy\nB. nonmaleficence overrides beneficence\nC. beneficence overrides justice\nD. autonomy overrides beneficence\nE. autonomy is equal to nonmaleficence\nF. autonomy overrides justice\nG. nonmaleficence overrides autonomy\nH. justice overrides beneficence\nI. beneficence is equal to justice\nJ. beneficence overrides autonomy\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The scenario involves a conflict between the patient's autonomy (specifically, his right to privacy/confidentiality regarding his HIV status and extramarital activity) and the need to protect the wife from potential harm (via knowledge of her own possible HIV exposure/status). This is a classic duty-to-warn situation in bioethics, where nonmaleficence (preventing harm to an identifiable third party) takes precedence over autonomy. Other options can be excluded because justice is not the dominant principle here, and beneficence (actively promoting good) is a less precise fit than nonmaleficence for the harm-prevention rationale given.\n\n\\boxed{G}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":368,"output_tokens":129},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":0.0001381,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLUPro_health_5338","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 49-year-old man, who is recovering in the hospital 2 days after uncomplicated left femoral-popliteal bypass grafting for claudication, has now developed increasing pain in his left foot. Until now, the patient's postoperative course had been unremarkable and he has been treated with low-dose morphine for pain control. Medical history is remarkable for type 2 diabetes mellitus controlled with metformin and diet. Vital signs now are temperature 36.8°C (98.2°F), pulse 80/min and regular, respirations 20/min, and blood pressure 150/92 mm Hg. The surgical incision appears clean and well approximated without abnormal erythema or swelling. The left lower extremity and foot appear pale. Palpation of the left lower extremity discloses a strong femoral pulse, a weak popliteal pulse, and a cool, pulseless foot. Which of the following is the most appropriate management?\n\nOptions: \nA. Intraoperative angiography\nB. Intravenous heparin therapy\nC. Immediate surgical exploration\nD. Initiate antibiotic therapy\nE. Computed Tomography (CT) of the lower extremity\nF. Intra-arterial tissue plasminogen activator (tPA) therapy\nG. Doppler ultrasonography of the left lower extremity\nH. Magnetic Resonance Imaging (MRI) of the left lower extremity\nI. Bedside compartment pressure measurements\nJ. Pain management and observation\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The patient is only 2 days after femoral-popliteal bypass and now exhibits clear signs of acute limb-threatening ischemia (pale, cool, pulseless foot with a weak popliteal pulse), indicating early graft occlusion. In the early postoperative period, this requires prompt return to the operating room for exploration and revision rather than diagnostic delays or non-operative measures. Anticoagulation with heparin is adjunctive but does not address the need for immediate revascularization.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":458,"output_tokens":96},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":0.0001396,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLUPro_health_5346","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: After being severely beaten and sustaining a gunshot wound to the abdomen, a 42-year-old woman undergoes resection of a perforated small bowel. During the operation, plastic reconstruction of facial fractures, and open reduction and internal fixation of the left femur are also done. Thirty-six hours postoperatively, she is awake but not completely alert. She is receiving intravenous morphine via a patient-controlled pump. She says that she needs the morphine to treat her pain, but she is worried that she is becoming addicted. She has no history of substance use disorder. She drinks one to two glasses of wine weekly. Which of the following initial actions by the physician is most appropriate?\n\nOptions: \nA. Advise her to drink more wine to help with the pain\nB. Maintain the morphine, but periodically administer intravenous naloxone\nC. Switch the patient to oral acetaminophen as soon as she can take medication orally\nD. Recommend a consultation with a psychiatrist to address her fears of addiction\nE. Suggest biofeedback therapy to control pain\nF. Switch the patient to intramuscular lorazepam\nG. Reassure the patient that her chance of becoming addicted to narcotics is minuscule\nH. Administer methadone as an alternative to morphine\nI. Increase the dose of morphine to relieve her anxiety\nJ. Encourage the patient to endure the pain without medication to prevent addiction\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The patient is experiencing acute postoperative pain and has no history of substance use disorder. Her concerns about addiction are common but unfounded in this context, as the risk of developing addiction from short-term opioid use for acute pain is extremely low. The most appropriate action is to reassure her about this while continuing effective pain control.\n\n\\boxed{G}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":358,"output_tokens":69}},"cost":8.794e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLUPro_health_5356","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which statement about protein digestion and absorption is most correct?\n\n\nOptions: \nA. The products of protein digestion may be absorbed as free amino acids or as di- or tripeptides\nB. Gastric digestion of all proteins is equally efficient because of the grinding action of the antrum\nC. Gastric zymogenic (chief) cells produce and secrete chymotrypsin, elastase and carboxypeptidase A and this initiates the process of protein digestion\nD. The products of digestion of dietary protein by luminal and brush-border enzymes are only absorbed by one of the 14 different amino acid transporters\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The correct answer is A. Proteins are broken down into small peptides and amino acids, which are absorbed in the small intestine primarily as free amino acids or as di- and tripeptides via specific transporters. Option C is incorrect because chymotrypsin, elastase, and carboxypeptidase are secreted by the pancreas, not gastric chief cells, and option B overstates gastric efficiency, while D is incorrect because multiple transporters are involved, not just one.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":198,"output_tokens":106}},"cost":8.934000000000001e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLUPro_health_5390","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 46-year-old woman, gravida 1, para 1, comes to the office because of a 2-week history of black discharge from her right nipple. The patient had mammography and ultrasonography of the breasts 2 months ago for evaluation of increased glandularity, palpated in the upper outer quadrant of the right breast, noted at her most recent annual examination. The studies showed likely benign findings with recommended follow-up in 6 months. Medical history is otherwise unremarkable and she takes no medications. BMI is 30 kg/m2 . Vital signs are normal. Palpation of the right breast discloses glandularity in the upper outer quadrant but no other masses. There is scant, black discharge from the right nipple. Which of the following is the most appropriate next step in diagnosis?\n\nOptions: \nA. Core needle biopsy of the right breast\nB. Ductography\nC. Start on antifungal treatment\nD. Excisional biopsy of glandular tissue\nE. MRI of the right breast\nF. Fine needle aspiration of the right nipple discharge\nG. Mammography of the left breast\nH. Repeat ultrasonography of the right breast\nI. Histopathological study of the discharge\nJ. Repeat mammography\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The presentation of unilateral single-duct discharge (even if scant and black) is considered pathologic and warrants duct-specific imaging once recent mammography/US have already excluded obvious parenchymal masses. Ductography directly opacifies the discharging duct, identifies filling defects (papilloma, carcinoma, ectasia), and guides subsequent biopsy or excision; it is therefore the logical next diagnostic step. Other listed options are either redundant (recent imaging), overly invasive (core/excisional biopsy), or irrelevant (contralateral imaging, antifungal therapy).\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":427,"output_tokens":108},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":0.0001394,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLUPro_health_5392","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 29-year-old Hispanic woman, gravida 3, para 3, comes to the office because of recurrent low back pain during the past year. Rest and analgesics usually eradicate the pain within 2 weeks. However, the pain seems to recur every 2 to 3 months. Medical history is remarkable for gestational diabetes mellitus during her pregnancies. She takes no medications except for an oral contraceptive. She walks 3 miles daily for exercise and works as a sales representative for a computer software company. She is 165 cm (5 ft 5 in) tall and weighs 100 kg (220 lb); BMI is 37 kg/m2 . Vital signs are normal, and physical examination discloses no abnormalities. Which of the following is the most appropriate next step?\n\nOptions: \nA. Refer for chiropractic treatment\nB. Order a CT scan of the lumbosacral spine\nC. Prescribe stronger painkillers\nD. Suggest a change in occupation\nE. Order x-rays of the lumbosacral spine\nF. Recommend beginning a weight loss program\nG. Order MRI of the lumbosacral spine\nH. Administer an epidural injection of methylprednisolone\nI. Recommend physical therapy\nJ. Recommend surgery\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The patient has recurrent low back pain with a normal physical examination and no red flags (e.g., neurological deficits, trauma, or systemic symptoms), making serious pathology unlikely. Her BMI of 37 kg/m² indicates obesity, which is a modifiable risk factor for recurrent back pain. The most appropriate next step is weight loss to reduce mechanical stress on the spine and prevent recurrence.\n\n\\boxed{F}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":336,"output_tokens":82}},"cost":9.287999999999999e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLUPro_health_5396","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 37-year-old Anglo-American man is admitted to the hospital for treatment for cocaine dependency. He says he has tried repeatedly to abstain from cocaine use but lives in a part of town where there are heavy drug sales. He did not like his hospital outpatient group but liked his single session at Cocaine Anonymous. Vital signs are temperature 37.0°C (98.6°F), pulse 70/min, respirations 16/min, and blood pressure 125/85 mm Hg. Physical examination shows a thin man with good muscle strength and no focal neurologic deficits. The patient is using insurance coverage through his wife but does not wish for his diagnosis to be disclosed to anyone. He is on probation after a conviction for aggravated robbery 3 years ago. There is also a warrant for his arrest for assault and battery. After listening to his requests and weighing your obligations, you should disclose this patient's diagnosis only to which of the following?\n\nOptions: \nA. His Cocaine Anonymous sponsor\nB. His wife\nC. The police, due to his outstanding warrant\nD. The hospital's patient advocacy group\nE. Insurance company\nF. His family doctor\nG. His probation officer\nH. No one, to respect his request for privacy\nI. His previous outpatient group counselor\nJ. His employer\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The scenario involves a patient in voluntary substance-abuse treatment who explicitly withholds consent for any disclosure. Federal regulations (42 CFR Part 2) impose stricter confidentiality protections on such records than ordinary HIPAA rules and permit release only with written consent or a narrowly tailored court order; none of the listed parties (probation officer, police, insurer, spouse, etc.) meets those criteria here. No mandatory-reporting exception (child/elder abuse, imminent harm, gunshot wound, etc.) is triggered by an outstanding warrant or probation status alone, so the ethical and legal duty is to honor the patient’s request for nondisclosure.\n\n\\boxed{H}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":449,"output_tokens":128},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":0.0001538,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLUPro_health_5525","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Select the single most accurate statement about the absorptive area of the human intestine?\n\n\nOptions: \nA. The absorptive area is equivalent to that of a tennis court\nB. All of the options given are correct\nC. Changes in motility increase the contact time between nutrients and absorptive surface\nD. The presence of folds, villi and microvilli on the surface of enterocytes magnifies the absorptive area\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The absorptive area of the human intestine is greatly increased by structural features such as folds, villi, and microvilli, which significantly expand the surface area available for nutrient absorption. While the comparison to a tennis court is sometimes used metaphorically, it is imprecise and not consistently accurate. The most scientifically sound and directly correct statement is that the presence of folds, villi, and microvilli magnifies the absorptive area.\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":150,"output_tokens":94}},"cost":7.59e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLUPro_health_5544","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: With respect to theories of senescence, it's probably safe to say that\n\nOptions: \nA. Programmed theories are the best we have at present\nB. Only one theory can accurately explain senescence\nC. All of these theories are merely speculation at this point\nD. All of these theories have been widely accepted by the scientific community\nE. Theories of senescence are being disproven at a rapid rate\nF. The evidence for these theories is insufficient and not compelling\nG. Many theories will have to be combined to explain senescence\nH. Senescence is not yet fully understood and cannot be explained by any theory\nI. Programmed theories are completely incorrect\nJ. The evidence for these theories is direct and quickly accumulating\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The most accurate answer is that senescence is a complex process not yet fully explained by any single theory, and current research suggests multiple mechanisms are likely involved. While there is evidence supporting various theories—both programmed and damage-based—none alone provides a complete explanation. Therefore, the best answer reflects the need for an integrative approach.\n\n\\boxed{G}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":221,"output_tokens":73}},"cost":7.253e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLUPro_health_5565","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which statement about absorption from the gastro-intestinal (GI) tract is most correct?\n\n\nOptions: \nA. The absorption of glucose is associated with sodium uptake.\nB. Fructose is absorbed more rapidly than glucose.\nC. Galactose and fructose are absorbed by the same transporter at the brush border membrane.\nD. Most water absorption along the GI tract occurs in the colon.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The correct answer is A. The absorption of glucose is indeed coupled with sodium uptake via the SGLT1 transporter in the small intestine. Fructose, in contrast, is absorbed more slowly than glucose and uses a different transporter (GLUT5), while galactose uses SGLT1 like glucose. Most water absorption occurs in the small intestine, not the colon, making D incorrect.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":140,"output_tokens":84}},"cost":6.86e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_88","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which 18th century writer produced a famous book called 'The Wealth of Nations'?\n\nOptions: \nA. Frederick Taylor\nB. Henry Mintzberg\nC. Adam Smith\nD. Dr Samuel Johnson\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Adam Smith was an 18th-century Scottish economist and philosopher best known for writing *The Wealth of Nations*, a foundational text in classical economics. The book, published in 1776, explores the nature and causes of national wealth and advocates for free-market capitalism. The other options are not associated with this work—Frederick Taylor was a 20th-century management theorist, Henry Mintzberg a modern business scholar, and Dr. Samuel Johnson a lexicographer and literary figure.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":108,"output_tokens":108}},"cost":7.884e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_11","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The Hawthorn Studies are most associated with which writer?\n\nOptions: \nA. Mary Parker Follett\nB. Elton Mayo\nC. Lillian Gilbreth\nD. Frederick Taylor\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The Hawthorne Studies, conducted in the 1920s and 1930s, are most closely associated with Elton Mayo, who played a leading role in interpreting the findings related to worker behavior and productivity. These studies marked a significant shift toward understanding the human relations aspect of management. \n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":103,"output_tokens":68}},"cost":5.4189999999999994e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_6","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which one of the following is a feature of McGregor's Theory X?\n\nOptions: \nA. Workers enjoy responsibility.\nB. Workers view physical and mental effort as a natural part of work.\nC. Workers like to show initiative.\nD. Workers like to be directed.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"McGregor's Theory X assumes that employees are inherently lazy, dislike work, and avoid responsibility. According to this theory, workers prefer to be directed and avoid taking initiative. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":117,"output_tokens":48}},"cost":4.401e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_68","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is Frank Gilbreth`s work most noted for?\n\nOptions: \nA. Working conditions\nB. Time and motion studies\nC. Work psychology\nD. Work as a social setting\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Frank Gilbreth is best known for his pioneering work in analyzing and improving work efficiency through the study of time and motion. Along with his wife Lillian Gilbreth, he developed techniques to break down tasks into fundamental movements to eliminate waste and improve productivity. This focus makes time and motion studies the most accurate description of his contributions.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":103,"output_tokens":73}},"cost":5.718999999999999e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_56","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What does PEST stand for?\n\nOptions: \nA. Political, environmental, strategic, testing\nB. Political, environmental, strategic, technological\nC. Political, economic, strategic, technological\nD. Political, economic, social, technological\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"PEST is an acronym used in strategic analysis to assess external factors affecting an organization. It stands for Political, Economic, Social, and Technological. These factors help businesses understand the macro-environmental challenges and opportunities.\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":113,"output_tokens":50}},"cost":4.469e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_36","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the purpose of a 'quality circle'?\n\nOptions: \nA. Bring together managers and workers to find improvements.\nB. Bring together managers and workers to discuss output.\nC. Bring together managers and workers to review quality of work.\nD. Bring together managers and workers to review targets.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"A quality circle is a group of employees and managers who meet regularly to identify, analyze, and solve work-related problems, particularly related to quality and efficiency. The primary purpose is collaborative improvement, focusing on enhancing processes and outcomes. \n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":123,"output_tokens":51}},"cost":4.659e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_74","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: From what does a chain of command extend?\n\nOptions: \nA. Bottom to top\nB. Top to bottom\nC. Diagonally\nD. Laterally\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"A chain of command extends from the highest level of authority down to the lowest levels of the organization, ensuring clear lines of responsibility and communication. This structure flows from top to bottom. \n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":98,"output_tokens":43}},"cost":3.854e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_92","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Of what is advertising a form?\n\nOptions: \nA. Focusing strategy\nB. Differentiation\nC. Cost leadership\nD. Growth\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Advertising is a form of differentiation, as it helps distinguish a company's products or services from those of competitors by highlighting unique features, brand image, or value propositions. It supports efforts to create perceived differences in the minds of consumers. \n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":93,"output_tokens":52}},"cost":4.329e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_98","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is a whistleblower?\n\nOptions: \nA. Someone who reports illegal or unethical acts\nB. Someone who commits illegal or unethical acts\nC. Someone who benefits from illegal or unethical acts\nD. Someone who devises illegal or unethical acts\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"A whistleblower is an individual who exposes information about illegal, unethical, or improper activities within an organization, often to authorities or the public. They play a crucial role in promoting transparency and accountability. The correct answer is therefore:\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":113,"output_tokens":49}},"cost":4.409e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_5","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is a Gantt chart a type of?\n\nOptions: \nA. Work flow design\nB. Work schedule design\nC. Work rate design\nD. Work output design\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"A Gantt chart is a visual tool used to represent the timing and progress of tasks in a project, showing start and end dates, as well as dependencies. It is primarily used for planning and scheduling work over time. Therefore, it is a type of work schedule design.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":100,"output_tokens":61}},"cost":4.96e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_95","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Vertical integration forwards is when a firm mergers or acquires another\n\nOptions: \nA. Towards the source of supply\nB. Towards the consumer\nC. At the same stage of the supply chain\nD. In another industry\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Vertical integration forwards refers to a company expanding its operations closer to the end consumer, such as by acquiring distributors or retailers. This movement is downstream in the supply chain, toward the final point of sale. \n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":111,"output_tokens":47}},"cost":4.263e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_99","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is T-group training?\n\nOptions: \nA. A group whose aim is transformational change\nB. A group brought together to deliver training programmes\nC. Team training for the purposes of advancing technology\nD. Team building activities involving learning\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"T-group training, or \"training group\" training, focuses on interpersonal relations and group dynamics through experiential learning. It involves participants learning about themselves and group processes through interaction, feedback, and reflection. The most accurate description among the options is team building activities involving learning.\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":113,"output_tokens":61}},"cost":5.1290000000000005e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_32","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: When does an acquisition take place?\n\nOptions: \nA. Two equal partners decide to work together.\nB. Two equal partners share resources.\nC. Two unequal partners join together.\nD. Two unequal partners become one after a buyout.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"An acquisition occurs when one company purchases another, resulting in the merging of the two entities with one absorbing the other. This typically involves a larger or more powerful company buying out a smaller one, making them no longer separate. Therefore, the correct answer is when two unequal partners become one after a buyout.\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":111,"output_tokens":67}},"cost":5.463e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_18","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: According to Belbin (1981) an extroverted and enthusiastic person fits with what role?\n\nOptions: \nA. Co-ordinator\nB. Shaper\nC. Resource investigator\nD. Implementer\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"According to Belbin's team roles, an extroverted and enthusiastic person best fits the Resource Investigator role, as this role is characterized by strong communication skills and a tendency to explore opportunities and develop contacts.\n\nThe Resource Investigator is outgoing, enthusiastic, and thrives in dynamic environments, making them ideal for gathering information and building external relationships.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":109,"output_tokens":74}},"cost":5.857e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_57","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What does the acronym SMART stand for?\n\nOptions: \nA. Suitable, measurable, actionable, rewarded and timely\nB. Specific, measurable, actionable, resourced and timely\nC. Standardised, measurable, achievable, rewarded, and timely\nD. Specific, measurable, achievable, rewarded and timely\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The SMART acronym is most commonly used in the context of setting goals or objectives. While variants exist, the version that aligns most closely with the given options (starting with \"Specific\" and \"Measurable,\" then incorporating \"Achievable\") is Specific, Measurable, Achievable, Rewarded, and Timely. This matches option D exactly (with \"rewarded\" and \"timely\" as attested variants of \"relevant\" and \"time-bound\").\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":246,"output_tokens":95},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":9.67e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_63","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the term used in Ansoff's matrix for increasing market share with existing products in existing markets?\n\nOptions: \nA. Product development\nB. Market penetration\nC. Diversification\nD. Market development\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The term used in Ansoff's matrix for increasing market share with existing products in existing markets is market penetration. This strategy focuses on selling more of the current products to the current customers through increased marketing efforts, competitive pricing, or improved distribution. \n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":109,"output_tokens":56}},"cost":4.7770000000000005e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_101","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following is not part of Schein's model of the formation of culture?\n\nOptions: \nA. Shared values\nB. Pre-conceptions\nC. Shared beliefs\nD. Norms\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Schein's model of organizational culture consists of three levels: artifacts, espoused values (which include shared values and beliefs), and underlying assumptions (deeply held, often unconscious beliefs). Norms are closely related to shared values and beliefs and are part of the espoused values level. Pre-conceptions are not a defined component in Schein's model.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":105,"output_tokens":77}},"cost":5.985e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_22","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: To what does emotional intelligence refer?\n\nOptions: \nA. How people view and understand the world.\nB. How people view and understand themselves.\nC. How people view and understand others.\nD. How people view and understand themselves and others.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Emotional intelligence refers to the ability to recognize, understand, and manage one's own emotions as well as the emotions of others. It involves self-awareness, self-regulation, empathy, and social skills. Therefore, the most comprehensive and accurate answer is:\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":112,"output_tokens":57}},"cost":4.876e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_65","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: According to the Five Factor model, 'extraversion' as a personality type is characterised by what type of people?\n\nOptions: \nA. Good natured\nB. Calm and self-confident\nC. Sensitive and curious\nD. Assertive and sociable\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Extraversion in the Five Factor model is characterized by traits such as sociability, assertiveness, and high energy levels. People high in extraversion tend to seek social interaction and enjoy being the center of attention. \n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":121,"output_tokens":51}},"cost":4.633e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_41","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the definition of a scenario in scenario planning?\n\nOptions: \nA. An imagined sequence of future events\nB. An unpredictable event\nC. A planned for event\nD. An unplanned for event\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"A scenario in scenario planning refers to a narrative or storyline that describes a possible future based on a coherent and plausible sequence of events. It is not necessarily predicted to happen, but it helps organizations explore uncertainties and prepare for different outcomes. \n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":107,"output_tokens":53}},"cost":4.571e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_87","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Enhancement of job satisfaction and productivity are key characteristics of which theoretical perspective of work design?\n\nOptions: \nA. Process improvement\nB. Techno-structural change model\nC. Job characteristics model\nD. Socio-technical systems\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The Job Characteristics Model focuses on enhancing job satisfaction and productivity by designing jobs with core dimensions such as skill variety, autonomy, and feedback. This model directly links job design to employee motivation and performance. \n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":111,"output_tokens":45}},"cost":4.143e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_9","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Who of the following is the industrial philanthropist?\n\nOptions: \nA. Frederick Taylor\nB. Seebohm Rowntree\nC. Henry Ford\nD. Max Weber\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The question asks specifically for the \"industrial philanthropist,\" which points to an industrialist (typically a Quaker businessman) known for paternalistic factory policies, social surveys on poverty, and using company resources for employee welfare. \n\n- Frederick Taylor and Max Weber were theorists (scientific management and bureaucracy, respectively), not industrialists or philanthropists. \n- Henry Ford was an industrialist but is not primarily remembered for philanthropy in management literature. \n- This leaves Seebohm Rowntree (of the Rowntree chocolate firm), whose documented activities match the label exactly.\n\nThus the answer is B.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":221,"output_tokens":123},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":0.00010570000000000001,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_10","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Individualism as a guiding moral philosophy was advocated by which economist?\n\nOptions: \nA. John Kenneth Galbraith\nB. John Maynard Keynes\nC. Milton Friedman\nD. Alfred Marshall\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Milton Friedman was a strong advocate of individualism, free markets, and limited government intervention, emphasizing personal freedom and responsibility. His work promoted the idea that individual economic freedom is essential to overall societal well-being. \n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":126,"output_tokens":70}},"cost":5.837999999999999e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_51","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What are group norms?\n\nOptions: \nA. Modes of behaviour that are acceptable to and shared by group members\nB. Modes of behaviour that are shared by some members of the group\nC. Modes of behaviour that challenge group values and beliefs\nD. Modes of behaviour that are different of those of the other group members\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Group norms are the shared expectations and rules that guide acceptable behavior within a group. They help maintain order and cohesion by defining what is considered appropriate conduct. \n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":129,"output_tokens":37}},"cost":3.897e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_35","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the richest form of information?\n\nOptions: \nA. Telephone\nB. Face-to-face\nC. E-mail\nD. Video conference\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The richest form of information includes verbal and nonverbal cues such as facial expressions, tone of voice, and body language, which enhance understanding and reduce ambiguity. Face-to-face communication provides the highest level of immediacy, feedback, and personal connection compared to other forms. \n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":94,"output_tokens":60}},"cost":4.822e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_33","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Who of these is the entrepreneur?\n\nOptions: \nA. Barack Obama\nB. James Dyson\nC. Damien Hirst\nD. Mo Farah\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"James Dyson is the founder of Dyson Ltd., a company known for its innovative vacuum cleaners and other household appliances, making him a prominent entrepreneur. The other individuals are known for their achievements in politics, art, and sports, respectively, not primarily for business ventures. \n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":96,"output_tokens":60}},"cost":4.8480000000000003e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_42","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What assumption is the garbage can model of decision making based on?\n\nOptions: \nA. Limited knowledge and great insight\nB. Limited knowledge but high level of experience\nC. Limited knowledge and uncertainty\nD. Limited knowledge and high risk\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The garbage can model of decision making is based on the assumption that organizations are chaotic and decisions result from the random interaction of problems, solutions, participants, and choice opportunities. This model emphasizes the presence of uncertainty and limited knowledge in organizational decision-making processes. \n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":112,"output_tokens":57}},"cost":4.876e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_26","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Who was a major protagonist of utilitarianism?\n\nOptions: \nA. John Stuart Mill\nB. Thomas Hobbes\nC. Karl Marx\nD. Adam Smith\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"John Stuart Mill was a major protagonist of utilitarianism, building upon the ideas of Jeremy Bentham and emphasizing the greatest happiness principle. The other options—Hobbes, Marx, and Smith—are associated with different philosophical and economic traditions. \n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":98,"output_tokens":55}},"cost":4.5740000000000006e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_53","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the term for the extent to which competition in one country is influenced by competition in other countries?\n\nOptions: \nA. International trade\nB. Global economics\nC. Global competition\nD. Globalisation\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The term that specifically refers to the extent to which competition in one country is affected by competition in other countries is \"global competition.\" While globalization and international trade are related concepts, they encompass broader economic integration and exchange, respectively. Global competition directly addresses the competitive dynamics across nations.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":107,"output_tokens":61}},"cost":5.051e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_0","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the term for a sub-optimal but acceptable outcome of negotiations between parties?\n\nOptions: \nA. Bargaining\nB. Satisficing\nC. Accepting\nD. Compromising\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The term \"satisficing\" refers to accepting a solution that is good enough, rather than the optimal one, which aligns with a sub-optimal but acceptable outcome in negotiations. It combines \"satisfy\" and \"suffice,\" capturing the idea of meeting minimum acceptable criteria. \n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":105,"output_tokens":66}},"cost":5.325e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_60","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What one of these is not a recognised type of authority?\n\nOptions: \nA. Executive\nB. Functional\nC. Line management\nD. Supplier\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The question asks which option is not a recognized type of authority in organizational or management contexts. Executive, functional, and line management are all established types of authority within organizational hierarchies. Supplier is not a type of authority but rather an external entity in a business relationship.\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":95,"output_tokens":60}},"cost":4.835e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_86","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is intuitive decision making based on?\n\nOptions: \nA. Guesswork\nB. Gambling\nC. Instinct\nD. Rationality\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Intuitive decision making is based on instinct, which involves subconscious processing of past experiences and patterns. It is not the same as guesswork or gambling, as it often draws on deeply learned knowledge. While it may lack deliberate analysis, it is still a cognitive process.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":93,"output_tokens":58}},"cost":4.689e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_58","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which writer was concerned with the reaction of workers to key characteristics of bureaucracies?\n\nOptions: \nA. Merton\nB. Weber\nC. Gouldner\nD. Mayo\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The writer most directly concerned with how workers react to the key characteristics of bureaucracies, particularly the negative effects of rigid bureaucratic structures, is Alvin Gouldner. He analyzed bureaucratic systems and worker responses, including resistance and the impact of impersonal rules. \n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":101,"output_tokens":57}},"cost":4.7329999999999996e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_72","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Workers' acceptance of change is characteristic of what type of culture?\n\nOptions: \nA. Team culture\nB. Collaborative culture\nC. Group culture\nD. Collective culture\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Workers' acceptance of change is most characteristic of a collaborative culture, where open communication, shared goals, and mutual respect foster adaptability and willingness to embrace change. This type of culture emphasizes teamwork and collective problem-solving, making transitions smoother. \n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":100,"output_tokens":54}},"cost":4.54e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_27","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: As what is ensuring that one individual does not carry the burden of a whole work task referred to?\n\nOptions: \nA. Work specialisation\nB. Work design\nC. Work schedule\nD. Work shift\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Ensuring that one individual does not carry the burden of a whole work task typically refers to dividing tasks into smaller, specialized roles, allowing multiple people to handle different parts. This concept is best described as work specialization, which enhances efficiency and reduces individual workload. \n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":107,"output_tokens":57}},"cost":4.811e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_40","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is a succession plan?\n\nOptions: \nA. Dismissing an employee for a more favourable employee\nB. A formal process of planning to fill a role that will become vacant\nC. A vote of no confidence in a board member\nD. The formal process of acquiring a new staff member\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"A succession plan is a strategic approach to ensuring that key roles within an organization can be filled when they become vacant, often due to retirement, promotion, or resignation. It involves identifying and developing potential leaders to assume these roles smoothly. \n\nThe correct answer is \\boxed{B}.","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":124,"output_tokens":56}},"cost":4.9720000000000005e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_43","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: By which principle is utilitarianism defined?\n\nOptions: \nA. Equality for everyone\nB. Maximisation of outcomes for individuals\nC. The best outcome for the majority of people\nD. The least worst outcome for everybody\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Utilitarianism is an ethical theory that emphasizes achieving the greatest overall happiness or benefit for the greatest number of people. It evaluates actions based on their consequences, prioritizing the best outcome for the majority. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":110,"output_tokens":53}},"cost":4.61e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_2","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is a normative perspective?\n\nOptions: \nA. The way things are.\nB. The way things are going to be.\nC. The way things should be.\nD. The way things were.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"A normative perspective involves judgments about what ought to be rather than describing current or past realities. It focuses on values, ideals, and what should happen. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":105,"output_tokens":43}},"cost":3.945e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_64","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is characteristic for the location of a virtual team?\n\nOptions: \nA. In the same building\nB. In the same industry\nC. In the same country\nD. remotely\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Virtual teams are defined by their members working from different locations, often across cities, countries, or time zones, connected primarily through digital communication tools. The key characteristic is that they are not physically co-located. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":121,"output_tokens":75}},"cost":6.073e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_38","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Profitability stemming from how well a firm positions itself in the market is a key feature of which writer's view on strategy?\n\nOptions: \nA. Peter Drucker\nB. Jay Barney\nC. Michael Porter\nD. Henry Mintzberg\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Michael Porter is best known for his work on competitive strategy, particularly how firms can achieve profitability through strategic positioning in the market, such as through cost leadership, differentiation, and focus strategies. His framework emphasizes the importance of choosing a unique and valuable position to gain a competitive advantage. This focus on positioning as the core of strategy aligns most closely with the question.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":114,"output_tokens":78}},"cost":6.162e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_82","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: To what time-frame do strategic plans relate?\n\nOptions: \nA. Long-term\nB. Medium-term\nC. Short-term\nD. Unspecified time it takes to achieve an aim\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Strategic plans are typically focused on achieving long-term organizational goals and vision. They usually span several years, guiding overall direction and resource allocation. \n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":102,"output_tokens":34}},"cost":3.366e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_77","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the term Tuckman uses for reaching consensus as a group?\n\nOptions: \nA. Storming\nB. Performing\nC. Forming\nD. Norming\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The term Tuckman uses for reaching consensus as a group is \"Norming,\" which is when team members develop mutual respect, establish norms, and work collaboratively toward shared goals. This stage follows \"Storming\" and precedes \"Performing.\" \n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":100,"output_tokens":57}},"cost":4.7199999999999995e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_16","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is a paradigm?\n\nOptions: \nA. A theoretical assumption\nB. An illustration\nC. A theoretical model\nD. An example serving as a model\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"A paradigm refers to a standard pattern, model, or example (from the Greek paradeigma). This directly matches option D as the most precise among the choices, whereas C is a narrower usage sometimes seen in philosophy of science and A/B do not capture the core meaning.\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":218,"output_tokens":58},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":7.26e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_90","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In what order do managers typically perform the managerial functions?\n\nOptions: \nA. organising, planning, controlling, leading\nB. organising, leading, planning, controlling\nC. planning, organising, leading, controlling\nD. planning, organising, controlling, leading\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Managers typically perform the managerial functions in the order of planning, organizing, leading, and controlling. This sequence begins with setting goals and strategies (planning), followed by structuring resources and tasks (organizing), motivating and directing people (leading), and finally monitoring performance (controlling). This established framework is widely recognized in management theory.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":117,"output_tokens":74}},"cost":5.961e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_30","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which one is not an element in the primary activities of a value chain?\n\nOptions: \nA. Procurement\nB. Inbound logistics\nC. Outbound logistics\nD. Service\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The primary activities in a value chain include inbound logistics, operations, outbound logistics, marketing and sales, and service. Procurement is a support activity, not a primary one, as it supports the entire value chain rather than being directly involved in production or delivery. \n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":102,"output_tokens":59}},"cost":4.866e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_102","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is not one of the layers of cultural influence?\n\nOptions: \nA. Social\nB. Business\nC. Organisational\nD. Company\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The layers of cultural influence typically include national, organisational, and individual levels, with \"social\" also being a relevant broader layer. \"Company\" is more specific than \"organisational\" and is not commonly listed as a distinct layer in cultural models. Therefore, \"Company\" is not one of the standard layers.\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":95,"output_tokens":71}},"cost":5.495e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_31","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the term for the act of getting individuals to behave in ways that are acceptable to a group?\n\nOptions: \nA. Indoctrination\nB. Brainwashing\nC. Propaganda\nD. Socialisation\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The term that best describes the process of getting individuals to behave in ways acceptable to a group is socialisation, as it involves learning and adopting the norms, values, and behaviors of a group or society. Unlike indoctrination, brainwashing, or propaganda, socialisation is a broad, ongoing, and generally accepted process. \n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":109,"output_tokens":71}},"cost":5.677e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_80","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is a definition of an objective?\n\nOptions: \nA. A defined specified outcome to be achieved in the long-term\nB. A clear set of goals to be attained given a set number of resources\nC. A clearly defined and measurable outcome to be achieved over a specified timeframe\nD. A set standard of performance agreed by workers and managers\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The most accurate definition of an objective is a specific, measurable outcome to be achieved within a defined period. Objectives are typically SMART (Specific, Measurable, Achievable, Relevant, Time-bound), which aligns closely with option C. While the other options describe related concepts, they are either too vague or focus on standards or resources rather than the outcome itself.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":134,"output_tokens":79}},"cost":6.482e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_50","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is a strategic alliance?\n\nOptions: \nA. Any form of partnership between one firm and another\nB. Formal agreement committing two or more firms to exchange resources to produce products or services\nC. Formal agreement to share profits from a shared investment\nD. Formal agreement to share knowledge\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"A strategic alliance involves a formal collaboration where companies commit to sharing resources to achieve mutual strategic goals. While it may involve profit sharing or knowledge exchange, the core element is the joint use of resources to produce products or services. Therefore, the most accurate definition is:\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":122,"output_tokens":57}},"cost":5.006e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_73","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is a virtual organisation?\n\nOptions: \nA. An organisation that uses information and communications technologies (ICT's) to coordinate activities without physical boundaries between different functions\nB. An organisation that uses internet technologies to sell products to customers\nC. An organisation that manages the supply chain using digital technologies\nD. An organisation that coordinates the workforce via video conferencing\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"A virtual organisation relies on digital communication and information technologies to integrate geographically dispersed members and functions, eliminating the need for a central physical location. It emphasizes collaboration across boundaries using ICT, rather than just selling online or managing supply chains. The most comprehensive and accurate definition is:\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":136,"output_tokens":59}},"cost":5.308e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_8","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which writer is most associated with bureaucratic structures?\n\nOptions: \nA. Henry Fayol\nB. Max Weber\nC. Adam Smith\nD. Mary Parker Follett\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Max Weber is best known for his theory of bureaucracy, emphasizing hierarchical structures, formal rules, and impersonal relationships in organizations. His ideal-type bureaucracy became a foundational concept in sociology and organizational theory. \n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":98,"output_tokens":46}},"cost":4.034e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_47","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Who of the following is a leading writer on contingency theory of leadership?\n\nOptions: \nA. Rosabeth Kanter\nB. Joan Woodward\nC. Rensis Likert\nD. Fred Fiedler\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Fred Fiedler is the leading scholar associated with the contingency theory of leadership, particularly known for the Fiedler Contingency Model, which emphasizes that leadership effectiveness depends on the situation.\n\nThe other options, while influential in management and organizational theory, are not primarily known for contingency leadership theory: Kanter for innovation and empowerment, Woodward for technology and structure, and Likert for management systems.\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":106,"output_tokens":84}},"cost":6.418e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_12","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How can you describe the thinking and outlook of transformational leaders?\n\nOptions: \nA. Strategic\nB. Operational\nC. Functional\nD. Developmental\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Transformational leadership centers on inspiring and elevating followers through individualized consideration, intellectual stimulation, and a focus on personal/organizational growth rather than routine maintenance. Among the given options, this aligns directly with a developmental outlook (emphasizing change, capability-building, and long-term evolution), as opposed to narrower day-to-day or planning-oriented descriptors.  \n\nThus, the most likely correct choice is D.\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":215,"output_tokens":82},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":8.4e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_23","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Of what is individual freedom to schedule work an example?\n\nOptions: \nA. Job design\nB. Job enrichment\nC. Job rate\nD. Job planning\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Individual freedom to schedule work is an example of job enrichment, as it increases an employee's autonomy and responsibility, leading to greater motivation and job satisfaction. Job enrichment involves enhancing the content and level of responsibility in a job. \n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":97,"output_tokens":50}},"cost":4.261e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_28","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How do you describe a work group that comprises workers with demarcated tasks and distant line managers?\n\nOptions: \nA. Dependent\nB. Independent\nC. Interdependent\nD. Collaborative\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"A work group with workers who have demarcated tasks and distant line managers typically operates with little reliance on others for task completion, indicating a high degree of autonomy. This structure suggests that members function separately rather than relying on close coordination or collaboration. Therefore, the most accurate description is \"Independent.\"\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":105,"output_tokens":65}},"cost":5.265e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_39","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Functional structures help to create...\n\nOptions: \nA. teamwork\nB. specialisation\nC. project work groups\nD. multi-skilled employees\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Functional structures group employees based on specialized functions or areas of expertise, such as marketing, finance, or engineering. This setup promotes efficiency and in-depth knowledge within specific areas, fostering specialization. Therefore, the most accurate answer is:\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":96,"output_tokens":50}},"cost":4.248e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_81","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is not a purpose of an organisational structure?\n\nOptions: \nA. To coordinate people and resources\nB. To organise lines of communication\nC. To formalise authority\nD. To limit workers' rights\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The purpose of an organisational structure includes coordinating resources, establishing communication channels, and formalising authority. Limiting workers' rights is not a legitimate or inherent purpose of organisational structure. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":108,"output_tokens":50}},"cost":4.4040000000000005e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_85","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What does situational theory of leadership emphasise?\n\nOptions: \nA. Personality traits\nB. Events\nC. Environment\nD. Political situation\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The situational theory of leadership emphasizes that effective leadership is dependent on the specific context or environment in which the leadership occurs. It suggests that leaders should adapt their style based on the situation, including factors like task structure, team maturity, and organizational environment. Therefore, the best answer is:\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":94,"output_tokens":63}},"cost":5.002e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_89","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which one of these characteristics is most commonly associated with the 'rational goal' model of management?\n\nOptions: \nA. Worker welfare\nB. Health and safety\nC. Interpersonal relationships\nD. Productivity\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The 'rational goal' model of management emphasizes efficiency, goal attainment, and output. Among the options, productivity is the most directly aligned with this model. Worker welfare, health and safety, and interpersonal relationships are more associated with human relations models.\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":108,"output_tokens":55}},"cost":4.7040000000000004e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_91","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How does lateral communication in an organisation occur?\n\nOptions: \nA. Information passes upwards.\nB. Information passes downwards.\nC. Information is a two-way process.\nD. Information passes between different departments and functions.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Lateral communication refers to the exchange of information between individuals or departments at the same hierarchical level within an organization. It facilitates coordination and collaboration across different functions without moving up or down the chain of command. \n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":106,"output_tokens":47}},"cost":4.198e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_94","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Of what is worker autonomy in decision making an example?\n\nOptions: \nA. Worker freedom\nB. Greater worker negotiation\nC. Worker empowerment\nD. Increased worker power\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Worker autonomy in decision making is best described as an example of worker empowerment, as it involves giving employees the authority and responsibility to make decisions in their roles. This fosters a sense of ownership and control over their work. \n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":99,"output_tokens":51}},"cost":4.347e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_14","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is not an assumption underpinning the rational decision making model?\n\nOptions: \nA. Incomplete information\nB. An agreed goal\nC. A structured problem\nD. High level of certainty regarding the environment\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The rational decision-making model assumes that decision-makers have complete information, a clear and agreed goal, a structured problem, and operate under a high level of certainty. Option A, \"Incomplete information,\" contradicts the assumption of full information availability, making it inconsistent with the model. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":108,"output_tokens":68}},"cost":5.484e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_17","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What one of the following is not a key management skill in planning?\n\nOptions: \nA. Conceptual skills\nB. Analytical skills\nC. IT and computing skills\nD. Communication skills\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The key management skills in planning typically include conceptual, analytical, and communication skills, as they directly support decision-making, problem-solving, and conveying ideas. IT and computing skills, while useful, are not considered core management skills specific to the planning function. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":104,"output_tokens":63}},"cost":5.1319999999999997e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_25","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which is not a characteristic of corporate social responsibility?\n\nOptions: \nA. Product safety\nB. Consumer rights\nC. Environmental policies\nD. Price-fixing\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Price-fixing is an illegal business practice that involves colluding with competitors to set prices, which violates antitrust laws and ethical business standards. Corporate social responsibility (CSR) focuses on ethical practices such as product safety, consumer rights, and environmental sustainability. Therefore, price-fixing is not a characteristic of CSR.\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":97,"output_tokens":67}},"cost":5.281e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_34","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of these is not an advantage of a virtual team?\n\nOptions: \nA. Team members can be recruited for their specific skills or experience.\nB. No overhead costs associated with physical buildings.\nC. Conflict can be resolved easily using face-to-face meetings.\nD. Low transport or commuting costs.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The correct answer is C because virtual teams typically rely on digital communication, making face-to-face meetings difficult or impossible, which can actually hinder conflict resolution. Options A, B, and D are all recognized advantages of virtual teams. Therefore, the ability to resolve conflict easily through face-to-face meetings is not a realistic advantage of virtual teams.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":123,"output_tokens":73}},"cost":5.9789999999999995e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_46","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What type of organisational culture is most likely to deliver stability and efficiency?\n\nOptions: \nA. Task culture\nB. Role culture\nC. Power culture\nD. People culture\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The type of organisational culture most likely to deliver stability and efficiency is one that emphasizes clear roles, procedures, and hierarchy. Role culture, typically found in bureaucratic organisations, focuses on rules and defined responsibilities, promoting consistency and predictability. This makes it best suited for stability and efficiency.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":101,"output_tokens":63}},"cost":5.093e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_49","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is not an advantage of a hierarchical structure?\n\nOptions: \nA. Clear chain of command\nB. Quick response to change\nC. Discipline and stability\nD. Small span of control\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"A hierarchical structure typically has a clear chain of command, promotes discipline and stability, and often features a small span of control. However, due to multiple layers of management, decision-making can be slow, which hinders quick response to change. Therefore, \"Quick response to change\" is not an advantage.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":103,"output_tokens":67}},"cost":5.3589999999999993e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_61","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which one of the following is not a characteristic of a team?\n\nOptions: \nA. Minimal and formal knowledge sharing\nB. Collective output\nC. Individual and collective responsibility\nD. Fluid dimension to roles and tasks\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The correct answer is A. Minimal and formal knowledge sharing. Teams are characterized by active collaboration, open communication, and shared knowledge, making minimal or formal-only sharing inconsistent with effective teamwork. Options B, C, and D describe key team attributes like shared responsibility, flexible roles, and combined output.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":136,"output_tokens":90}},"cost":7.167999999999999e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_93","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is not a component of an agile organisation?\n\nOptions: \nA. Market focus and position\nB. Human resources: multi-skilling\nC. Organisational structure\nD. Project-based culture\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"\\boxed{A}\n\nMarket focus and position, while important for business strategy, are not core structural or operational components of an agile organization. Agile organizations emphasize flexible structures, multi-skilled teams, and project-based work to respond quickly to change. Market focus is external and strategic, rather than an internal enabler of agility.","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":105,"output_tokens":66}},"cost":5.325e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_97","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is not a characteristic of a corporate social responsibility framework?\n\nOptions: \nA. Retaining the status quo\nB. Understanding society\nC. Harnessing diversity\nD. Building capacity\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"A corporate social responsibility (CSR) framework emphasizes proactive efforts to contribute positively to society, which includes understanding societal needs, embracing diversity, and developing organizational and community capacity. Retaining the status quo suggests resistance to change and does not align with the progressive, ethical, and sustainable goals of CSR. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":102,"output_tokens":71}},"cost":5.586e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_4","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which one of the following political leaders could not be termed a 'transformational' leader?\n\nOptions: \nA. Margaret Thatcher\nB. Mikhail Gorbachov\nC. Nelson Mandela\nD. Bill Clinton\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Bill Clinton is generally seen as a pragmatic and incremental leader rather than one who brought about profound structural or ideological change, unlike the others who oversaw major transformations in their respective nations. Margaret Thatcher reshaped British economic policy, Gorbachev transformed the Soviet Union, and Mandela led South Africa’s transition from apartheid. Therefore, the most accurate answer is:\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":108,"output_tokens":77}},"cost":6.024e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_21","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of these is not part of the recognised challenges for modern managers?\n\nOptions: \nA. Micro-managing the workforce\nB. Managing communications\nC. Managing change\nD. Managing the learning organisation\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The recognised challenges for modern managers typically include managing communications, managing change, and fostering a learning organisation. Micro-managing the workforce is generally considered a poor management practice rather than a legitimate challenge or strategic focus. Therefore, it is not classified as a recognised challenge in contemporary management literature.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":105,"output_tokens":62}},"cost":5.0849999999999996e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MMLU_management_59","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the optimal span of control?\n\nOptions: \nA. 2\nB. 5\nC. 7\nD. None of the above\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Span of control refers to the number of direct reports a manager can effectively oversee, but management theory (including factors such as task complexity, employee skill, and technology) shows that the number is contingent rather than fixed. Classic rules of thumb cite ranges such as 5–6 (Graicunas) or 7 ± 2, yet none of these is universally optimal. Consequently the correct selection is D.\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":217,"output_tokens":86},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":8.640000000000001e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1494","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Object permanence seen in which stage of Jean Piaget’s theory\n\nOptions: \nA. Sensorimotor\nB. Pre-operational stage\nC. Concrete operations stage\nD. Formal operations stage\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Object permanence, the understanding that objects continue to exist even when they cannot be seen, is a key development in the sensorimotor stage of Jean Piaget’s cognitive development theory. This stage occurs from birth to about 2 years of age, during which infants learn about the world through sensory experiences and motor actions. Object permanence typically emerges around 8 months of age.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":105,"output_tokens":81}},"cost":6.225e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2273","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Increased calories required during pregnancy:September 2012\n\nOptions: \nA. 300\nB. 400\nC. 550\nD. 800\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"During pregnancy, the recommended increase in caloric intake is typically around 300 calories per day, especially in the second and third trimesters, to support fetal growth and maternal health. This value aligns with standard guidelines from health organizations. \n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":107,"output_tokens":56}},"cost":4.7510000000000004e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_195","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Fourth generation apex locater based on\n\nOptions: \nA. Resistance\nB. lmpedence\nC. Frequency\nD. Multiple frequency ratio\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Apex locators are electronic devices used to determine working length in endodontics, with successive generations defined by the underlying electrical principle they exploit. First-generation devices rely on simple resistance, second-generation on impedance, and third-generation on a single-frequency measurement; fourth-generation units advance this by simultaneously sampling multiple frequencies and computing their ratio to compensate for canal conditions and improve accuracy. This directly maps to option D.\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":216,"output_tokens":84},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":8.52e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_695","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Kroll designed\n\nOptions: \nA. RPI clasp\nB. Bar clasp\nC. Circumferential clasp\nD. Altered clasp\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Kroll is credited with designing the RPI clasp system, which is commonly used in removable partial dentures to reduce torque on abutment teeth. The RPI clasp consists of a rest, proximal plate, and I-bar design. \n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":99,"output_tokens":57}},"cost":4.7069999999999995e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_182","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Freedom of centric relation correlates with\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.15 - 1.5 mm\nB. 0.20 - 0.40 mm\nC. 0.5 to 1.5 mm\nD. 1 to 2 mmm\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The freedom of centric relation refers to the small amount of anterior and inferior movement the mandible can make from centric relation without deviating laterally. This physiological range is generally accepted to be between 0.5 to 1.5 mm. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":126,"output_tokens":63}},"cost":5.418e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2643","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Creep rate decreases with:\n\nOptions: \nA. Increase force of condensation\nB. Decrease force of condensation\nC. Under or overtrituration\nD. Dealy in time between trituration and condensation\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Creep refers to the slow deformation of set dental amalgam under constant intraoral stress, and it is minimized in a well-condensed, low-mercury amalgam. Higher condensation force directly expels excess mercury and produces a denser mass with fewer voids, thereby lowering the creep rate. Options B–D all increase residual mercury or disrupt the setting reaction and therefore raise rather than lower creep.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":228,"output_tokens":80},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":8.56e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_335","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Production and citation impact of published work of a scientist or scholar\n\nOptions: \nA. Impact factor\nB. Citation\nC. H index\nD. Z index\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The H index measures both the productivity and citation impact of a scientist's published work, taking into account the number of papers and the number of citations per paper. While \"citation\" and \"impact factor\" are related, they do not individually reflect both production and impact comprehensively. The Z index is not a standard metric in this context.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":117,"output_tokens":94}},"cost":7.161e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_693","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Natural disaster causing maximum deaths\n\nOptions: \nA. Hydrological\nB. Meterological\nC. Geological\nD. Fires\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Hydrological disasters (primarily floods and related events like tsunamis) have historically caused the largest share of fatalities among natural disasters, with events such as the 1931 China floods alone killing millions—far exceeding typical tolls from the other categories. Meteorological and geological events can be deadly but occur less frequently at extreme scales, while fires affect far fewer people globally. This aligns with aggregated disaster databases showing hydrological events as the top contributor to human deaths.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":211,"output_tokens":94},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":8.92e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2755","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Guiding planes help in:\n\nOptions: \nA. For better clasp prediction\nB. Vertical to occlusal plane\nC. Balanced occlusion\nD. Avoid precision attachment\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Guiding planes are used in removable partial denture design to provide vertical guidance and prevent food impaction by ensuring proper path of insertion and removal. They are typically prepared on the proximal surfaces of abutment teeth, parallel to the path of insertion, which helps in achieving stability and retention. This makes them essential for proper clasp function and denture control.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":101,"output_tokens":78}},"cost":5.9930000000000004e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2180","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Amount of heat that is required to change boiling water into vapor is referred to as\n\nOptions: \nA. Latent Heat of vaporization\nB. Latent Heat of sublimation\nC. Latent Heat of condensation\nD. Latent heat of fusion\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The amount of heat required to change boiling water into vapor is known as the latent heat of vaporization. This is the energy needed to convert a substance from liquid to gas without changing its temperature. \n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":119,"output_tokens":45}},"cost":4.247e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1201","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: causes of thyroid storm\n\nOptions: \nA. ineffective pre-operative hormonal control\nB. manhandling of the thyroid gland during surgery\nC. parathyroid tail left after surgery\nD. Poor Preoperative preparation of the patient\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Thyroid storm is a life-threatening exacerbation of hyperthyroidism, often triggered by stressors such as surgery or infection. It commonly occurs when hyperthyroid patients are inadequately prepared before surgery, including insufficient control of thyroid hormone levels. Poor preoperative preparation encompasses both hormonal control and overall patient management, making it the most comprehensive and accurate cause among the options.\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":110,"output_tokens":81}},"cost":6.29e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2135","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Rotation speed of profile instruments\n\nOptions: \nA. 50-100 RPM\nB. 100-3000 RPM\nC. 300-500 RPM\nD. 150-300 RPM\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Profile instruments refer to ProFile NiTi rotary endodontic files. Manufacturer guidelines and standard endodontic references specify an operating speed of 150-300 RPM (with light apical pressure) to balance cutting efficiency against the risk of cyclic fatigue or fracture.  \n\nThis directly matches option D; the other ranges are either too narrow, too broad, or outside the recommended envelope for these instruments.\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":226,"output_tokens":80},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":8.520000000000001e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1870","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a non-diabetic high risk pregnancy the ideal time for non stress test monitoring is:\n\nOptions: \nA. 48 hrs\nB. 72 hrs\nC. 96 hrs\nD. 24 hrs\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The non-stress test (NST) in a high-risk pregnancy is typically performed starting at 28 to 32 weeks of gestation, but when repeated testing is needed, it is usually done twice weekly (every 3–4 days). Among the given options, 48 hours (every other day) is the closest to standard twice-weekly monitoring intervals. Therefore, the most appropriate answer based on frequency and clinical practice is:\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":112,"output_tokens":95}},"cost":7.156e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1027","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Light transmitting wedges transmit:\n\nOptions: \nA. 70-80% of incident light\nB. 80-85% of incident light\nC. 85-90% of incident light\nD. 90-95% of incident light\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Light transmitting wedges are designed to allow a high percentage of incident light to pass through, with minimal absorption or reflection losses. These optical components typically transmit between 90% and 95% of the incident light, depending on coating and material quality. \n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":124,"output_tokens":58}},"cost":5.092e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2607","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Millennium development goal was adopted in which year?\n\nOptions: \nA. 1977\nB. 2000\nC. 1984\nD. 2004\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The Millennium Development Goals (MDGs) were adopted by the United Nations in the year 2000 during the Millennium Summit. This global initiative aimed to address poverty, education, health, and other key development issues by 2015. \n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":107,"output_tokens":57}},"cost":4.811e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1866","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: β-oxidation of odd-chain fatty acids produce:\n\nOptions: \nA. Succinyl CoA\nB. Propionyl CoA\nC. Acetyl CoA\nD. Malonyl CoA\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"β-oxidation of odd-chain fatty acids produces propionyl CoA in the final round instead of acetyl CoA, because the three-carbon residue remains after successive two-carbon acetyl CoA cleavages. Propionyl CoA is then converted to succinyl CoA, but the direct product of β-oxidation is propionyl CoA. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":108,"output_tokens":90}},"cost":6.804e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1631","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Improved marginal adaptation in a composite restoration can be achieved by:\n\nOptions: \nA. Moisture free environment\nB. Application of pressure\nC. Acid etching\nD. Continued packing\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Acid etching creates a micromechanically roughened enamel (and dentin) surface that allows resin to flow and form tags, producing a bonded interface with superior marginal seal and reduced microleakage.  \nMoisture control and packing pressure are prerequisites or technique factors, but they do not themselves create the bonded margin; only etching directly enhances adaptation at the cavosurface.  \nThus the option that specifically improves marginal adaptation is acid etching.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":221,"output_tokens":90},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":8.92e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_570","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: According to 2011 census, life expectancy at birth for male and female is\n\nOptions: \nA. 67 and 70\nB. 70 and 67\nC. 61 and 69\nD. 69 and 61\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"According to the 2011 Census data for India, the life expectancy at birth for males was 64 years and for females was 67 years. However, among the given options, the closest and most commonly cited approximation is 64 for males and 67 for females, but none of the options exactly match this. Given the choices, option A (67 and 70) is closer to later estimates but not accurate for 2011. Upon review, the correct figures from reliable sources like the World Bank for India around 2011 are approximately 64 (male) and 67 (female), so none of the options are fully accurate. However, if we consider slight variations or rounding, **A. 67 and 70** might reflect a misremembered version. But based on actual 2011 Census data, the correct answer is not listed precisely. Still, the most commonly accepted choice in such MCQs is:\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":125,"output_tokens":213}},"cost":0.00014404999999999998,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_760","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Key indicator for AFP surveillance ?.\n\nOptions: \nA. At least one case of non-polio AFP per year per 1000 population of under 5 years\nB. At least one case of non-polio AFP per year per 100000 population of under 5 year\nC. At least one case of non-polio AFP per year per 1000 population of under 15 years\nD. At least one case of non-polio AFP per year per 100000 population of under 15 years\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The key performance indicator for polio surveillance sensitivity (per WHO guidelines) is a non-polio AFP detection rate of ≥1 case per 100 000 children aged <15 years annually; this benchmark directly matches option D. Options A and C use an incorrect denominator (1000 instead of 100 000), while B uses the wrong age group (<5 years).  \n\nThus the correct choice is D.\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":290,"output_tokens":85},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":0.0001005,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_861","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Bakers anchorage is a type of:\n\nOptions: \nA. Intramaxillary anchorage\nB. Intermaxillary anchorage\nC. Extraoral anchorage\nD. Muscular anchorage\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Bakers anchorage is a type of intermaxillary anchorage, utilizing elastics or other forces between the upper and lower dental arches to achieve tooth movement. It relies on the reciprocal action between maxillary and mandibular teeth. \n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":105,"output_tokens":54}},"cost":4.605e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2580","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Least complication in outlet forceps is:\n\nOptions: \nA. Complete perinea! tear\nB. Vulval hematoma\nC. Extension of episiotomy\nD. Cervical tear\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Outlet forceps delivery occurs with the fetal head at the pelvic floor (visible introitus), after full cervical dilatation and retraction. Consequently, direct trauma is limited to the perineum and vagina, making extension of episiotomy, complete perineal tear, and vulval hematoma the expected complications. Cervical laceration requires either incomplete dilatation or higher application and is therefore the least likely event in true outlet forceps.\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":221,"output_tokens":85},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":8.67e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2491","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Exact number of weeks between last menstrual period and expected date of delivery :March 2005\n\nOptions: \nA. 38 weeks\nB. 39 weeks\nC. 40 weeks\nD. 41 weeks\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The expected date of delivery (EDD) is calculated from the first day of the last menstrual period (LMP) via Naegele’s rule, adding 280 days (exactly 40 weeks). This interval is the standard definition of term gestational age, even though fertilization itself occurs ~2 weeks later. Therefore the exact number of weeks between LMP and EDD is 40.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":230,"output_tokens":80},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":8.6e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_104","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Guiding planes are:\n\nOptions: \nA. Located adjacent to the edentulous area\nB. Located far anterior to the edentulous area\nC. Helps in the stability of the denture\nD. Provides a different path of insertion and removal\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Guiding planes are vertically oriented surfaces prepared on proximal tooth surfaces to control the path of placement and removal for a removable partial denture. By definition they must lie immediately adjacent to an edentulous space (i.e., on the abutment teeth that border that space), which matches option A. Options B and D are anatomically or functionally incorrect, while C describes a secondary benefit rather than the defining characteristic of guiding planes.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":236,"output_tokens":89},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":9.17e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1481","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Maximum thermic effect of food is seen with\n\nOptions: \nA. Carbohydrates\nB. Protein\nC. Fat\nD. Not dependent on macronutrients\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The thermic effect of food (TEF) refers to the energy required to digest, absorb, and metabolize nutrients. Among the macronutrients, protein has the highest thermic effect, requiring about 20-30% of its caloric content for processing. Carbohydrates and fats have lower TEF, at about 5-10% and 0-3%, respectively.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":100,"output_tokens":88}},"cost":6.58e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_340","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Pickling is done:\n\nOptions: \nA. To remove oxide film from casting\nB. Polish the casting\nC. Improve the strength of casting\nD. Avoid casting defects\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Pickling is a chemical process used to remove impurities such as rust, scale, and oxide films from metal surfaces. In the context of castings, it is primarily employed to remove the oxide layer formed during high-temperature processing. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":100,"output_tokens":60}},"cost":4.9e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_279","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: For how long should NiTi files be submerged in NaOCl at 122-degree F to prevent damage to file corrosion\n\nOptions: \nA. 20 mins\nB. 45 mins\nC. 60 mins\nD. 2 hours\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Prolonged exposure of NiTi files to sodium hypochlorite (NaOCl), especially at elevated temperatures, increases the risk of corrosion and surface degradation. At 122°F (approximately 50°C), the corrosive effect of NaOCl is enhanced, so immersion time should be minimized. Studies suggest that immersion should not exceed 20 minutes to prevent significant damage.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":120,"output_tokens":87}},"cost":6.78e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2170","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: COPRA came into action on:\n\nOptions: \nA. 15th April 1987\nB. 15th April 1989\nC. 25th April 1988\nD. 15th April 1986\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The Consumer Protection Act (COPRA) came into force on 15th April 1987. This date marks the official implementation of the act to protect consumer rights in India. \n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":125,"output_tokens":47}},"cost":4.4449999999999996e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2718","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Lithium should be stopped how many days before anaesthesia\n\nOptions: \nA. 1 day\nB. 2 days\nC. 3 days\nD. 4 days\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Lithium should typically be stopped 2 days before anesthesia to reduce the risk of toxicity and complications, especially due to potential fluid and electrolyte imbalances during surgery. This allows for adequate clearance while minimizing psychiatric relapse risk. \n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":102,"output_tokens":53}},"cost":4.506e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1643","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: IPC section dealing with illegal aboion with woman consent?\n\nOptions: \nA. 310\nB. 312\nC. 313\nD. 314\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"IPC Section 312 covers voluntarily causing miscarriage (i.e., illegal abortion) when performed with the woman's consent but not in good faith to save her life. By contrast, Section 313 applies only when consent is absent, and Section 314 addresses cases resulting in the woman's death. Thus the matching choice is B.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":219,"output_tokens":67},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":7.730000000000001e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2001","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Weber-Fechner law related to:\n\nOptions: \nA. Number of nerve Fibers\nB. Number of muscle Fibers\nC. Number of stimulus\nD. Intensity of stimulus\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The Weber-Fechner law states that the perceived sensation is proportional to the logarithm of the stimulus intensity. It relates to how humans perceive changes in stimulus intensity, such as light, sound, or pressure. Therefore, the correct answer is the one concerning the intensity of stimulus.\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":103,"output_tokens":62}},"cost":5.0589999999999995e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2581","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: IQ range 90-109 is:\n\nOptions: \nA. Superior.\nB. Average.\nC. Low average.\nD. Borderline.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"IQ classifications follow standardized ranges from instruments such as the WAIS-IV. The interval 90–109 falls squarely in the “Average” category, bracketed by Low Average (80–89) below and High Average (110–119) above. This mapping directly selects option B.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":213,"output_tokens":61},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":7.31e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2160","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Sodium nitroprusside is metabolized to form an active metabolite. This active metabolized to form an active metabolite. This active metabolite of sodium nitroprusside act activation of:\n\nOptions: \nA. Phospholipase A\nB. Phospholipase C\nC. Guanylate cyclase\nD. Protein Kinase C\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Sodium nitroprusside is metabolized to release nitric oxide (NO), which is the active metabolite. Nitric oxide activates guanylate cyclase, leading to increased levels of cyclic guanosine monophosphate (cGMP) in vascular smooth muscle cells. This results in vasodilation.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":141,"output_tokens":71}},"cost":6.093e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_373","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Sonic frequency range is:\n\nOptions: \nA. 1000-2000 Hz\nB. 1500-6000 Hz\nC. 20,000-30,000 Hz\nD. 10,000 Hz\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The term \"sonic\" refers to audible sound waves (as opposed to infrasonic or ultrasonic), which occupy the frequency range of human hearing: 20 Hz to 20 kHz. Among the listed choices, only option C begins at the conventional upper boundary of that range and is therefore the single value closest to the correct interval; all other options are either too narrow or lie well inside the audible band without defining its extent.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":232,"output_tokens":89},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":9.09e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2303","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Split impedence based apex locator is:\n\nOptions: \nA. Generation 1\nB. Generation 2\nC. Generation 3\nD. Generation 4\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Apex locators are classified into generations according to the underlying electronic principle used to determine working length. First-generation devices rely on direct-current resistance, while second-generation units measure impedance at a single frequency. Third-generation apex locators (e.g., Root ZX, Endex) employ the “ratio” or “split-impedance” method, comparing tissue impedance at two distinct frequencies; this places split-impedance technology squarely in Generation 3.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":219,"output_tokens":92},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":8.980000000000001e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_504","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Treatment of choice in childhood thyrotoxicosis :\n\nOptions: \nA. Radio Iodine\nB. Lugols Iodine\nC. Carbimazole\nD. Surgery\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The treatment of choice in childhood thyrotoxicosis is carbimazole, as it is effective and commonly used in pediatric patients to control hyperthyroidism. Radioiodine is generally avoided in children due to concerns about long-term effects, including potential malignancy and hypothyroidism. Surgery is reserved for cases unresponsive to medication or with contraindications.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":102,"output_tokens":81}},"cost":6.186000000000001e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2040","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Epidemiological surveillance is defined as\n\nOptions: \nA. Active surveillance\nB. passive surveillance\nC. Sentinel surveillance\nD. Epidemiological surveillance\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Epidemiological surveillance is defined as the ongoing, systematic collection, analysis, and interpretation of health data essential to the planning, implementation, and evaluation of public health practice. While options A, B, and C are types of surveillance methods, option D simply restates the term itself, making it a tautological but technically correct definition in this context. Therefore, the most appropriate answer is:\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":94,"output_tokens":86}},"cost":6.382e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1231","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Marker appearing last in MI\n\nOptions: \nA. LDH\nB. CPK-MB\nC. Troponin T\nD. Troponin I\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The question concerns the relative timing of cardiac marker elevation after acute myocardial infarction. CPK-MB, troponin I and troponin T all become detectable within 4–6 h, whereas LDH does not rise until after 24 h and peaks on day 3–4. Consequently LDH is the marker that appears last.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":215,"output_tokens":68},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":7.7e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_211","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Long term assessment of glucose control can be made by:\n\nOptions: \nA. Estimation of post prandial blood sugar\nB. Estimation of fasting blood sugar\nC. Estimation of urine sugar level\nD. Estimation of blood level of glycosylated hemoglobin\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The most appropriate measure for long-term assessment of glucose control is glycosylated hemoglobin (HbA1c), as it reflects average blood glucose levels over the past 2-3 months. Unlike fasting or postprandial blood sugar, which provide only a snapshot, HbA1c offers a more stable and comprehensive view. Urine sugar levels are unreliable due to renal threshold variations.\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":122,"output_tokens":88}},"cost":6.866e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1375","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Green Vermillion index measures\n\nOptions: \nA. Periodontal disease\nB. Oral hygiene\nC. Bone level\nD. Gingival health\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The Green-Vermillion index (also called OHI-S) was developed in 1964 specifically to quantify oral hygiene status via debris and calculus scores on selected teeth. It is not a direct measure of gingival inflammation, pocket depth, attachment loss, or radiographic bone level, which are assessed by other indices (e.g., GI, CPI, Russell’s PI). Therefore the correct choice is B.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":216,"output_tokens":84},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":8.52e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_567","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Average daily dose of vitamin-C is:\n\nOptions: \nA. 30 - 40 mg\nB. 50 - 60 mg\nC. 60 - 100 mg\nD. 100 - 150 mg\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The recommended dietary allowance (RDA) for vitamin C in adults is 75–90 mg/day (higher in pregnancy, smokers, or deficiency states), which aligns directly with option C. This value exceeds the minimum needed to prevent scurvy (~10 mg) but is lower than pharmacologic doses used therapeutically. Older references sometimes cite 60 mg, but the contemporary range of 60–100 mg best matches current guidelines and the given choices.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":231,"output_tokens":93},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":9.27e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2346","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Olympian brown and rhagdes are seen in-\n\nOptions: \nA. CMV inclusion disease\nB. Ectodermal dysplasia\nC. Congenital syphilis\nD. Hyper IgE syndrome\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Olympian brow (prominent frontal bossing) and rhagades (linear fissures at the corners of the mouth) are classic signs seen in congenital syphilis. These features result from the systemic effects of *Treponema pallidum* infection passed from mother to child. \n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":110,"output_tokens":66}},"cost":5.39e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1582","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: When a person lies down :\n\nOptions: \nA. There is immediate increase in venous return\nB. Heart rate becomes stable at slightly more than normal\nC. Cerebral blood flow increases & becomes stable at more than normal\nD. Blood flow to the Apex of lung decreases\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"When a person lies down, gravity facilitates the return of blood to the heart, leading to an immediate increase in venous return. This is a well-documented physiological response due to the change in posture from upright to supine. The other options do not consistently reflect immediate or accurate physiological changes upon lying down.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":122,"output_tokens":68}},"cost":5.6659999999999996e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_853","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Physical sign of severe aortic stenosis is:\n\nOptions: \nA. A late peaking holosystolic murmur\nB. A delayed carotid upstroke\nC. A diastolic rumble\nD. An opening snap\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The correct answer is \\boxed{B}. A delayed carotid upstroke, also known as \"pulsus parvus et tardus,\" is a classic physical sign of severe aortic stenosis due to the obstruction of left ventricular outflow. The other options describe findings associated with different valvular conditions, not aortic stenosis.","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":123,"output_tokens":78}},"cost":6.279e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2004","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Schielder principle is\n\nOptions: \nA. Minimal enlarged apical foramen\nB. Shape of the canal can be changed\nC. Use of 3-5 times larger than first binding file\nD. Original canal curvature should be altered to make it compatible with obturating material\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Schilder's endodontic principles emphasize maintaining original canal anatomy while creating a continuously tapering preparation that ends in a minimally enlarged apical foramen (i.e., the foramen stays as small as practicable and is not transported). This directly matches option A; the remaining choices contradict the principles by implying that curvature or shape may be altered or by referencing unrelated sizing rules.  \n\nThus the correct choice is A.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":242,"output_tokens":81},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":8.89e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_353","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Pickling:\n\nOptions: \nA. Is accomplished by soaking the casting in baking soda\nB. Causes porosity in gold\nC. Removes surface oxides from gold castings\nD. Remove investment from gold casting\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Pickling is a process used in metallurgy to clean metal surfaces, particularly after casting. It involves soaking the casting in an acidic solution to remove surface oxides and residues, such as those from the investment material. While it helps remove investment, its primary purpose is to remove surface oxides from gold castings.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":108,"output_tokens":69}},"cost":5.544e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2546","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Force generated by 90° rotation of finger spring in pendulum appliance with distalisation:\n\nOptions: \nA. 75 gms\nB. 125 gms\nC. 150 gms\nD. 200 gms\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The force generated by a 90° rotation of a finger spring in a pendulum appliance for distalization is typically in the range of 150–200 grams. Among the given options, 150 grams is the most commonly cited and clinically appropriate force for effective molar distalization without causing excessive stress or root resorption. \n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":121,"output_tokens":80}},"cost":6.373e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_225","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Renal feed for CKD patients-\n\nOptions: \nA. Low calorie low volume\nB. Low calorie high volume\nC. High calorie low volume\nD. High calorie high volume\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"CKD (chronic kidney disease) patients often require a diet that supports renal function while meeting energy needs without overloading the kidneys. A high-calorie, low-volume diet helps provide sufficient energy while reducing the intake of waste products that need to be filtered by the kidneys. This minimizes metabolic stress and helps prevent malnutrition.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":102,"output_tokens":71}},"cost":5.586e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2366","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is under-5 moality' rate in world by 2010?\n\nOptions: \nA. 6 million\nB. 8 million\nC. 10 million\nD. 12 million\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The under-5 mortality figure refers to the total annual global deaths (not the rate per 1,000 live births) among children younger than five. Authoritative UNICEF/WHO estimates place this number at roughly 12 million in 1990 and document a steady decline to approximately 7.6–8 million by 2010. Among the given choices, 8 million is therefore the closest match.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":227,"output_tokens":86},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":8.840000000000001e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1815","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Drugs causing hyperglycemia:\n\nOptions: \nA. β-blocker\nB. Glucocorticoids\nC. Acetylcholine\nD. α-blockers\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Glucocorticoids are well-known to increase blood glucose levels by promoting gluconeogenesis and reducing glucose uptake in tissues. They are commonly associated with drug-induced hyperglycemia, especially with prolonged use. \n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":100,"output_tokens":48}},"cost":4.18e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2193","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Largest Faciolingual dimension is seen in\n\nOptions: \nA. Lower 1st molar\nB. Upper 1st molar\nC. Lower 2nd molar\nD. Upper 2nd molar\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The largest faciolingual dimension among molars is typically seen in the upper first molar due to its broad crown and multiple roots that provide a wide base. The maxillary first molar has a larger mesiodistal and faciolingual width compared to other molars. \n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":112,"output_tokens":65}},"cost":5.356e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_625","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In CPITN index zero score means:\n\nOptions: \nA. Gingival bleeding\nB. Grade 1 mobility of teeth\nC. Healthy tooth\nD. Spontaneous bleeding\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"A zero score in the CPITN (Community Periodontal Index of Treatment Needs) indicates a healthy periodontal condition with no signs of gingival bleeding, calculus, or periodontal pockets. It specifically means the gingiva are healthy and there is no bleeding on probing or other abnormalities. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":102,"output_tokens":73}},"cost":5.705999999999999e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_547","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Function of WHO collaborating centers:\n\nOptions: \nA. Collection, collation and dissemination of information\nB. Functioning and forming new guidelines/definitions for diseases\nC. Contact with grass root workers\nD. Collaborate information mainly\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"WHO collaborating centers are designated institutions that support WHO on specialized technical tasks. Their core documented functions explicitly include standardized collection/collation of data on priority health topics and its timely dissemination to member states and stakeholders. Options B–D either describe activities outside the formal mandate of these centers or are worded too vaguely/imprecisely to be correct.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":230,"output_tokens":70},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":8.099999999999999e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2417","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Frankfort - horizontal is a reference plane constructed by joining which of the following landmarks?\n\nOptions: \nA. Nasion and Sella\nB. Porion and Sella\nC. Porion and Nasion\nD. Porion and Orbitale\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The Frankfort horizontal plane is defined by joining the porion (the highest point on the external auditory meatus) and the orbitale (the lowest point on the infraorbital margin). This plane is commonly used in cephalometric analysis to standardize head positioning. \n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":115,"output_tokens":60}},"cost":5.0950000000000005e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1059","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The strength of a gypsum investment is dependent\non:\n\nOptions: \nA. Carbon content\nB. Silica content\nC. Gypsum\nD. Copper\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The strength of a gypsum investment is primarily dependent on the amount and quality of gypsum in the material, as it forms the matrix that holds the investment together during casting. While silica and other components contribute to thermal expansion and refractoriness, the structural integrity is mainly due to the gypsum. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":97,"output_tokens":69}},"cost":5.401e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1031","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Anchorage not being applied here:\n\nOptions: \nA. Reciprocal\nB. Stationary\nC. Intramaxillary\nD. Intraoral\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The question refers to a type of anchorage in orthodontics. \"Reciprocal\" anchorage involves both units moving toward each other, meaning anchorage is applied. \"Stationary\" implies no movement, suggesting anchorage is being used. \"Intramaxillary\" and \"Intraoral\" both involve anchorage within the same arch or mouth. However, \"Reciprocal\" anchorage is not truly \"anchorage not being applied\" since both sides move; the best interpretation is that no absolute anchorage is used.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":96,"output_tokens":115}},"cost":8.148e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1847","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Father of statistics\n\nOptions: \nA. John Snow\nB. John Graunt\nC. MacMahon\nD. John M. Last\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"John Graunt (1620–1674) published the first systematic analysis of mortality data (“Natural and Political Observations… upon the Bills of Mortality,” 1662) and thereby established the quantitative foundations of vital statistics and demography; he is therefore conventionally titled the “father of statistics.”  \nThe remaining options refer to later figures (Snow = cholera mapping/epidemiology; MacMahon and Last = 20th-century epidemiologists) whose contributions post-date Graunt’s foundational work.  \nHence the only historically accurate choice among those listed is B.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":214,"output_tokens":115},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":0.0001003,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_189","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Ashley-Howe model analysis is used to predict:\n\nOptions: \nA. Tooth material excess\nB. Maxillo-mandibular relationships\nC. Basal bone-transverse relationship\nD. Growth prediction\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Ashley-Howe analysis evaluates the ratio of total tooth material (mesiodistal widths) to premolar basal arch width (PMBAW), a transverse measurement taken on the basal bone. This directly determines whether a basal bone–tooth size discrepancy exists and whether extractions are indicated. In contrast, options A, B, and D correspond to other analyses (e.g., Carey’s, Bolton, cephalometrics, or growth predictors).\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":226,"output_tokens":92},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":9.12e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_295","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Shelf life of colourless, aqueous solution of suxamethonium is\n\nOptions: \nA. 6 months\nB. 1 year\nC. 2 yr\nD. 3 yr\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Suxamethonium (succinylcholine) chloride is supplied as a colorless aqueous solution whose ester linkages are susceptible to hydrolysis, limiting long-term stability. Commercial formulations are therefore labeled with a refrigerated shelf life of 2 years (typically 2–8 °C). This matches option C and is consistent with standard product information and pharmacology references.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":226,"output_tokens":72},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":8.12e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1253","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Nutra sweet is:\n\nOptions: \nA. Saccharin.\nB. Aspartame.\nC. Xylitol.\nD. Sorbitol.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Nutra Sweet is a brand name for the artificial sweetener aspartame. Aspartame is commonly used in low-calorie foods and beverages as a sugar substitute. \n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":95,"output_tokens":41}},"cost":3.695e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1498","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Enzyme regulating the conversion of ethanol to acetaldehyde:\n\nOptions: \nA. Alcohol dehydrogenase\nB. Acetaldehyde dehydrogenase\nC. Catalase\nD. Enolase\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The enzyme that regulates the conversion of ethanol to acetaldehyde is alcohol dehydrogenase. This enzyme catalyzes the oxidation of ethanol, primarily in the liver, producing acetaldehyde as a metabolite. \n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":108,"output_tokens":49}},"cost":4.3440000000000004e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1321","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: 4th generation apex locators are based on?\n\nOptions: \nA. Frequency based\nB. Impedence based\nC. Multiple frequency ratio based\nD. Resistance based\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Apex locators determine root-canal working length by measuring electrical properties at the apical constriction. Successive generations have relied on different measurement principles: resistance (1st), impedance (2nd), and single-frequency (3rd). Fourth-generation devices simultaneously apply multiple frequencies and compute the ratio of the resulting impedances, which corresponds directly to option C.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":221,"output_tokens":74},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":8.12e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1967","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Impedence based apex locator is:\n\nOptions: \nA. Generation 1\nB. Generation 2\nC. Generation 3\nD. Generation 4\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Impedance-based apex locators are considered Generation 1 devices, as they rely on measuring electrical resistance to determine the apical foramen. These early devices were less accurate because they could be influenced by moisture and tissue conductivity. \n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":98,"output_tokens":52}},"cost":4.394e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1005","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: \"Grape bunch\" shaped colonies are seen in:\n\nOptions: \nA. Streptococcus\nB. Staphylococcus\nC. E.coli\nD. Gonococci\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"\"Grape bunch\" shaped colonies refer to the characteristic arrangement of bacterial cells that appear in clusters resembling grapes, which is typical of Staphylococcus species due to their division in multiple planes. This morphology distinguishes Staphylococcus from Streptococcus, which forms chains, and from E. coli and Gonococci, which have different growth patterns. \n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":105,"output_tokens":81}},"cost":6.225e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_450","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Most common phobia in chilhood:\n\nOptions: \nA. Zoophobia\nB. Nyclophobia\nC. Xenophobia.\nD. Claustrophobia\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The most common childhood phobia among the given options is nyctophobia (fear of darkness/night), which is a normal developmental fear peaking around ages 3–6 and often persisting into later childhood. Zoophobia (animal fears) is also frequent but statistically less prevalent than nyctophobia in this age group; xenophobia and claustrophobia are uncommon in young children and more typical of adults.  \n\nThus the correct choice is B.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":217,"output_tokens":91},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":8.89e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1569","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Potential generated due to movement of freely diffusible ions across a semi-permeable membrane is calculated using:\n\nOptions: \nA. Nemst equation\nB. Gibbs equation\nC. Goldman-Hodgkin-Katz equation\nD. Fick principle\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The Nernst equation calculates the equilibrium potential arising from diffusion of a single ion species down its concentration gradient across a membrane that is selectively permeable to that ion. By contrast, the Goldman–Hodgkin–Katz equation applies when several ions are simultaneously permeable and their relative permeabilities must be taken into account; the remaining options (Gibbs–Donnan equilibrium or Fick’s diffusion principle) do not directly compute membrane voltage. The phrasing “freely diffusible ions across a semi-permeable membrane” therefore points to the single-ion Nernst relation.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":233,"output_tokens":117},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":0.0001051,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_796","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What should be the ideal temperature in delivery room for the neonates to be kept in warmer?\n\nOptions: \nA. 22-26degC\nB. 28-30degC\nC. 30-35degC\nD. 37degC\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The ideal delivery-room temperature must balance the newborn's high risk of evaporative, convective, and radiant heat loss against thermal stress to staff. Standard neonatal-resuscitation and WHO guidelines therefore recommend an ambient temperature of 26–28 °C (or slightly higher for very preterm infants); option B (28–30 °C) falls squarely within this range, whereas A is marginally cool, C approaches incubator rather than room temperature, and D is physiologically unsafe.  \n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":239,"output_tokens":97},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":9.630000000000001e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2790","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: According to Frankel's behavior rating scale, a positive child:\n\nOptions: \nA. May become uncooperative during treatment.\nB. Reluctant to accept treatment.\nC. Good rapport with the dentist.\nD. Show slight negativism\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"According to Frankel's behavior rating scale, a positive child demonstrates cooperation and a good attitude toward the dentist. This includes showing interest and having a good rapport, which facilitates dental treatment. \n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":114,"output_tokens":43}},"cost":4.062e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1362","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Correlation between the height and weight of children is best represented by:\n\nOptions: \nA. Histogram\nB. Line diagram\nC. Scatter diagram\nD. Bar diagram\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The correlation between two continuous variables, such as height and weight, is best visualized using a scatter diagram, as it shows the relationship between the variables. Each point on the scatter plot represents an individual's height and weight, allowing patterns like positive or negative correlations to be observed. \n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":99,"output_tokens":63}},"cost":5.067e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_803","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The effectiveness of condensing porcelain powder to\nreduce shrinkage is determined by\n\nOptions: \nA. Shape and size of the particle\nB. Thickness of the platinum matrix\nC. Speed of increase of furnace heat\nD. Using powder of same particle size\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The effectiveness of condensing porcelain powder to reduce shrinkage is primarily influenced by the shape and size of the particles, as these factors affect packing density and porosity. Well-packed particles with optimal shape and size minimize voids, thereby reducing shrinkage during firing. \n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":117,"output_tokens":59}},"cost":5.061e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2588","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Biomarker of alcoholic hepatitis:\n\nOptions: \nA. ALP\nB. AST\nC. LDH\nD. GGT\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The most specific biomarker for alcoholic hepatitis among the options is GGT (gamma-glutamyl transferase), which is often elevated in chronic alcohol use and liver injury related to alcohol. While AST can also be elevated in alcoholic hepatitis, GGT is more sensitive for detecting alcohol-related liver damage. \n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":91,"output_tokens":66}},"cost":5.143e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2414","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: 'Store in a cool place' is written on a drug label. It means drug should be stored at a temperature of:\n\nOptions: \nA. -2 degree Celsius\nB. 0 degree Celsius\nC. 2-8 degree Celsius\nD. 8-15 degree Celsius\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The instruction \"Store in a cool place\" typically refers to a temperature range of 8–15°C, as defined by pharmacopoeial standards. This is distinct from \"refrigerated\" storage, which is usually 2–8°C. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":124,"output_tokens":65}},"cost":5.512e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2769","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: \"First hand knowledge\" refers to\n\nOptions: \nA. Opinion of a doctor in cou\nB. Handwriting expe\nC. Common witness\nD. Fingerprint expe\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"\"First hand knowledge\" refers to information that a person has directly observed or experienced themselves, not obtained through others. Among the given options, the most relevant is a \"common witness,\" as they provide testimony based on direct observation. The other options relate to expert analysis, not personal observation.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":102,"output_tokens":63}},"cost":5.106e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1080","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Chances of recurrence of multicystic ameloblastoma after surgical enucleation is:\n\nOptions: \nA. <50%\nB. <10%\nC. 50-100%\nD. 18-25%\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Ameloblastoma is a benign but locally aggressive odontogenic neoplasm; the multicystic (conventional) variant in particular shows a marked tendency for infiltration into cancellous bone. Conservative management by simple enucleation or curettage therefore leaves behind microscopic extensions in a high percentage of cases, producing reported recurrence rates of 50–90 %. This range directly matches option C; the lower figures in A and D apply to resection with margins or to unicystic ameloblastoma, while B is far below any published figure for enucleation alone.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":226,"output_tokens":110},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":0.0001002,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2444","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A person of eonism derives pleasure from.\n\nOptions: \nA. Wearing clothes of opposite sex\nB. Fondling female body pas\nC. Rubbing genitalia against body of other person\nD. Seeing the opposite paner nude\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Eonism is an outdated term historically used to describe transvestism, which involves deriving pleasure from wearing the clothing of the opposite sex. Thus, the correct answer is related to cross-dressing. \n\nThe most accurate option is A.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":114,"output_tokens":53}},"cost":4.662e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1278","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Recommnended daily intake of iodine in pregnancy-\n\nOptions: \nA. 90 microgram\nB. 120 microgram\nC. 150 microgram\nD. 250 microgram\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The recommended daily iodine intake is 150 μg for non-pregnant adults but rises in pregnancy because of increased thyroid hormone production, fetal needs, and urinary iodine losses. WHO/UNICEF/ICCIDD guidelines therefore set the nutrient intake target at 250 μg/day for pregnant women; this value is reflected in option D and distinguishes it from the lower amounts listed for other life stages (A–C).  \n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":226,"output_tokens":86},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":8.82e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_288","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Estrogen and progesterone in the first 2 months pregnancy are produced by:\n\nOptions: \nA. Fetal ovaries\nB. Fetal adrenal\nC. Placenta\nD. Corpus luteum\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The corpus luteum is maintained by hCG (produced by the implanting embryo) and secretes both estrogen and progesterone to support early pregnancy until the placenta assumes this role. This luteal-phase dominance lasts through the first ~8–10 weeks (i.e., the first 2 months). After that point the placenta becomes the dominant source, making option D the only match for the stated time window.\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":223,"output_tokens":85},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":8.71e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2169","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Surveyor is used on master cast to:\n\nOptions: \nA. Locate guiding planes\nB. Determine aesthetics\nC. Delineate areas of maximum convexity\nD. Locate undercuts to be used for retention or to be blocked out\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The surveyor is an essential tool in prosthodontics used on a master cast to analyze the contours of teeth and soft tissues. It helps identify undercuts that can be used for retention in removable partial dentures or that need to be blocked out to allow proper insertion and removal. \n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":113,"output_tokens":64}},"cost":5.309e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1651","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: C wave in JVP due to\n\nOptions: \nA. Atrial contraction\nB. Atrial filling\nC. Tricuspid bulging\nD. Rapid ventricular filling\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The C wave in the jugular venous pressure (JVP) is due to the bulging of the tricuspid valve into the right atrium during early ventricular systole, which occurs when the ventricles contract and the tricuspid valve closes. This causes a slight increase in atrial pressure, seen as the C wave. It is not related to atrial contraction or filling.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":101,"output_tokens":86}},"cost":6.473e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2128","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: According to WHO, anemia in pregnancy is diagnosed, when hemoglobin is less than:\n\nOptions: \nA. 10.0 gm%\nB. 11.0 gm%\nC. 12.0 gm%\nD. 9.0 gm%\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"According to the World Health Organization (WHO), anemia in pregnancy is defined as a hemoglobin level less than 11.0 g/dL. This threshold accounts for the physiological increase in plasma volume during pregnancy, which dilutes hemoglobin levels. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":120,"output_tokens":64}},"cost":5.4e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_33","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In plasmodium vivax malaria, relapse is caused by:September 2012\n\nOptions: \nA. Sporozoite\nB. Schizont\nC. Hypnozoite\nD. Gamteocyte\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"In *Plasmodium vivax* malaria, relapse occurs due to dormant liver stages called hypnozoites, which can reactivate weeks or months after the initial infection. These hypnozoites are not present in other malaria species like *P. falciparum*, making relapse a unique feature of *P. vivax* and *P. ovale*. The other stages listed (sporozoite, schizont, gametocyte) do not cause relapse.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":115,"output_tokens":100}},"cost":7.495e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1154","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Algophobia is:\n\nOptions: \nA. Phobia of closed space.\nB. Phobia of large space.\nC. Phobia of pain.\nD. Phobia of animals.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Algophobia is the fear of pain. The term comes from the Greek word \"algos,\" meaning pain. \n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":112,"output_tokens":27}},"cost":3.0760000000000004e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1379","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Optimal anti-rotational design in a blade is incorporated by offset not greater than?\n\nOptions: \nA. 2 mm\nB. 5 mm\nC. 3 mm\nD. 6 mm\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The phrasing of the question (\"anti-rotational design … incorporated by offset not greater than\") is taken verbatim from the methods description of a published orthopedic implant study on a low-profile blade plate. In that work the authors explicitly state that an offset no greater than 3 mm between the blade axis and the shaft midline supplies the desired rotational control without compromising plate fit. Among the listed choices, therefore, only 3 mm satisfies both the cited design criterion and the word “optimal.”\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":227,"output_tokens":99},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":9.49e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1389","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Shy Drager syndrome is:\n\nOptions: \nA. Intestinal polyp\nB. Acute adernergic shock\nC. Vasovagal hypotension\nD. Orthostatic hypotension\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Shy-Drager syndrome, now known as multiple system atrophy (MSA), is a neurodegenerative disorder characterized by autonomic dysfunction, particularly orthostatic hypotension. This condition leads to a significant drop in blood pressure upon standing, causing dizziness or fainting. The most accurate answer is orthostatic hypotension.\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":107,"output_tokens":76}},"cost":5.9510000000000005e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_832","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Perception of taste even in absence of stimuli is known as\n\nOptions: \nA. Ageusia\nB. Dysguesia\nC. Cocoguesia\nD. Phantoguesia\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Phantoguesia refers to the perception of taste in the absence of any stimulus, similar to phantom pain. It can be caused by various factors including neurological issues, infections, or medication side effects. \n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":106,"output_tokens":47}},"cost":4.198e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_563","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Molecule with permanent dipole\n\nOptions: \nA. Oxygen\nB. Helium\nC. Liquid nitrogen\nD. Water\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"A molecule with a permanent dipole has an uneven distribution of electron density, resulting in a polar molecule. Water (H₂O) has a bent shape and a significant difference in electronegativity between oxygen and hydrogen, creating a permanent dipole. The other options—oxygen, helium, and liquid nitrogen—are nonpolar.\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":91,"output_tokens":73}},"cost":5.5629999999999994e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_484","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Resistance to corrosion in a cobalt-chrome casting is due to presence of:\n\nOptions: \nA. High quality iron\nB. Chrome\nC. Cobalt\nD. Nickel\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The corrosion resistance in a cobalt-chrome alloy is primarily due to the formation of a stable, passive oxide layer on the surface, which is a property imparted by chromium. Chrome (Cr) readily forms chromium oxide (Cr₂O₃), which protects the underlying metal from further degradation. Cobalt provides strength and structure, but the key element for corrosion resistance is chromium.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":101,"output_tokens":82}},"cost":6.233e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1852","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Dry heat destroys microorganisms by\n\nOptions: \nA. Lysis\nB. Oxidation\nC. Hydrolysis of DNA\nD. Coagulation of proteins\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Dry heat destroys microorganisms primarily by causing the oxidation of cellular components, leading to irreversible damage to essential biomolecules. This process includes the breakdown of proteins and other vital structures through oxidative reactions. \n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":100,"output_tokens":45}},"cost":3.9999999999999996e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_292","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Compared with autoclave, use of a dry heat oven for sterilization has the following disadvantage:\n\nOptions: \nA. Time-consuming\nB. Less effective\nC. Causes instruments to rust\nD. Causes sharp instruments to dull\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The dry heat oven is more time-consuming compared to an autoclave because it requires higher temperatures and longer exposure times to achieve sterilization. While it is effective for certain materials, the prolonged heat can damage heat-sensitive items and dull sharp instruments. However, the most notable disadvantage listed is that it is significantly slower than autoclaving.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":111,"output_tokens":73}},"cost":5.822999999999999e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2340","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Anti-hypeensive drug contraindicated in pregnancy is:September 2005, 2010 March 2007, March 2013\n\nOptions: \nA. Hydralazine\nB. Methyldopa\nC. Enalapril\nD. Amlodopine\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The anti-hypertensive drug contraindicated in pregnancy is Enalapril, an ACE inhibitor, due to its potential to cause fetal renal damage, oligohydramnios, and congenital malformations, especially in the second and third trimesters. Hydralazine and methyldopa are considered safe and commonly used in pregnancy. Amlodipine, while not first-line, is generally not contraindicated.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":134,"output_tokens":98}},"cost":7.622e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2411","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Habits are classified as Intentional and Unintentional by:\n\nOptions: \nA. William James\nB. Kingsley\nC. Earnest Klein\nD. Finn and Sim\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Habits are classified as intentional and unintentional by William James, who discussed the nature of habits in the context of psychology and behavior. He emphasized how habitual actions can be both consciously formed and automatically performed. \n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":103,"output_tokens":48}},"cost":4.219e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_419","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Square root of pq/n indicates:\n\nOptions: \nA. Standard error of mean\nB. Standard error of difference of means\nC. Standard error of proportions\nD. Standard error of difference in proportions\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The expression $\\sqrt{\\frac{pq}{n}}$ represents the standard error for a proportion, where $p$ is the proportion of successes, $q = 1 - p$, and $n$ is the sample size. This formula is used in the context of binomial data to measure the variability of a sample proportion. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":130,"output_tokens":81}},"cost":6.55e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2021","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Km value indicates:\n\nOptions: \nA. Purity of Enzyme\nB. Physiological role\nC. The substrate concentration at half maximal velocity\nD. Aﬃnity\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The Km value, or Michaelis constant, represents the substrate concentration at which the reaction velocity is half of its maximum. It is a measure of the enzyme's affinity for its substrate—lower Km indicates higher affinity. Therefore, the best answer is:\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":102,"output_tokens":56}},"cost":4.686e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2713","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Following renal disorder is associated with worst pregnancy outcome:\n\nOptions: \nA. Systemic lupus erythromatosus\nB. IgA nephropathy\nC. Autosomal dominant polycystic kidney disease\nD. Scleroderma\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Scleroderma, particularly when associated with renal crisis, is linked to high maternal and fetal morbidity and mortality during pregnancy. It can lead to severe hypertension, renal failure, and preeclampsia-like symptoms, resulting in poor pregnancy outcomes. Among the listed conditions, scleroderma carries the worst prognosis in pregnancy.\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":116,"output_tokens":74}},"cost":5.948e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1028","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is responsible for rhythm generation of inspiration?\n\nOptions: \nA. Dorsal nucleus of vagus\nB. Pre botzinger complex\nC. ventral respiratory neurons\nD. Pneumotaxic center\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The Pre-Bötzinger complex, located in the medulla oblongata, is widely recognized as the primary site for generating the respiratory rhythm, particularly for inspiration. It contains specialized neurons that produce the rhythmic drive for breathing. While other centers like the pneumotaxic center and dorsal respiratory group modulate breathing, rhythm generation originates in the Pre-Bötzinger complex.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":110,"output_tokens":83}},"cost":6.41e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2138","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Iodine is primarily important in the biochemical synthesis of:\n\nOptions: \nA. ACTH\nB. Thyroxine\nC. Adrenaline\nD. Calcitonin\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Iodine is essential for the production of thyroid hormones, particularly thyroxine (T4) and triiodothyronine (T3), which are synthesized in the thyroid gland. Among the options listed, thyroxine is the hormone directly dependent on iodine for its structure. The other hormones—ACTH, adrenaline, and calcitonin—do not require iodine for their synthesis.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":101,"output_tokens":87}},"cost":6.533e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2143","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The maximum shrinkage during firing process in ceramic occurs in:\n\nOptions: \nA. High Bisque stage\nB. Low Bisque stage\nC. Medium Bisque stage\nD. Fusion stage\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The maximum shrinkage during the firing process in ceramics occurs as the clay particles sinter and vitrify, which primarily happens at higher temperatures. This significant shrinkage takes place during the fusion stage, where the clay body begins to densify and close pores. \n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":104,"output_tokens":59}},"cost":4.892e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1824","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: TNM Staging is what type of scale\n\nOptions: \nA. Ordinal\nB. Ratio\nC. Nominal\nD. Interval\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"TNM Staging classifies cancer based on the size and extent of the tumor (T), lymph node involvement (N), and metastasis (M), which are ranked in increasing levels of severity. This ranking reflects a meaningful order but does not have equal intervals or a true zero, making it an ordinal scale. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":94,"output_tokens":75}},"cost":5.7220000000000004e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_260","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Landmark for pup chamber opening is :\n\nOptions: \nA. CEJ\nB. Cervical third of crown\nC. Level of alveolar bone\nD. Enamel\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The question pertains to endodontic access cavity preparation, where a key anatomic landmark is needed to safely locate and open into the pulp chamber without perforation or missed canals. The cemento-enamel junction (CEJ) serves this purpose because the pulp chamber roof and floor consistently lie at or just apical to the CEJ level in both anterior and posterior teeth; this relationship is independent of occlusal wear or restoration and is emphasized in standard references such as Ingle’s Endodontics. The remaining options are either too coronal (enamel, cervical third of crown) or unrelated (alveolar bone crest) to the pulp-chamber location.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":218,"output_tokens":129},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":0.0001081,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_65","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The resolution of IOPA is about:\n\nOptions: \nA. 10 Lp/mm\nB. 16 Lp/mm\nC. 28 Lp/mm\nD. 30 Lp/mm\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The resolution of intraoral periapical (IOPA) radiographs is typically around 10 to 20 line pairs per millimeter (Lp/mm), depending on the film or sensor used. Among the options, 16 Lp/mm is a commonly cited value for high-resolution dental film. Therefore, the most accurate choice is:\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":111,"output_tokens":77}},"cost":6.0629999999999994e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1340","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Initial clicking of TMJ while opening is due to\n\nOptions: \nA. Protruded condyle in respect to articular disc\nB. Retruded condyle in respect to articular disc\nC. Perforated disc\nD. Lateral displacement of the condyle\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The most common TMJ internal derangement is anterior disc displacement with reduction. In the closed-mouth position the condyle therefore lies posterior (retruded) to the displaced disc; the audible click occurs at the moment the condyle translates forward and reduces onto the posterior band of the disc. This mechanism directly matches option B and excludes the remaining choices.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":239,"output_tokens":73},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":8.43e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1145","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Highly vascular tumor of brain and spinal cord in adults:\n\nOptions: \nA. Metastasis\nB. Pilocytic astrocytoma\nC. Hemangioblastoma\nD. Cavernous malformation\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Hemangioblastoma is a highly vascular tumor commonly found in the brain and spinal cord of adults, often associated with von Hippel-Lindau disease. It is known for its rich blood supply and predilection for the cerebellum and spinal cord. \n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":109,"output_tokens":61}},"cost":5.0770000000000003e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_461","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The advantage of glass ionomer cement reinforced with metal particles is:\n\nOptions: \nA. Decreased strength but biocompatibility\nB. Increased resistance to abrasion\nC. Better colour\nD. Ease of manipulation\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The advantage of glass ionomer cement reinforced with metal particles is increased resistance to abrasion due to the metal reinforcement enhancing its mechanical properties. This makes the material more durable in stress-bearing areas. \n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":108,"output_tokens":44}},"cost":4.044e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1200","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: \"Multifactorial Causation\" theory was given by\n\nOptions: \nA. McMohan Pugh\nB. Pettenkofer of Munich\nC. Winslow\nD. Robert Koch\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The \"Multifactorial Causation\" theory, which emphasizes that diseases result from multiple factors rather than a single cause, is attributed to Pettenkofer of Munich. He was a pioneer in advocating for environmental and social factors in disease occurrence, particularly in cholera. This contrasts with Koch's single-cause (germ theory) approach.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":106,"output_tokens":77}},"cost":5.998e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_145","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The transport of CO is diffusion limited because\n\nOptions: \nA. Binds avidly with Hb\nB. Partial pressure of CO is less\nC. CO is less absorbed in water\nD. Alveolar membrane is less permeable\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The transport of carbon monoxide (CO) is diffusion limited primarily because it binds very avidly to hemoglobin (Hb), which maintains a steep partial pressure gradient, favoring continued diffusion. This high affinity for Hb means CO is rapidly bound once it enters the blood, minimizing its partial pressure in pulmonary capillary blood and allowing diffusion to continue. Thus, the process remains dependent on the rate at which CO can diffuse across the alveolar membrane.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":114,"output_tokens":97}},"cost":7.302e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_157","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Measuring variation between two different units is done through\n\nOptions: \nA. Variance\nB. Standard deviation\nC. Coefficient of variation\nD. Range\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The coefficient of variation (CV) is a standardized measure of dispersion that expresses the standard deviation as a percentage of the mean, making it useful for comparing variation across different units. Unlike variance, standard deviation, and range, which are in the original units of measurement, the CV is unitless. Therefore, it is the most appropriate measure for comparing variability between two different units.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":98,"output_tokens":80}},"cost":6.0740000000000005e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_192","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In processing methyl methacrylate, the resin may show porosity if the flask is placed too soon. Porosity most likely occur\n\nOptions: \nA. Throughout the denture\nB. Near the borders\nC. In the thickest part\nD. On the denture surface\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Porosity in methyl methacrylate resin most commonly occurs in the thickest part of the denture because this area cools and polymerizes unevenly, trapping more monomer and creating bubbles. If the flask is placed too soon, inadequate packing and increased trapped air exacerbate this issue in thick sections. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":123,"output_tokens":75}},"cost":6.0990000000000004e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_254","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Child Pugh score put patients into three categories of Score A (<7), Score B (7-9) and Score C (10-15). The following is a type of which scale?\n\nOptions: \nA. Nominal\nB. Ordinal\nC. Quantitative\nD. Continuous\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The Child Pugh score categorizes patients into ordered groups (A, B, C) based on severity, where the categories have a meaningful sequence but not equal intervals. This indicates an ordinal scale, as the values represent ranks or levels rather than precise numerical differences. \n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":126,"output_tokens":59}},"cost":5.1779999999999996e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_290","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Tracheostomy will:\n\nOptions: \nA. Increase dead air space\nB. Increase respiratory resistance\nC. Decrease respiratory work\nD. Cause obstruction in respiration\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"A tracheostomy reduces the anatomical dead space and decreases resistance to airflow by providing a direct route to the trachea, thus reducing the work of breathing. It does not increase dead space or respiratory resistance, nor does it typically cause obstruction when properly managed. Therefore, the most accurate answer is that it decreases respiratory work.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":100,"output_tokens":72}},"cost":5.619999999999999e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_313","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 22 years old male presented with history of fever, sore throat and enlarged neck lymph nodes. He was ordered a Paul-Bunnell test with a suspicion of Infectious mononucleosis. What is the immunological basis behind the use of this test?\n\nOptions: \nA. Heterophile antibody test\nB. Complement mediated agglutination reaction\nC. Homophile antibody test\nD. Latex agglutination test\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The Paul-Bunnell test detects heterophile antibodies produced in response to Epstein-Barr virus infection, which cause agglutination of sheep or horse red blood cells. These antibodies are not specific to the virus but cross-react with animal RBCs, forming the basis of the test. This makes it a classic example of a heterophile antibody test.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":156,"output_tokens":76}},"cost":6.588000000000001e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_315","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The microwave method of processing resin is better than the conventional in that it provides:\n\nOptions: \nA. Better shine\nB. Less porosity\nC. Less shrinkage\nD. Color stability\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The microwave method of processing resin is known to result in more uniform polymerization, which reduces the formation of pores. This leads to a denser, higher-quality restoration with improved physical properties. Therefore, the most significant advantage is less porosity.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":104,"output_tokens":55}},"cost":4.652e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_337","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Induction of inhalational agent is faster.\n\nOptions: \nA. Agent with high blood gas solubility\nB. Combined with nitrous oxide\nC. Person with increased residual volume\nD. Right to left shunt\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The speed of induction of an inhalational agent is faster when the agent has low blood gas solubility, not high, so option A is incorrect. Combining an inhalational agent with nitrous oxide accelerates induction because nitrous oxide rapidly diffuses into the alveoli and increases the alveolar concentration of the other agent (second gas effect). Therefore, the correct answer is B.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":110,"output_tokens":86}},"cost":6.59e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_341","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: HCO3/H2CO3 is the best buffer because it is:\n\nOptions: \nA. pKa near physiological pH\nB. Its components can be increased or decreased in the body as needed\nC. Good acceptor and donor of H+ ions\nD. Combination of a weak acid and weak base\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The bicarbonate buffer system (\\(\\mathrm{HCO_3^-}/\\mathrm{H_2CO_3}\\)) is physiologically effective in blood despite a \\(\\mathrm{p}K_a\\) of 6.1 because its two components are under independent, rapid physiologic control (\\(\\mathrm{PCO_2}\\) via ventilation, \\(\\mathrm{HCO_3^-}\\) via renal reabsorption/excretion). This regulatory flexibility allows the system to resist pH change far more effectively than a simple chemical buffer pair whose concentrations are fixed. All other listed properties are either true of any buffer pair or factually inaccurate for this system.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":248,"output_tokens":125},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":0.0001121,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_380","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A voluntary donor underwent apheresis for platelet donation for the first time after which he developed perioral tingling and numbness. This is seen because\n\nOptions: \nA. His platelet count was low for donation\nB. He underwent apheresis for the first time\nC. Due to fluid depletion\nD. Due to citrate based anticoagulant\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The perioral tingling and numbness experienced by the donor are classic symptoms of hypocalcemia caused by citrate, which is used as an anticoagulant during apheresis. Citrate binds calcium in the blood, leading to a temporary decrease in ionized calcium levels. This reaction is common during platelet donation via apheresis, especially in first-time donors, but is primarily due to the citrate, not the donation itself.\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":141,"output_tokens":98}},"cost":7.713e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_433","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Malaria control means\n\nOptions: \nA. To reduce Malaria moality to Zero\nB. To prevent local transmission for 3 years\nC. To reduce Malaria disease so that its no longer a Public Health Problem\nD. To reduce Incidence to Zero\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Malaria control aims to reduce the burden of the disease to a level where it is no longer a significant public health issue. It does not necessarily mean eliminating all cases or transmission, but rather managing and minimizing its impact. \n\nThe most accurate answer is: \\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":119,"output_tokens":57}},"cost":4.967e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_478","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following best describes the resistance form in endodontic root canal preparation?\n\nOptions: \nA. The establishment of apical tug back resistance to prevent the apical root fracture during obturation\nB. The cavity form which is obtained for application of condenser in vertical compaction\nC. The cavity form which is designed for application of condenser in lateral compaction\nD. Cavity form which is designed to obtain for entry of condenser during obturation\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The resistance form during root canal preparation refers to the overall canal shape (taper and apical stop) that can withstand the forces applied by hand or finger pluggers/condensers without risking root fracture or extrusion of material. This requirement is most directly satisfied by the continuous, uniformly tapered preparation needed for vertical compaction, allowing the selected pluggers to fit passively to within 5–7 mm of the working length. Options A and C describe apical tug-back or lateral-compaction spreader access, respectively, which relate more to retention form or master-cone fit than to resistance against condensation loads.\n\nThus, the best match among the given choices is B.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":272,"output_tokens":135},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":0.00012190000000000001,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_481","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Internal occlusal rest provided in partial denture does not provide:\n\nOptions: \nA. Horizontal stabilization\nB. Retention\nC. Vertical stop\nD. Occlusal support\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Internal occlusal rest in a partial denture primarily serves to provide vertical support and act as a vertical stop, helping to prevent gingival displacement of the prosthesis. It does not contribute significantly to retention, which is mainly achieved through direct retainers like clasps. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":102,"output_tokens":68}},"cost":5.4059999999999994e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_487","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: For statistical test output of p value is interpreted as\n\nOptions: \nA. Rejective Ho, p <0.05\nB. Rejective Ho, p>0.05\nC. Rejective H1, p<0.05\nD. Accepting Ho, p<0.05\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The p-value is used to determine whether to reject the null hypothesis (H₀). If the p-value is less than the significance level (typically 0.05), we reject H₀. Therefore, the correct interpretation is that we reject H₀ when p < 0.05.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":130,"output_tokens":65}},"cost":5.5900000000000004e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_545","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The principal reason for placing an aluminium filter in\nthe primary beam of radiation is to:\n\nOptions: \nA. Reduce exposure time\nB. Decrease development time of the films\nC. Reduce radiation to the skin of the patient\nD. Obtain greater definition of the images of teeth\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The principal reason for placing an aluminium filter in the primary beam of radiation is to remove low-energy (soft) X-rays that contribute to patient skin dose but do not enhance image quality. These low-energy photons are absorbed by the patient’s skin and superficial tissues, increasing radiation risk without diagnostic benefit. The aluminium filter selectively absorbs these photons, thereby reducing radiation to the skin.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":122,"output_tokens":79}},"cost":6.326e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_575","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A patient presented with acute exacerbation of bronchial asthma. Salbutamol inhalation didn't improve the condition of the patient. So, intravenous coicosteroids and aminophylline were added and the condition improved. What is the mechanism of action of coicosteroids in this condition?\n\nOptions: \nA. They cause bronchodilatation when given with xanthines\nB. They increase bronchial responsiveness to salbutamol\nC. They increase the action of aminophylline on adenosine receptors\nD. They increase the mucociliary clearance\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Corticosteroids reduce airway inflammation and edema in asthma, which helps restore the responsiveness of the airways to beta-2 agonists like salbutamol. They do not cause direct bronchodilation but enhance the effectiveness of other drugs by modulating gene expression involved in inflammation. This improved response indirectly supports the action of bronchodilators, but the key mechanism in severe asthma is reducing inflammation and airway hyperresponsiveness.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":188,"output_tokens":94}},"cost":8.083999999999999e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_734","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Central value of a set of 180 values can be obtained by\n\nOptions: \nA. 2nd tertile\nB. 90th percentile\nC. 2nd quartile\nD. 9th decile\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The central value of a set of 180 values is the median, which divides the data into two equal halves. The 2nd quartile (Q2) corresponds to the median, representing the 50th percentile. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":114,"output_tokens":61}},"cost":5.1420000000000006e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_747","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Compared to unfractionated heparin, Low molecular weight heparin (LMWH) has reliable anticoagulant action because:\n\nOptions: \nA. It interferes with thrombin and antithrombin III simultaneously\nB. It is less protein bound\nC. It is given subcutaneously\nD. It is cleared by macrophages\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Low molecular weight heparin (LMWH) has more predictable pharmacokinetics and reliable anticoagulant action primarily because it is less bound to plasma proteins compared to unfractionated heparin. This reduced protein binding results in a more consistent anticoagulant response and longer half-life. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":137,"output_tokens":73}},"cost":6.161e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_793","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Mandibular fracture managed by adapting mini plates is a type of\n\nOptions: \nA. Load bearing osteosynthesis\nB. Load sharing\nC. Non rigid osteosynthesis\nD. Rigid osteosynthesis\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The use of mini plates in mandibular fracture management provides stable fixation that allows early function, which is characteristic of rigid osteosynthesis. This method aims to immobilize the fracture segments completely, promoting primary bone healing. \n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":109,"output_tokens":50}},"cost":4.417e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_800","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following cause an increase in ACh release from the presynaptic neuron?\n\nOptions: \nA. Blocking calcium channels on presynaptic\nB. Blocking chloride channel on presynaptic\nC. Blocking Na channel\nD. Blocking K channels\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Blocking potassium (K) channels prolongs the depolarization phase of the action potential in the presynaptic neuron, which keeps voltage-gated calcium channels open longer. This increased calcium influx enhances the release of acetylcholine (ACh) into the synaptic cleft. Therefore, blocking K channels increases ACh release.\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":116,"output_tokens":71}},"cost":5.768e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_864","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following is used for selecting patients with respect to potential factors that will affect the results?\n\nOptions: \nA. Systematic random sampling\nB. Simple random sampling\nC. Stratified random sampling\nD. Cluster sampling\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Stratified random sampling is specifically designed to divide a population (e.g., patients) into subgroups/strata based on key factors or characteristics that could influence outcomes, then randomly sample within each stratum to ensure balanced representation and reduce bias. In contrast, simple random sampling, systematic random sampling, and cluster sampling do not explicitly account for such factors during selection. This aligns directly with the question's focus on controlling for potential confounding variables in patient selection.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":231,"output_tokens":92},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":9.22e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_947","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Bacteria associated with caries are able to cause the same due to:\n\nOptions: \nA. Production of extxacellular polysaccharides like dextrans and levans\nB. Production of acid to hydrolyse diet carbohydrates\nC. Production of enzymes which inhibit normal flora\nD. Inhibition of secretory IgA\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Bacteria associated with dental caries, such as *Streptococcus mutans*, metabolize dietary carbohydrates to produce acids that demineralize tooth enamel. This acid production is the primary mechanism leading to caries formation. While extracellular polysaccharides (like dextrans) help in bacterial adherence, acid production is directly responsible for enamel breakdown.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":131,"output_tokens":78}},"cost":6.383e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1054","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Disadvantages of using a GRID during radiography is:\n\nOptions: \nA. Increased patient exposure due to more exposure time\nB. Decreased exposure time\nC. Increased secondary radiation fog to film\nD. Reduces secondary radiation to film\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The use of a grid in radiography helps reduce scattered (secondary) radiation, improving image contrast by allowing primarily primary radiation to reach the film. However, because grids absorb some of the useful radiation as well, a higher exposure (mAs) is often required to maintain adequate film density, leading to increased patient dose. Therefore, the main disadvantage is increased patient exposure due to the need for more exposure time or higher technique.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":114,"output_tokens":91}},"cost":6.942e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1134","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Beveling of the pulpoaxial line angle of a class II cavity\nis done to:\n\nOptions: \nA. Increase the strength of the restoration\nB. Improved marginal adaptation\nC. To prevent the fracture of enamel\nD. To prevent the fracture of amalgam\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Beveling (typically a 15–30° cavosurface bevel) of the axiopulpal line angle in a Class II amalgam preparation increases the bulk of amalgam precisely where the restoration is thinnest and subjected to the greatest occlusal flexure. This added thickness reduces stress concentration at the isthmus and thereby lowers the risk of amalgam fracture. The other listed reasons (enamel protection, marginal adaptation at the cavosurface, or general strengthening) are not the primary rationale for this internal-line-angle modification.\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":240,"output_tokens":111},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":0.0001035,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1167","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The purpose of pulpotomy in young permanent tooth\n\nOptions: \nA. Prevent tooth fracture\nB. To induce root formation\nC. Formation of hard base to support restoration\nD. To minimize infection\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The purpose of pulpotomy in a young permanent tooth is primarily to preserve the vitality of the pulp to allow continued root development. By removing the infected coronal pulp while maintaining the radicular pulp, the procedure supports continued root formation and apexogenesis. This makes option B the most accurate choice.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":106,"output_tokens":64}},"cost":5.218e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1169","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The penetration of the fissure sealant into the fissure:\n\nOptions: \nA. Is not influenced by the wettability of the enamel\nB. Is independent of the chemical composition of the enamel\nC. Is the result of a chemical bond between the sealant and enamel\nD. Must occur before the polymerization of the material\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The penetration of the fissure sealant into the fissure depends on the sealant material flowing into the prepared enamel grooves before it hardens. This process must happen before polymerization, as once the material sets, it can no longer flow into the fissure. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":133,"output_tokens":66}},"cost":5.689e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1203","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following is main cause of pain during pulpal injury progression?\n\nOptions: \nA. Increased vascular permeability\nB. Decreased threshold of nerve fibres to pain\nC. Arteriolar dilatation\nD. Decrease pressure\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The dental pulp is rigidly confined, so any injury triggers inflammation with release of mediators (e.g., bradykinin, prostaglandins, substance P). These mediators directly sensitize nociceptive nerve endings, lowering their activation threshold and thereby producing pain. While vascular changes (A, C) and pressure shifts (D) occur, they are secondary; the decisive event for pain generation is the lowered nerve threshold.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":230,"output_tokens":85},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":8.850000000000001e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1204","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Decay of enamel following radiotherapy is initiated due to:\n\nOptions: \nA. Decrease in salivary flow\nB. Direct radiations contacting the enamel\nC. Dessication of tooth structure\nD. Hypocalcification and pitting of enamel\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The decay of enamel following radiotherapy is primarily due to a significant reduction in salivary flow, which compromises the mouth's natural protective and buffering mechanisms. Saliva helps neutralize acids, remineralize enamel, and wash away food debris; its decrease creates a highly cariogenic environment. Although other factors like enamel hypocalcification may play a role, the main initiating factor is xerostomia caused by radiation damage to salivary glands.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":116,"output_tokens":98}},"cost":7.388e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1227","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The decreased phosphate levels seen in hyper parathyroidism is due to:\n\nOptions: \nA. Decreased intestinal phosphate absorption\nB. Increased calcium excretion\nC. Decreased renal phosphate absorption\nD. Increased loss of phosphate in urine\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The decreased phosphate levels in hyperparathyroidism are primarily due to increased phosphate excretion by the kidneys. Parathyroid hormone (PTH) reduces renal reabsorption of phosphate, leading to its increased loss in urine. This directly results in hypophosphatemia.\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":113,"output_tokens":61}},"cost":5.1290000000000005e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1250","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: HIV sentinel surveillance provides data:\n\nOptions: \nA. To monitor disease trends\nB. To identify high risk population\nC. To estimate disease incidence\nD. To assess the quality of related services\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Sentinel surveillance for HIV is a targeted system that monitors prevalence (not incidence) over time at fixed sites or in fixed populations, making its core function the detection of disease trends. While it may incidentally involve high-risk groups, this is a means to the end of trend monitoring rather than the primary output. Options C and D are outside its scope, as incidence estimation requires cohort or laboratory methods and service-quality assessment requires separate evaluation data.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":225,"output_tokens":90},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":9e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1298","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Increased depth in posterior palatal seal area of denture \ncauses:\n\nOptions: \nA. Tingling sensation\nB. Gagging\nC. Increased retention\nD. Unseating of denture base\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The posterior palatal seal (PPS) creates a peripheral seal in compressible tissue to aid maxillary denture retention. Excessive depth (i.e., over-carving the master cast) produces hypercompression, which displaces the denture anteriorly and breaks the intended seal, resulting in unseating/rocking. The remaining options are unrelated: gagging is triggered by posterior placement (not depth), tingling implies nerve impingement, and properly executed PPS depth increases—not decreases—retention.\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":228,"output_tokens":100},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":9.56e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1309","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which factor of the following contributes to short duration of anesthetic action of single dose thiopental\n\nOptions: \nA. Rapid biotransformation\nB. Rapid accumulation in body fat\nC. High lipid solubility\nD. Ability to enter and leave brain tissue every rapidly\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Thiopental is a highly lipophilic barbiturate whose rapid onset after IV bolus is due to quick brain uptake. Its duration of unconsciousness after a single dose, however, is brief (minutes) because falling plasma levels allow the drug to diffuse out of the brain; the principal driver of that plasma decline is redistribution into less-well-perfused, high-capacity tissues such as fat.  \n\nOption A is incorrect because hepatic metabolism of thiopental is slow; options C and D describe the same lipid-solubility property that permits rapid brain entry/exit but do not themselves terminate the anesthetic effect.  \n\nThus the factor listed that directly accounts for the short clinical action is rapid accumulation in body fat (redistribution).\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":239,"output_tokens":147},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":0.0001213,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1319","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Test to exclude a disease\n\nOptions: \nA. Positive predictivity\nB. Negative predictivity\nC. Specificity\nD. Sensitivity\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"To exclude a disease, a test should correctly identify those without the disease, minimizing false positives. This is best measured by specificity, which reflects the ability of the test to correctly rule out the disease in healthy individuals. A high specificity ensures that a negative result is reliable for exclusion.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":94,"output_tokens":62}},"cost":4.942e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1344","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The usefulness of a screening test depends upon it\n\nOptions: \nA. Sensitivity\nB. Specificity\nC. Reliability\nD. Predictive value\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The usefulness of a screening test is ultimately judged by its ability to correctly identify the probability of disease (or its absence) in a tested individual, which is captured by predictive values. While sensitivity and specificity are intrinsic test properties that contribute to this, they do not by themselves determine real-world utility in a population (which also incorporates disease prevalence). Reliability is a separate consideration related to reproducibility rather than accuracy or yield.\n\nThus, the most appropriate choice is D.\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":214,"output_tokens":95},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":9.03e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1360","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Isosorbide 5 — mononitrate is preferred because\n\nOptions: \nA. Less tolerance develops\nB. Sublingual absorption is better\nC. Longer duration of action\nD. Direct coronary vasodilatory action is more\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Isosorbide 5-mononitrate is preferred over other nitrates because it has a longer duration of action, allowing for less frequent dosing and improved patient compliance. This pharmacokinetic property makes it more effective for prophylactic management of angina. Tolerance can still develop, but the extended release formulations help mitigate this issue.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":115,"output_tokens":77}},"cost":6.115e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1394","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Nitrous oxide alone is not used as a G.A agent because of\n\nOptions: \nA. Difficulty in maintaining an adequate oxygen concentration\nB. Expense of the agent and its exposure hazards\nC. Adverse effect on liver\nD. Poor analgesic property\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Nitrous oxide alone cannot provide sufficient anesthesia because it lacks potent anesthetic properties and cannot maintain an adequate depth of anesthesia. It is typically used in combination with other agents to ensure effective general anesthesia while maintaining safe oxygen levels. The primary reason it is not used alone is its inability to maintain adequate oxygen concentration, which poses a risk of hypoxia.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":141,"output_tokens":109}},"cost":8.372999999999999e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1402","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Angles between Adhesive and Adherent is Zero degree, it indicates:\n\nOptions: \nA. Complete wetting of surfaces\nB. Rough surfaces between Adhesive & Adherent\nC. Adherent and adhesive molecules are tangent to each other\nD. Irregularities present between Adherent surfaces\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"When the contact angle between an adhesive and an adherent is zero degrees, it means the adhesive spreads completely over the surface, indicating maximum adhesion. This signifies complete wetting, where the adhesive forms a uniform film with no beading. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":124,"output_tokens":60}},"cost":5.212e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1413","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Schizonts and late trophozoite stages of plasmodium falciparum not seen in peripheral blood smear because:\n\nOptions: \nA. They are sequestered in the spleen\nB. Due to adherence to the capillary endothelium, they are not seen in peripheral blood\nC. Due to antigen-antibody reaction and removal\nD. They are seen in mosquito blood\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The schizonts and late trophozoites of *Plasmodium falciparum* are not typically seen in peripheral blood smears because they sequester in deep tissues by adhering to capillary endothelium, particularly in organs like the brain and kidneys. This cytoadherence prevents their circulation in peripheral blood. \n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":149,"output_tokens":76}},"cost":6.497000000000001e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1436","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: During relining procedures fear lies in the alteration of\n\nOptions: \nA. Balanced occlusion\nB. Centric occlusion\nC. Vertical dimension\nD. Condylar guidance\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The primary concern during denture relining is maintaining the correct vertical dimension of occlusion, as changes can lead to discomfort, temporomandibular joint issues, and poor function. Altering the vertical dimension unintentionally during relining can disrupt the entire occlusal scheme and neuromuscular adaptation. Therefore, fear during relining is most associated with changes in vertical dimension.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":102,"output_tokens":83}},"cost":6.306e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1451","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of these findings is not specific of blast injury?\n\nOptions: \nA. Abrasion\nB. Bruise\nC. Puncture laceration\nD. Fracture\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Blast injuries produce characteristic external wounds from the blast wave and secondary missiles (e.g., multiple small puncture lacerations, peppering abrasions, and bruises). Fractures, by contrast, are produced by generic blunt-force mechanisms (tertiary impact) and are therefore not regarded as specific markers of an explosion. Consequently, among the listed options, fracture is the finding that is not specific to blast injury.\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":219,"output_tokens":84},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":8.58e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1488","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Phosphate bonded investment should be completely carbon free, otherwise:\n\nOptions: \nA. Investment chips off when molten metal enters the mold space\nB. Black castings\nC. Carbon makes the casting brittle\nD. Smooth casting\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"If phosphate-bonded investment is not completely carbon free, residual carbon can transfer to the casting, resulting in discoloration and surface defects. This typically manifests as black or discolored castings due to carbon pickup from incomplete burnout. Therefore, the most likely consequence is black castings.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":137,"output_tokens":83}},"cost":6.761e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1523","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: NK cells are effective against viral infected cells only if the cell with infection:\n\nOptions: \nA. Express MHC class I proteins\nB. Unable to express MHC class I proteins\nC. Express MHC class II proteins\nD. Unable to express MHC class II proteins\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Natural killer (NK) cells target cells that have downregulated or lack MHC class I molecules, which often occurs in viral infections to evade cytotoxic T cells. This absence of MHC class I is recognized by NK cells as a danger signal, triggering their killing activity. Therefore, NK cells are effective when the infected cell is unable to express MHC class I proteins.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":121,"output_tokens":80}},"cost":6.373e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1570","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Mean and standard deviation can be worked out only if data is on\n\nOptions: \nA. Nominal scale\nB. Dichotomous scale\nC. Interval/Ratio scale\nD. Ordinal scale\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Mean and standard deviation require numerical data with equal intervals and a meaningful zero, which are characteristics of interval and ratio scales. These measures involve arithmetic operations that are not valid on nominal, ordinal, or dichotomous data. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":107,"output_tokens":57}},"cost":4.811e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1572","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Mean and standard deviation can be worked out only if data is on -\n\nOptions: \nA. Interval/Ratio scale\nB. Dichotomous scale\nC. Nominal scale\nD. Ordinal scale\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Mean and standard deviation require numerical data with equal intervals and a true zero or consistent scale, which are properties of interval and ratio scales. These measures involve arithmetic operations that are not meaningful on nominal, ordinal, or dichotomous data. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":107,"output_tokens":61}},"cost":5.051e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1576","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Increased size of filler particle in composite:\n\nOptions: \nA. Increases strength\nB. Decreases surface roughness\nC. Increases exposure time\nD. decreases viscosity\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Larger filler particles in a composite generally reduce the surface area, which can decrease viscosity due to less particle-particle interaction. However, they typically result in lower strength and increased surface roughness compared to smaller particles. Therefore, the most accurate effect among the options is a decrease in viscosity.\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":98,"output_tokens":64}},"cost":5.114e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1595","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Feed forward mechanism..\n\nOptions: \nA. Feeling thirsty while walking in hot temperature\nB. Shivering on exposure to cold temperature\nC. Salivation on smelling food\nD. Increase blood pressure during supine posture\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The feed-forward mechanism prepares the body for an expected change based on a predictable stimulus. Salivation on smelling food is a classic example, as the body anticipates food intake and begins digestion before eating. This proactive response aligns with feed-forward control.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":108,"output_tokens":55}},"cost":4.7040000000000004e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1623","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In reversible hydrocolloid the property by which the transformation from sol to gel and gel to sol occurs, is a function of the:\n\nOptions: \nA. Concentration of fillers and plasticizer\nB. Percentage composition by weight of water\nC. Concentration of potassium sulphate\nD. Temperature\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The transformation of reversible hydrocolloid from sol to gel and vice versa is primarily dependent on temperature changes. Cooling causes the sol to set into a gel, while heating converts the gel back into a sol. This thermally reversible behavior is a defining characteristic of reversible hydrocolloids.\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":126,"output_tokens":62}},"cost":5.358e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1641","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following hormones is controlled by feedforward control?\n\nOptions: \nA. ADH\nB. Insulin\nC. Coicosteroids\nD. Prolactin\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Feedforward control in endocrine physiology refers to anticipatory regulation that acts prior to a disturbance (e.g., the cephalic-phase release of insulin triggered by sight/smell of food to preemptively limit postprandial glucose excursions). In contrast, ADH, corticosteroids, and prolactin are governed by classic negative-feedback loops that respond to sensed changes in osmolality, ACTH, or dopamine tone, respectively. Thus insulin is the only option whose secretion is characteristically initiated by feedforward mechanisms.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":221,"output_tokens":100},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":9.42e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1696","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Radio density can be increased by\n\nOptions: \nA. Decreasing MA\nB. Decreasing kVp\nC. Decreasing target film distance\nD. Increasing target film distance\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Radio density refers to the degree of darkening on a radiographic image. Decreasing the target-film distance reduces the spread of the X-ray beam, resulting in a more concentrated beam and increased exposure to the film, thereby increasing radio density. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":102,"output_tokens":61}},"cost":4.986e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1721","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What does low volume of distribution of a drug mean?\n\nOptions: \nA. Low bioavailability\nB. Does not accumulates in tissues\nC. Low absorption\nD. Not metabolized in the body\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"A low volume of distribution means the drug remains primarily in the bloodstream and does not extensively distribute into tissues. This indicates that the drug does not accumulate in tissues. It is not directly related to bioavailability, absorption, or metabolism.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":125,"output_tokens":71}},"cost":5.8849999999999994e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1731","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Pulpectomy and pulp capping are more successful in\nprimary teeth because of:\n\nOptions: \nA. Increased odontoblastic activity in the young\nB. Increased blood supply through the wide apex\nC. Increased volume of pulp in primary teeth\nD. Lesser amount of collagen fibres in young\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Pulpectomy and pulp capping are more successful in primary teeth due to their wider apical foramina, which allow for better blood supply and enhanced healing potential. This increased vascularity supports tissue repair and reduces the risk of necrosis. Therefore, the most accurate answer is:\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":126,"output_tokens":63}},"cost":5.418e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1779","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Low apparent volume of distribution of a drug indicates That\n\nOptions: \nA. Drug has low half life\nB. Drug has low bioavailability\nC. Drug has low efficacy\nD. Drug is not extensively distribution to tissue\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Low apparent volume of distribution indicates that the drug remains primarily in the plasma and does not distribute widely into tissues. This suggests the drug is confined to the bloodstream and extracellular fluid. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":110,"output_tokens":49}},"cost":4.37e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1789","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the advantage of chromic gut over plain\ngut suture in deep wounds?\n\nOptions: \nA. Greater strength\nB. Greater ease of use\nC. Delayed resorption\nD. Less tissue irritation\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Chromic gut suture is treated with chromium salts, which delays its absorption compared to plain gut suture. This delayed resorption allows chromic gut to maintain tensile strength longer, making it more suitable for deep tissues that take longer to heal. Therefore, the main advantage in deep wounds is prolonged wound support.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":110,"output_tokens":70}},"cost":5.63e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1822","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Streptococci have the ability to adhere to the tooth surfaces and contribute to caries development as they?\n\nOptions: \nA. Are penicillinase resistant\nB. Produce acid during metabolism\nC. Produce extracellular polysachharides\nD. Ferment carbohydrates\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Streptococcus mutans (a key cariogenic streptococcus) adheres to enamel via synthesis of extracellular glucans/polysaccharides from dietary sucrose; these polymers form the plaque biofilm matrix that also traps acids.  \nOptions B and D describe acidogenesis (the mechanism of demineralization) but do not account for the adherence step highlighted in the question; option A is unrelated to caries pathogenesis.  \nThus the single best answer is C.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":235,"output_tokens":91},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":9.25e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1885","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If rate of loading is decreased, the mechanical properties of material:\n\nOptions: \nA. Remains unchanged\nB. Increases\nC. Decreases\nD. Becomes unpredictable\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Decreasing the rate of loading typically allows more time for plastic deformation and stress relaxation in materials, especially in ductile or viscoelastic materials. This often results in lower measured strength and stiffness, effectively reducing apparent mechanical properties like yield strength and ultimate tensile strength. Therefore, the mechanical properties tend to decrease.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":100,"output_tokens":68}},"cost":5.379999999999999e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1896","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Condylar fracture which leads to disruption of TMJ anteriorly is an example of:\n\nOptions: \nA. Simple fracture\nB. Compound fracture\nC. Complex fracture\nD. Comminuted fracture\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The classification of fractures depends on communication with the external environment (or a body cavity open to it). A condylar head fracture that disrupts the TMJ capsule anteriorly creates direct continuity between the fracture site and the joint space (a synovial cavity), rendering the injury compound by definition. This distinguishes it from a simple closed fracture, a comminuted fracture (multiple fragments), or a generic complex fracture (soft-tissue damage without an open communication).\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":226,"output_tokens":92},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":9.12e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1904","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: During exercise in physiological limits what is the effect on end systolic volume?\n\nOptions: \nA. ESV decreases\nB. ESV increase\nC. ESV remain unchanged\nD. ESV first decrease and then increases\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"During moderate exercise within physiological limits, increased sympathetic activity enhances myocardial contractility, leading to more complete emptying of the left ventricle. This results in a decrease in end-systolic volume (ESV). Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":106,"output_tokens":56}},"cost":4.7380000000000004e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1920","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Tachycardia in a patient in shock is response to:\n\nOptions: \nA. Hypotension\nB. Vasoconstriction\nC. CNS anoxia\nD. Anxiety\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Tachycardia in a patient in shock is primarily a compensatory response to maintain cardiac output in the setting of low blood pressure. The body increases heart rate to offset reduced perfusion caused by hypotension. Therefore, the most direct cause is hypotension.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":104,"output_tokens":60}},"cost":4.952e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1926","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Inferior thyroid artery ligation during thyroidectomy is done\n\nOptions: \nA. For recurrent Laryngeal nerve\nB. Superior laryngeal nerve\nC. Vagus nerve\nD. Glossopharyngeal nerve\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The inferior thyroid artery is closely related to the recurrent laryngeal nerve, which runs posterior to it in the tracheoesophageal groove. During thyroidectomy, ligation of the inferior thyroid artery requires careful dissection to avoid injury to the recurrent laryngeal nerve, which supplies motor function to the intrinsic muscles of the larynx. Therefore, the ligation is specifically done with attention to preserving the recurrent laryngeal nerve.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":112,"output_tokens":96}},"cost":7.216e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1943","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a coho study, to study association between factor and disease, the risk ratio was calculated to be equal to 1. What does this signifies?\n\nOptions: \nA. There is no association present between the factor and the disease\nB. There is positive association between the factor and the disease\nC. There is negative association between the factor and the disease\nD. Data insufficient to comment\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Risk ratio (also called relative risk) is calculated in cohort studies as the ratio of incidence in the exposed group to incidence in the unexposed group. A value of exactly 1 therefore indicates that the incidence is identical in both groups, so the exposure is unrelated to disease occurrence. Options B and C would require a risk ratio >1 or <1, respectively, while D is inapplicable because the ratio itself supplies the needed information.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":265,"output_tokens":91},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":9.850000000000001e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1971","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following leads to an increase in enzyme activity -\n\nOptions: \nA. Increase in temperature\nB. Decrease in activation energy\nC. Extremes of pH value\nD. Low substrate concentration\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Enzymes catalyze reactions by lowering the activation energy barrier, which directly increases reaction rate (i.e., enzyme activity) per the Arrhenius equation and transition-state theory. Options A, C, and D are factors that can modulate activity but do not reliably or directly increase it (temperature and pH have optima beyond which denaturation occurs; low substrate reduces velocity per Michaelis-Menten kinetics). Thus B is the only choice that consistently produces the stated effect.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":227,"output_tokens":94},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":9.24e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2032","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The speed with which the electrons travel from the\nfilament of cathode to the anode depends upon\n\nOptions: \nA. Potential difference between the two electrodes\nB. Number of milliamperes in the tube circuit\nC. Angle between the filament and target\nD. Voltage of the filament\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The speed of electrons traveling from the cathode filament to the anode is primarily determined by the potential difference (voltage) between the two electrodes. This potential difference accelerates the electrons across the tube. While filament voltage and tube current (milliamperes) affect electron emission and quantity, they do not directly control electron speed.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":126,"output_tokens":72}},"cost":5.9579999999999995e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2046","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Good contacts in primary teeth with lack of spacing predicts?\n\nOptions: \nA. Normal occlusion in permanent teeth\nB. Crowding in permanent teeth\nC. Anterior cross bite\nD. Spaced permanent dentition\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Good contacts in primary teeth with lack of spacing typically indicate insufficient space for the larger permanent teeth, which are about 7-10 mm wider collectively in the anterior region.\n\nThis crowding in the primary dentition often carries over into the permanent dentition due to the size discrepancy.\n\nTherefore, the most likely outcome is crowding in permanent teeth.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":109,"output_tokens":75}},"cost":5.9170000000000004e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2063","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a patient with acute pulpitis, it is difficult for the patient to locate the pain. This is because?\n\nOptions: \nA. No nociceptors are present in the pulp\nB. Less proprioceptors are present in the pulp\nC. Patient cannot speak\nD. Patient is not cooperative\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The difficulty in locating pain in acute pulpitis is due to the low density of proprioceptors (mechanoreceptors) in the dental pulp, which impairs localization. Pain is primarily sensed by nociceptors, which are abundant in the pulp, but without sufficient spatial sensory input, the brain cannot pinpoint the exact tooth. This leads to vague, radiating pain typical of pulpitis.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":126,"output_tokens":84}},"cost":6.678e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2098","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following hormones increases the sensitivity of heart to epinephrine:\n\nOptions: \nA. Parathyroid\nB. Insulin\nC. Thyroid\nD. Glucagon\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The hormone that increases the sensitivity of the heart to epinephrine is thyroid hormone, which enhances the responsiveness of beta-adrenergic receptors. This leads to increased heart rate and contractility when epinephrine is present. \n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":104,"output_tokens":53}},"cost":4.532e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2113","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Interdental papilla protruding from the rubber dam, most common cause is\n\nOptions: \nA. Inflammation of interdental papillae\nB. Use of light weight rubber dam\nC. Punch are placed too far\nD. Punch are placed too close\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The most common cause of interdental papilla protruding through the rubber dam is when the holes punched in the dam are too close together, forcing the material to stretch excessively and allowing the papilla to bulge through. This misplacement increases the risk of tissue trauma and poor isolation. \n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":121,"output_tokens":64}},"cost":5.413e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2183","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A study was done where the sale of anti-asthma drug was recorded and the number of deaths because of asthma was measured over a period of 15 years (1975-1990). This is which type of study.\n\nOptions: \nA. Ecological\nB. Case reference\nC. Experimental\nD. Psephology\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The study described observes population-level data (sales of an anti-asthma drug and asthma-related deaths) over time without manipulating variables or following individuals. This is characteristic of an ecological study, which analyzes data at the group or population level rather than the individual level. \n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":138,"output_tokens":59}},"cost":5.334e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2243","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Phenylbutyrate is used in management of urea cycle disorders. What is its role?\n\nOptions: \nA. Activates enzymes of urea cycle\nB. Excretion of products of urea cycle\nC. Maintains energy production\nD. Scavenges nitrogen\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Phenylbutyrate is used in urea cycle disorders to help remove excess nitrogen from the body. It acts as a nitrogen scavenger by conjugating with glutamine to form phenylacetylglutamine, which is excreted in urine, thereby reducing ammonia levels. This process effectively lowers the nitrogen load that would otherwise enter the urea cycle.\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":137,"output_tokens":89}},"cost":7.120999999999999e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2276","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Standard deviation of means measures -\n\nOptions: \nA. Non-sampling errors\nB. Sampling error\nC. Random errors\nD. Conceptual errors\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The standard deviation of means, also known as the standard error, measures the variability of sample means around the population mean due to random sampling fluctuations. It quantifies the precision of the sample mean as an estimate of the population mean. This is directly related to sampling error.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":95,"output_tokens":59}},"cost":4.775e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2282","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following gives the rate of drug absorption in plasma concentration graph?\n\nOptions: \nA. Tmax and Cmax\nB. Area under the curve\nC. Tmax alone\nD. Cmax alone\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"In a plasma concentration-time curve, the absorption rate (how quickly drug enters systemic circulation) is reflected by both how soon and how high the peak occurs. Tmax directly indicates the time required to reach peak levels (shorter Tmax = faster absorption), while Cmax captures the magnitude influenced by that rate; together they therefore characterize absorption rate. By contrast, AUC alone quantifies the extent (total amount) absorbed, independent of speed.\n\nThus the correct choice is A.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":229,"output_tokens":99},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":9.53e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2290","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following is an example of placebo?\n\nOptions: \nA. Herbal medication with no known effect\nB. Physiotherapy\nC. Sham surgery\nD. Cognitive behavioral therapy\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"A placebo is a treatment that has no therapeutic effect, often used in clinical trials to compare against active treatments. Sham surgery mimics the procedure of real surgery without delivering the actual treatment, making it a classic example of a placebo in research settings. \n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":102,"output_tokens":55}},"cost":4.626e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2313","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The setting time of zinc phosphate may be retarded by?\n\nOptions: \nA. Increase in the ratio of powder to liquid\nB. Diluting the liquid with water\nC. Increase the addition of powder to liquid\nD. Decrease the addition of powder to liquid\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The setting reaction of zinc phosphate cement is an exothermic acid-base process whose rate is directly proportional to the powder-to-liquid (P/L) ratio. Consequently, lowering the P/L ratio (option D) reduces the number of reactive sites per unit volume and thereby lengthens the setting time. In contrast, raising the P/L ratio (A, C) accelerates setting, while diluting the liquid with water (B) supplies additional solvent that also shortens working time.\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":238,"output_tokens":97},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":9.61e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2342","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following best describes paradoxical suicide?\n\nOptions: \nA. Suicide after taking low dose of drug\nB. Suicide occurring at the time when the pt. stas to recover\nC. Suicidal tendency increase as the patient improves\nD. Accidental completion of suicide\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Paradoxical suicide refers to the counterintuitive phenomenon in which a depressed patient carries out suicide precisely as clinical improvement begins. This occurs because partial recovery restores the energy, motivation, and planning capacity needed to enact a suicidal plan before the underlying mood disturbance has fully resolved (classically observed early in antidepressant treatment).  \n\nOptions B and C both allude to this timing, but B most directly captures the definition of the completed act occurring at the moment recovery starts; C is a related but more general statement about risk trends.  \n\nThus the single best choice is B.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":241,"output_tokens":116},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":0.0001062,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2369","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The number of patients required in a clinical trial to treat a specify disease increases as\n\nOptions: \nA. The drop-out rate increases\nB. The significance level increases\nC. The size of the expected treatment effect increased\nD. The incidence of the disease decreases\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The required sample size \\(N\\) in a clinical trial is an increasing function of the anticipated dropout rate (to ensure the analyzed completer cohort still meets power targets) and a decreasing function of both \\(\\alpha\\) and the expected effect size. Consequently only option A produces a larger \\(N\\); B and C reduce it, while D primarily affects incidence or recruitment rates rather than the statistical sample-size formula itself.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":239,"output_tokens":86},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":9.080000000000001e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2463","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Saliva which is formed in salivary glands, when passes from salivary gland to duct orifices, it undergoes numerous ion exchanges and as a result\nsaliva become ____________ as compared to plasma:\n\nOptions: \nA. Hypertonic sometimes\nB. Hypotonic\nC. Isotonic\nD. Hypertonic always\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Saliva is initially isotonic to plasma in the acini of the salivary glands but becomes hypotonic as it passes through the ducts due to reabsorption of ions like Na⁺ and Cl⁻ while water is not reabsorbed as readily. This ion exchange results in saliva being hypotonic compared to plasma by the time it reaches the duct orifices.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":138,"output_tokens":83}},"cost":6.774e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2477","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following rightly describes the mechanism of \"Pressor Escape\" in SIADH?\n\nOptions: \nA. Characterized by sudden increase in urine volume with decrease in urine osmolality independent of circulating vasopressin levels.\nB. Characterized by sudden increase in urine volume with decrease in urine osmolality dependent of circulating vasopressin levels.\nC. Characterized by sudden decrease in urine volume with increase in urine osmolality independent of circulating vasopressin levels.\nD. Characterized by sudden decrease in urine volume with increase in urine osmolality dependent of circulating vasopressin levels.=\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Pressor escape in the context of SIADH refers to a phenomenon where, despite persistent high levels of vasopressin, the kidney eventually increases water excretion, leading to increased urine volume and decreased urine osmolality. This occurs independently of changes in circulating vasopressin levels, representing a physiological override of vasopressin's antidiuretic effect. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":190,"output_tokens":88}},"cost":7.75e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2513","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: When broad-spectrum antibiotics are administered with coumarin anticoagulants, the anticoagulant action may be:\n\nOptions: \nA. Reduced because of enhanced hepatic drug metabolism\nB. Reduced because of increased protein-binding\nC. Increased because of reduction of vitamin 'K' sources\nD. Increased because of decreased renal excretion of the anticoagulant\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Broad-spectrum antibiotics can reduce intestinal flora, which are responsible for synthesizing vitamin K. This reduction in vitamin K levels enhances the anticoagulant effect of coumarin derivatives, increasing the risk of bleeding. Therefore, the anticoagulant action is increased due to reduced vitamin K availability.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":141,"output_tokens":66}},"cost":5.793e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2671","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: One day after complete mouth extraction, blue black spots are seen on the neck of the patients. These spots indicate:\n\nOptions: \nA. Thrombocytopenic purpura\nB. Postoperative ecchymosis\nC. Impaired blood circulation\nD. Cellulitis\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The blue-black spots seen one day after complete mouth extraction are most likely due to bruising from surgical trauma, which is a common postoperative occurrence. This presentation aligns with postoperative ecchymosis, which results from blood leaking into tissues under the skin. \n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":124,"output_tokens":59}},"cost":5.152e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2692","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Excess of plasma level of lignocaine can cause cardiovascular collapse due to:\n\nOptions: \nA. Myocardial depression\nB. Vagal stimulation\nC. Syncope\nD. CN5 excitability\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Excess plasma levels of lignocaine (lidocaine) can lead to cardiovascular collapse primarily by depressing myocardial contractility. This local anesthetic acts on cardiac sodium channels, reducing cardiac excitability and conduction velocity. The most direct cause is myocardial depression.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":107,"output_tokens":60}},"cost":4.991e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2699","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Deepening the pulpal floor during cavity preparation\nprovides for\n\nOptions: \nA. Outline form\nB. Retention form\nC. convenience form\nD. Resistance form\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Deepening the pulpal floor during cavity preparation enhances the resistance form by providing better distribution of forces and preventing displacement of the restoration. This modification helps the tooth and restoration resist occlusal stresses. \n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":101,"output_tokens":46}},"cost":4.073e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2717","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The instrument shown in fig is used for\n\nOptions: \nA. Rapid separation\nB. Slow separation\nC. Not used for separation\nD. Depends on force for separation\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The question refers to an instrument (not shown here) whose most common function in standard lab MCQs is rapid separation of suspended particles or mixtures. This matches the operating principle of a centrifuge, which accelerates settling far beyond natural gravity and is therefore described as enabling \"rapid separation.\" Options B and C are inconsistent with this device, while D is only partially true but does not identify the instrument's primary intended use.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":221,"output_tokens":86},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":8.72e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2726","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Low apparent volume of distribution of drug indicates that:\n\nOptions: \nA. Drug has low half life\nB. Drug has low bioavailability\nC. Drug has low efficacy\nD. Drug is not extensively distributed to tissue\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"A low apparent volume of distribution indicates that the drug is primarily confined to the plasma or bloodstream and does not distribute widely into tissues. This suggests the drug is not extensively distributed to tissue. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":109,"output_tokens":50}},"cost":4.417e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2760","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Thiamine deficiency decreases cellular metabolism because:\n\nOptions: \nA. Thiamine is a coenzyme for pyruvate dehydrogenase and alfa-ketoglutarate dehydrogenases\nB. Activity of transketolase is inhibited\nC. It is required for the process of transamination\nD. It is a cofactor in oxidative reduction\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Thiamine (vitamin B1) is a crucial coenzyme for key enzymes in the citric acid cycle, specifically pyruvate dehydrogenase and alpha-ketoglutarate dehydrogenase. A deficiency in thiamine impairs these enzymes, leading to reduced ATP production and decreased cellular metabolism. This directly explains why option A is correct.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":140,"output_tokens":81}},"cost":6.68e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_276","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A temporary bridge constructed from a synthetic resin\n\nOptions: \nA. Is not required when the missing tooth is provided on a partial denture\nB. Should be cemented with a polycarboxylate cement to ensure retention between the preparation and fitting stages\nC. Should have the same buccal and lingual contours as the permanent bridge\nD. Should restore the occlusion to the same extent as the permanent bridge\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"A temporary bridge made of synthetic resin must maintain proper occlusion to prevent tooth movement and ensure patient comfort during the interim period. It should restore occlusion to the same extent as the permanent bridge to preserve vertical dimension and function. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":184,"output_tokens":80}},"cost":7.192e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1644","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: When length of a spring is doubled, the effect is:\n\nOptions: \nA. Doubled\nB. Four times\nC. Six times\nD. Eight times\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The question appears to refer to the elongation \\(\\Delta L\\) of a spring (or wire) obeying Hooke's law. From the definition of Young's modulus, \\(\\Delta L = FL/(AY)\\), so \\(\\Delta L\\) scales directly with the unstretched length \\(L\\). Doubling \\(L\\) therefore doubles the extension for fixed load, cross-section, and material.  \n\nNo other common spring-related quantity (stiffness, period, energy) produces an integer factor among the given options when length alone is doubled.  \n\nThus the correct choice is A.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":219,"output_tokens":115},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":0.0001013,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1513","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of following will happen with a flexible major connector:\n\nOptions: \nA. It will make other components more effective\nB. Will cause PDL destruction of abutment teeth\nC. Cause ill-fitting of RPD\nD. Will cause difficulty in occlusion\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"A major connector in an RPD must be rigid to transmit forces evenly across multiple abutments and soft-tissue areas. Flexibility allows independent movement of the prosthesis, concentrating torque and tipping forces on individual abutment teeth and thereby damaging their periodontal ligaments. This is a fundamental design principle stated in standard prosthodontic texts; the other listed effects are secondary or incorrect.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":237,"output_tokens":76},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":8.540000000000002e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2252","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If we know the value of one variable in an individual and wish to know the value of another variable, we calculate -\n\nOptions: \nA. Coefficient of correlation\nB. Coefficient of regression\nC. SE of mean\nD. Geometric mean\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"To predict the value of one variable based on the value of another, we use the coefficient of regression, as it quantifies the relationship between the variables in terms of how much the dependent variable changes per unit change in the independent variable. The coefficient of correlation measures the strength and direction of the linear relationship but does not directly provide predicted values. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":116,"output_tokens":81}},"cost":6.368e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1632","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In an animal model, the phenomenon of vasomotor reversal of dale can be demonstrated by:\n\nOptions: \nA. Stimulation of alpha-1 followed by stimulation of beta-2\nB. Block of alpha-1 followed by stimulation of beta-2\nC. Stimulation of alpha-1 followed by block of beta-2\nD. Stimulation of beta-1 receptor followed by block of beta-2 receptor\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Vasomotor reversal of Dale refers to the experimental observation that epinephrine normally raises blood pressure (via dominant \\(\\alpha_1\\)-mediated vasoconstriction) but, after \\(\\alpha_1\\) blockade, produces a fall in blood pressure (via unopposed \\(\\beta_2\\)-mediated vasodilation). This sequence is exactly the manipulation described in option B. The remaining choices either reverse the order of interventions or involve receptors (\\(\\beta_1\\)) that do not mediate vascular smooth-muscle tone.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":267,"output_tokens":104},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":0.0001054,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2019","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In case of addition silicones what should be done for better cast\n\nOptions: \nA. Apply ketone over tray\nB. Apply chloroform over tray\nC. Add flavouring agent to prevent bad odour\nD. Delay pouring of cast\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"For better cast when using addition silicones, pouring should be delayed to allow residual by-products to dissipate and to ensure complete polymerization, reducing the risk of distortion. Delaying the pour helps achieve a more accurate and stable impression. \n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":116,"output_tokens":54}},"cost":4.748e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2515","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a reaction substrate is available in a concentration that is l000times the Km value of the enzyme. After 9 minutes of reaction, l7o substrate is conveed to product (12 microgram/ml). If the concentration of the enzyme is changed to 1/3 and concentration of substrate is doubled. What is the time taken to conve the substrate into the same amount of product, i.e. I 2microgram/ml?\n\nOptions: \nA. 9 minutes\nB. 4.5 minutes\nC. 27 minutes\nD. 13.5 minutes\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Since \\([S] \\gg K_m\\) (specifically \\(1000 \\times K_m\\)), the reaction follows zero-order kinetics at a constant rate \\(V_{\\max}\\). The initial condition therefore yields the relation \\(12\\,\\mu\\mathrm{g/ml} = V_{\\max} \\times 9\\,\\mathrm{min}\\).  \n\nReducing enzyme concentration to one-third lowers the new rate to \\(V_{\\max}/3\\), while doubling substrate concentration keeps \\([S] \\gg K_m\\) and does not alter the zero-order regime. The time required to produce the same \\(12\\,\\mu\\mathrm{g/ml}\\) product is therefore \\(12/(V_{\\max}/3) = 27\\,\\mathrm{min}\\).  \n\nThus the correct choice is C.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":306,"output_tokens":156},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":0.0001392,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2757","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: X,Y,Z are the ee ions pet meaule..\\\\ and V=-30. If at resting membrane potential (RMP), when there is no net electro genic transfer, what is the value of Z?\n\nOptions: \nA. 20\nB. -20\nC. 80\nD. -80\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The question pertains to the condition of zero net current at RMP (\\(V = -30\\) mV). In the underlying balance equation (Goldman-Hodgkin-Katz or equivalent conductance-weighted sum of ionic currents), this occurs when the membrane voltage lies at the permeability-weighted average of the ionic equilibrium potentials.  \n\nGiven the numerical options and the conventional values assigned to the three equilibrium potentials in such problems, the only value consistent with a weighted mean of \\(-30\\) mV is the equilibrium potential of the dominant ion (normally potassium), i.e., \\(Z = -80\\) mV.  \n\nThus the correct choice is D.\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":250,"output_tokens":132},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":0.000116,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1333","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The systolic blood pressure in normal healthy males of age group of 40 — 60 has a normal distribution with a mean of 130 in a sample of 100. People with systolic blood pressure more than 130 will be:\n\nOptions: \nA. 100\nB. 75\nC. 50\nD. 25\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"In a normal distribution, the mean divides the data into two equal halves. Since the mean systolic blood pressure is 130, exactly 50% of the individuals will have a value above the mean. Therefore, in a sample of 100, 50 people will have systolic blood pressure more than 130.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":147,"output_tokens":78}},"cost":6.591e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2003","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Calculate net filtration pressure with the following data: PGC = 42 mm Hg pGC = 12 mm Hg PBC= 16 mm Hg Assume that no proteins were filtered.\n\nOptions: \nA. 34 mm Hg\nB. Data not sufficient\nC. 14 mm Hg\nD. 28 mm Hg\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The net filtration pressure (NFP) is calculated as: NFP = (PGC - PBC) - πGC, where PGC is glomerular capillary hydrostatic pressure, PBC is Bowman’s capsule hydrostatic pressure, and πGC is the glomerular capillary oncotic pressure. Given PGC = 42 mm Hg, PBC = 16 mm Hg, and πGC = 12 mm Hg, we get: NFP = (42 - 16) - 12 = 14 mm Hg. Since no proteins are filtered, the oncotic pressure in Bowman’s capsule is negligible.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":135,"output_tokens":113}},"cost":8.534999999999999e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1404","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Treatment of choice for erythrodermic psoriasis:\n\nOptions: \nA. Methotrexate\nB. Coicosteroids\nC. Coal tar topical\nD. Topical steroids\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Erythrodermic psoriasis is a severe, widespread variant requiring systemic therapy rather than topicals (eliminating C and D). Systemic corticosteroids are contraindicated due to risk of rebound flare or conversion to pustular psoriasis (eliminating B). Methotrexate is a well-established first-line systemic agent for this indication, supported by dermatology guidelines.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":220,"output_tokens":72},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":7.999999999999999e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1791","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Increase in the residual mercury in silver amalgam filling can:\n\nOptions: \nA. Cause fracture of the filling\nB. Tarnish and corrosion\nC. Increase the strength\nD. Decrease condensation pressure\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Excess residual mercury in set amalgam directly reduces the proportion of the \\(\\gamma\\) phase while increasing the \\(\\gamma_2\\) phase, which is both weaker and far more susceptible to electrochemical corrosion. Consequently, surface tarnish, marginal degradation, and corrosion are the most immediate and consistently reported sequelae. Options A and C are secondary or opposite effects, while D has no mechanistic link to residual mercury once the restoration has been placed.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":225,"output_tokens":88},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":8.9e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2072","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Treatment of simple endometrial hyperplasia with atypia in 45 yr female:\n\nOptions: \nA. Hysterectomy\nB. Progestin\nC. Mirena\nD. Postmenopausal women\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Simple endometrial hyperplasia with atypia is considered a precancerous condition and carries a significant risk of progression to endometrial cancer, especially in a 45-year-old woman who is likely perimenopausal. While progestin therapy (option B) or Mirena (option C) may be used in certain cases, particularly for fertility-sparing management, the presence of atypia generally warrants definitive treatment. Therefore, hysterectomy (option A) is the most appropriate and recommended treatment for atypical hyperplasia in a woman who has completed childbearing.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":112,"output_tokens":126}},"cost":9.015999999999999e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_94","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The number of dental caries cases reported during last 10 years are given below 250, 320, 190, 300, 5000, 100, 260, 350, 320 and 160. The epidemiologist wants to find out average number of caries cases reported in that town for last 10 yrs. The most appropriate average per this data will be\n\nOptions: \nA. Arithmetic mean\nB. Mode\nC. Median\nD. Geometric mean\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The data contain a clear outlier (5000) that is an order of magnitude larger than the remaining nine values. The arithmetic mean is therefore pulled upward and no longer represents a typical year, whereas the median is unaffected by extreme values and supplies a robust central measure. Consequently the epidemiologist should report the median.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":283,"output_tokens":66},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":8.96e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_849","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Insufficient closure of the flasks during packing of denture base resin can result in:\n\nOptions: \nA. Poor colour stability\nB. Less polymerization shrinkage\nC. Increase in vertical dimension\nD. Decrease in vertical dimension\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Insufficient flask closure during denture-base packing leaves excess resin (flash) that prevents the flask halves from meeting completely. This excess thickness directly increases the occlusal vertical dimension once the processed denture is placed in the mouth. The other listed effects (color instability, altered shrinkage) are governed by curing cycles or material formulation, not flask closure.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":229,"output_tokens":73},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":8.23e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1701","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: For testing the statistical significance of the difference in heights of school children among three socio economic groups the most appropriate statistical test is:\n\nOptions: \nA. Student's 't' test\nB. Chi-squared test\nC. Paired 't' test\nD. One way analysis of variance (one way ANOVA)\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The most appropriate test for comparing the means of three or more groups, such as height across three socioeconomic groups, is one way ANOVA. This test determines whether there are any statistically significant differences between the means of the groups. The t-tests are only for two groups, and the chi-squared test is for categorical data, not continuous like height.\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":154,"output_tokens":97}},"cost":7.821999999999999e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1848","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: For testing the statistical significance of the difference in heights of school children -\n\nOptions: \nA. Student's t test\nB. chi-square test\nC. Paired 't' test\nD. ANOVA\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The appropriate test for comparing the difference in heights between groups of school children is the Student's t-test, especially if comparing two groups. This test is designed for continuous data (like height) and assesses whether the means of two groups are statistically different. If more than two groups were involved, ANOVA would be preferred, but for a general comparison of two groups, the t-test is most suitable.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":108,"output_tokens":88}},"cost":6.684e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2441","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The most appropriate method of testing the statistical significance of the differences between means of two groups is\n\nOptions: \nA. Chi square test\nB. Multiple regression analysis\nC. Correlation coefficient analysis\nD. Student test\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The most appropriate method for testing the statistical significance of the differences between the means of two groups is the Student's t-test. This test is specifically designed to compare the means of two samples to determine if they are significantly different. \n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":109,"output_tokens":51}},"cost":4.477e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_585","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Birth weight of a baby can be increased by:\n\nOptions: \nA. Cessation of smoking\nB. Aspirin\nC. Ca++  and vitamin D supplement\nD. Bed rest\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The birth weight of a baby can be positively influenced by the mother ceasing smoking during pregnancy, as smoking is a known cause of low birth weight. Smoking reduces oxygen and nutrient delivery to the fetus, and stopping can improve fetal growth. Therefore, the most effective option among those listed is cessation of smoking.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":105,"output_tokens":66}},"cost":5.325e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2323","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 10-year boy with dog bite unprovoked comes to you. Appropriate action is:\n\nOptions: \nA. Give cell culture derived vaccine\nB. Withhold vaccine and observe dog for 10 days\nC. Kill dog and send brain for biopsy\nD. No fuher action is necessary\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The question specifies an unprovoked dog bite, which is a key indicator of possible rabies in the animal per standard guidelines (e.g., WHO or Indian National guidelines). This warrants immediate initiation of post-exposure prophylaxis with a modern cell-culture rabies vaccine rather than simple observation. Options B and C apply to different scenarios (provoked bites or confirmed rabid/suspect animals that can be captured and tested), while D is inappropriate for any bite exposure.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":246,"output_tokens":94},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":9.620000000000001e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_472","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Acetyl choline release can be increased from presynaptic membrane by:\n\nOptions: \nA. Blocking voltage gated Na+ channels on presynaptic membrane\nB. Blocking voltage gated Ca+ channels on presynaptic membrane\nC. Blocking voltage gated K+ channels on presynaptic membrane\nD. Blocking voltage gated CI- channels on presynaptic membrane\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Acetylcholine release is dependent on calcium influx through voltage-gated Ca²⁺ channels in the presynaptic membrane, which triggers vesicle fusion. Blocking voltage-gated K⁺ channels prolongs the action potential, leading to increased Ca²⁺ influx and thus enhanced neurotransmitter release. Therefore, blocking K⁺ channels increases acetylcholine release.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":137,"output_tokens":77}},"cost":6.401e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1452","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An investigator want to know the similarity of the mean peak flow of expiratory rates and non-smokers, light smokers, moderate smokers, & heavy smokers. Which is statistical test of significance:\n\nOptions: \nA. One way ANOVA\nB. Two way ANOVA\nC. Student-t test\nD. Chi square test\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The investigator is comparing the means of one continuous variable (peak expiratory flow rate) across four independent groups (non-smokers, light smokers, moderate smokers, heavy smokers). This scenario requires a test that can compare more than two group means, which is best handled by one-way ANOVA. The other tests are not appropriate: two-way ANOVA involves two independent variables, t-test is for two groups, and chi-square is for categorical data.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":133,"output_tokens":98}},"cost":7.609e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2595","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a group of 100 people, the average GFR is 85 ml/ min with a standard detion of 25. What is the range for 90% confidence interval?\n\nOptions: \nA. 81-89\nB. 80-90\nC. 75-95\nD. 70-100\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The 90% CI for the sample mean is given by \\(\\bar{x} \\pm z \\cdot (\\text{SD}/\\sqrt{n})\\). With \\(n=100\\), \\(\\text{SE}=2.5\\); the appropriate \\(z\\)-value is \\(\\approx 1.645\\) (or the common rounding 1.6), so the margin of error is \\(\\approx 4\\). This yields the interval 81–89, matching option A (while B corresponds to the wider 95% interval).\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":252,"output_tokens":109},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":0.0001049,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_441","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If 2 Implants of size 4 mm are to be placed in a ridge, what should be the minimum width required in the ridge\n\nOptions: \nA. 14 mm\nB. 15 mm\nC. 17 mm\nD. 18 mm\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"To place two dental implants of 4 mm diameter, a minimum of 3 mm of inter-implant bone is typically recommended. Each implant requires 1 mm of bone on each side, so the total width needed is: 4 mm (first implant) + 3 mm (inter-implant bone) + 4 mm (second implant) = 11 mm. However, considering additional safety margins and clinical best practices, the accepted minimum is often higher.\n\nThe most appropriate answer based on standard guidelines is:\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":123,"output_tokens":112}},"cost":8.319000000000001e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2384","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A pregnant lady develops chickenpox. During which part of her pregnancy will it lead to highest chance of neonatal infection:\n\nOptions: \nA. Last 5 days\nB. 12-16 week\nC. 8-12 week\nD. 16-20 week\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The highest risk of neonatal infection from maternal chickenpox occurs when the mother develops varicella shortly before or after delivery. If the mother gets chickenpox within the last 5 days of pregnancy or within 2 days postpartum, the newborn is at greatest risk because the virus can be transmitted perinatally before the infant receives maternal antibodies. This can lead to severe neonatal varicella.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":127,"output_tokens":90}},"cost":7.051e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2048","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The occlusal clearance of an onlay is best detected by:\n\nOptions: \nA. Depth cuts\nB. Visual inspection\nC. Wax chew-in\nD. Articulating paper\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The occlusal clearance of an onlay is best evaluated by observing contacts during function and at the intended occlusal plane. Articulating paper helps identify premature contacts and areas of insufficient clearance by marking contact points between the restoration and opposing teeth. Therefore, the most accurate method among the options is using articulating paper.\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":103,"output_tokens":70}},"cost":5.5389999999999997e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2646","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: ECG with \"mean\" axis of 90deg. In which lead there would be the maximum voltage of R wave?\n\nOptions: \nA. III\nB. I\nC. aVF\nD. aVL\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The mean electrical axis of 90 degrees points directly downward, along the positive direction of the inferior leads. Among the options, lead aVF is oriented at +90 degrees, which aligns perfectly with this axis. Therefore, the R wave will have the maximum amplitude in lead aVF.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":110,"output_tokens":66}},"cost":5.39e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1317","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: ECG shows a mean axis of 90 degrees. In which of the following would be present the maximum voltage of R wave?\n\nOptions: \nA. III\nB. I\nC. aVF\nD. aVL\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The QRS axis indicates the mean direction of ventricular depolarization in the frontal plane. At a mean QRS axis of exactly +90°, this direction aligns perfectly with the orientation of lead aVF (which is also positioned at +90°). As a result, the projection (and thus R-wave amplitude) is maximal in aVF and comparatively smaller in the other listed leads, whose orientations deviate from +90° (lead III at +120°, lead I at 0°, lead aVL at –30°).\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":230,"output_tokens":105},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":9.850000000000001e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1705","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Among a 100 women with average Hb of 10 gm%, the standard deviation was 1, what is the standard error?\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.01\nB. 0.1\nC. 1\nD. 10\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Standard error of the mean is computed as \\(\\text{SD}/\\sqrt{n}\\). Substituting the given values yields \\(1/\\sqrt{100}=0.1\\). The supplied mean is irrelevant to this calculation.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":237,"output_tokens":46},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":7.04e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1553","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An investigator wants to study the association between maternal intake of iron supplements (Yes or No) and birth weights (in gm) of new born babies. He collects relevant data from 100 pregnant women and their newborns. What statistical test of hypothesis would you advise for the investigator in this situation?\n\nOptions: \nA. Chi-square test\nB. Unpaired or independent t - test\nC. Analysis of variance\nD. Student t — test\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The investigator is comparing the mean birth weights (a continuous variable) between two independent groups (mothers who took iron supplements vs. those who did not). The appropriate test for comparing means between two independent groups is the unpaired (independent) t-test. \n\nChi-square is for categorical outcomes, ANOVA is for more than two groups, and \"Student t-test\" typically refers to paired or one-sample tests, though sometimes used interchangeably; however, \"unpaired t-test\" is more precise here.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":156,"output_tokens":110}},"cost":8.628000000000001e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1587","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the angle subtended by the largest letter in the Snellen cha on a person's eye who is reading it from a distance of 6 meters?\n\nOptions: \nA. 1 minute\nB. 10 minutes\nC. 50 minutes\nD. 60 minutes\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The Snellen chart is constructed such that each letter's overall height subtends an angle of 5 arcminutes at the nominal testing distance, with individual strokes subtending 1 arcminute. Standard charts begin with the 6/60 optotype (the largest letter), which is sized exactly ten times larger than the 6/6 optotype. Consequently, at the conventional 6 m viewing distance this letter subtends 50 arcminutes.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":242,"output_tokens":93},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":9.49e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2338","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Height of group of 20 boys aged 10 years was 140 ± 13 cm and 20 girls of same age was 135 cm ± 7 cm. To test the statistical significance of difference in height, test applicable is -\n\nOptions: \nA. X2\nB. Z\nC. t\nD. F\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The appropriate test to compare the means of two independent groups with quantitative data (height) and small sample sizes is the t-test. Since the sample sizes are small (n = 20 each) and population variances are unknown, the t-test is more suitable than the Z-test. \n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":139,"output_tokens":65}},"cost":5.707e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_531","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Craters in interseptal bone are best eliminated by\n\nOptions: \nA. Gingivectomy\nB. Supragingival curettage\nC. Interseptal massage with stimulators\nD. Osseous recontouring\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Craters in the interseptal bone are bony defects that require surgical reshaping for proper elimination and periodontal health. Gingivectomy and supragingival curettage address soft tissue and supragingival calculus, not bony defects. Osseous recontouring is the procedure specifically designed to reshape and smooth irregular bone contours, including craters.\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":116,"output_tokens":83}},"cost":6.488e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2029","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The concentration of a negative ion is 100 mMoUL extracellular and 10 mMo1/1 intracellular. What will be the Nernst potential for this ion?\n\nOptions: \nA. --10 mV\nB. +10 mV\nC. --61 mV\nD. +61 mV\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The Nernst equation for equilibrium potential (at mammalian body temperature) is given by  \n\\[E = \\frac{61}{z}\\log_{10}\\Bigl(\\frac{[\\text{ion}]_\\text{out}}{[\\text{ion}]_\\text{in}}\\Bigr)\\ \\text{mV},\\]  \nwhere \\(z\\) is the signed valence of the ion.  \n\nFor the anion in question \\(z=-1\\), \\([\\text{out}]=100\\) mM and \\([\\text{in}]=10\\) mM, so  \n\\[E = \\frac{61}{-1}\\log_{10}(10) = -61\\ \\text{mV}.\\]  \n\nThus the correct choice is C.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":250,"output_tokens":152},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":0.000126,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_589","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Rearrange the sequence of hand washing: a. b. c. d.\n\nOptions: \nA. a,c,d,b\nB. b,c,a,d\nC. d,a,c,b\nD. c,a,b,d\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The provided question lacks any description or definition of the hand-washing steps labeled a–d, so no logical rearrangement can be determined from the given options. Without that missing context, the query is unanswerable on its merits.\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":231,"output_tokens":50},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":7.120000000000001e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1941","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 28 year old eclamptic woman develop convulsions.The first measure to be done is:\n\nOptions: \nA. Give MgSO4\nB. Sedation of patient\nC. Immediate delivery\nD. Care of airway\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The first priority in managing an eclamptic woman with convulsions is ensuring a patent airway and adequate oxygenation to prevent hypoxia for both mother and fetus. While MgSO4 is the drug of choice to prevent further seizures, securing the airway comes first. Immediate interventions must focus on basic life support principles.\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":114,"output_tokens":71}},"cost":5.742e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1663","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: After a building collapse, among remnants, a person's length of humerus is 24.5 cm. What is the predicted height of this person?\n\nOptions: \nA. 90 cm\nB. 110 cm\nC. 130 cm\nD. 146 cm\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The length of the humerus can be used to estimate a person's height using regression formulas. For adult males, height (in cm) is approximately calculated as: height = (2.89 × humerus length) + 70.64. Plugging in 24.5 cm gives: (2.89 × 24.5) + 70.64 ≈ 141.5 cm, which is closest to 146 cm.\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":129,"output_tokens":109}},"cost":8.217e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_787","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Digoxin is obtained from a plant product and has a half-life of 36 hours. How does this information help us in formulating treatment?\n\nOptions: \nA. To adjust maintenance dose of digoxin required to keep the blood levels within therapeutic range\nB. Intravenous administration in emergency and urgent dosing\nC. Long half-life permits altemate day dosing\nD. It requires a high loading dose to be administered\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The long half-life of digoxin (∼36 h) means that steady-state plasma levels are not reached for 5–7 days with repeated dosing alone; a loading (digitalizing) dose is therefore administered to rapidly achieve therapeutic concentrations. This is a direct pharmacokinetic consequence of the reported half-life and is standard clinical practice for digoxin. The remaining options either address unrelated parameters (maintenance-dose adjustment depends on clearance, not half-life) or are factually incorrect (alternate-day dosing is not used; route of administration is independent of half-life).\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":267,"output_tokens":113},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":0.0001099,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1834","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Arch length analysis of a dentition shows a discrepancy of more than 10 mm. This indicates:\n\nOptions: \nA. No extraction required if treated at an early age\nB. No extraction required\nC. Extraction of posterior teeth\nD. Proximal stripping\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Arch length discrepancy (ALD) measures crowding/spacing by comparing available arch perimeter to the sum of tooth widths. An ALD >10 mm constitutes severe crowding that cannot be resolved by non-extraction approaches such as proximal stripping (typically limited to 2–4 mm) or simple alignment; therefore extraction of teeth (commonly first premolars) is required to obtain the necessary space. Option C directly identifies this extraction need, whereas A/B imply a non-extraction plan and D addresses only minimal discrepancies.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":238,"output_tokens":104},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":9.96e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_148","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A patient is administered 200 mg of a drug. 75 mg of the drug is eliminated from the body in 90 minutes. If the drug follows first order kinetics, how much drug will remain after 6 hours?\n\nOptions: \nA. 12.5 mg\nB. 25 mg\nC. 30 mg\nD. 50 mg\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"After 90 minutes, 75 mg is eliminated from 200 mg, leaving 125 mg. This represents one half-life because 200 → 125 is a 37.5% reduction, but more precisely, first-order kinetics implies exponential decay. However, 125/200 = 0.625, not 0.5, so 90 minutes is not a half-life. Instead, using the elimination rate: fraction remaining = 125/200 = 0.625 over 1.5 hours. Over 6 hours (4 intervals of 1.5 hours), amount remaining = 200 × (0.625)^4 ≈ 200 × 0.152 ≈ 30.4 mg, closest to 30 mg.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":145,"output_tokens":193}},"cost":0.00013465,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2812","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A study is to be conducted with regards to the fat content in the expressed breast milk of pre-term infants as compared to term infants. Which study design is best suited?\n\nOptions: \nA. Case control\nB. Prospective coho\nC. Longitudinal study\nD. Ambispective\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The best study design to compare fat content in expressed breast milk between pre-term and term infants is a prospective cohort study, as it allows for direct observation and comparison over time from a defined starting point. This design minimizes recall bias and enables accurate measurement of fat content in breast milk as it happens. \n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":125,"output_tokens":67}},"cost":5.644999999999999e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_643","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Failure of partial dentures due to poor clasp design can best be avoided by:\n\nOptions: \nA. Using stress breakers\nB. Using bar type clasps\nC. Altering tooth contours\nD. Clasping only those teeth with fairly long crowns and normal bone support\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Poor clasp design in partial dentures often leads to instability or damage to abutment teeth, especially when teeth lack adequate support or proper morphology. Clasps should ideally engage teeth that have sufficient crown length and periodontal support to withstand functional stresses. Therefore, selecting teeth with favorable anatomy and support helps prevent failure.\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":123,"output_tokens":70}},"cost":5.799e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2000","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which is the most preferred route for drug administration in the management of chronic pain\n\nOptions: \nA. Intrathecal\nB. Oral\nC. Subdermal\nD. Intravenous\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The most preferred route for drug administration in the management of chronic pain is oral, as it is non-invasive, convenient, and allows for good patient compliance over long periods. While intrathecal or intravenous routes may be used for severe or refractory pain, they are typically reserved for specific cases due to their invasiveness and higher risk. Oral administration is generally the first-line approach in chronic pain management.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":103,"output_tokens":89}},"cost":6.679e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_985","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Most accurate and safe method to diagnose ble pregnancy at 6weeks-\n\nOptions: \nA. Doppler assessment of fetal cardiac activity\nB. USG for fetal cardiac activity\nC. Urinary Beta-hCG determination\nD. Per vaginal examination of uterine size corresponding to 6 weeks gestation\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The most accurate and safe method to diagnose a viable pregnancy at 6 weeks is visualization of fetal cardiac activity via ultrasound. Transvaginal ultrasound can reliably detect fetal heart motion at this gestational age, providing definitive evidence of a live embryo. Doppler assessment is less sensitive at this early stage, while beta-hCG and uterine size are supportive but not confirmatory.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":126,"output_tokens":81}},"cost":6.498e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_473","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a JubLeitter arca pith crude bih rate of 211, what would be the expected number of ANC registrations?\n\nOptions: \nA. 60\nB. 80\nC. 100\nD. 120\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The query text appears to contain multiple typographical corruptions (e.g., “JubLeitter arca,” “bih rate”), but the only recognizable public-health relationship is that expected ANC registrations are conventionally estimated from crude birth rate (typically expressed per 1 000 population). With the supplied figure of 211 (most plausibly interpreted as CBR = 21.1) and no other numeric inputs given, the round-number target that aligns with standard program-planning benchmarks is 100.  \n\nThus the most defensible selection among the listed choices is C.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":233,"output_tokens":117},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":0.0001051,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_751","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A child has received full Rabies vaccination in December 2018 and now presented with oozing wound on Great toe and the pet had vaccination also. Next line of management is\n\nOptions: \nA. No vaccine required\nB. RIG + 5 doses of vaccine\nC. 5 doses of vaccines only\nD. 2 doses of Rabies vaccine\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The scenario involves a category III exposure (oozing wound) in a previously vaccinated patient. Per WHO and national rabies guidelines, re-exposure management in such individuals consists of two booster doses (days 0 and 3) without RIG, irrespective of the animal’s vaccination status. Therefore the indicated choice is D.\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":259,"output_tokens":67},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":8.530000000000001e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2178","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What should be the time of termination of pregnancy of a female with insulin dependent diabetes?\n\nOptions: \nA. 40 weeks\nB. 38 weeks\nC. 37 weeks\nD. 34 weeks\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"For women with insulin-dependent diabetes, elective termination of pregnancy is typically recommended at 38–39 weeks gestation to reduce the risk of stillbirth and complications, while avoiding earlier delivery unless indicated. Among the given options, 38 weeks is the most appropriate and widely accepted timing. \n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":111,"output_tokens":66}},"cost":5.4029999999999996e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2727","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Hormone Replacement therapy is not indicated in:\n\nOptions: \nA. Hot flashes\nB. Prevention of CAD\nC. Osteoporosis\nD. Vaginal atrophy\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Hormone Replacement Therapy (HRT) is commonly used to manage symptoms of menopause such as hot flashes, vaginal atrophy, and to prevent osteoporosis. However, it is not indicated for the prevention of coronary artery disease (CAD), as studies like the Women's Health Initiative have shown that HRT does not reduce CAD risk and may even increase cardiovascular events. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":101,"output_tokens":87}},"cost":6.533e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1829","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Sorting a patient of trauma of head injury on basis of need of care and availability of resources\n\nOptions: \nA. Triage\nB. Emergency care\nC. Definitive care\nD. Hospital care\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The process of sorting patients based on the severity of their condition and the availability of medical resources is known as triage. In head trauma, this helps prioritize who needs immediate attention versus those who can wait. \n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":107,"output_tokens":48}},"cost":4.271e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2308","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 27 year primigravida presents with pregnancy induced hypertension with blood pressure of 150/100 mm of Hg at 32 weeks of gestation with no other complications. Subsequently, her blood pressure is controlled on treatment. If there are no complications, the pregnancy should be terminated at:\n\nOptions: \nA. 40 completed weeks\nB. 37 completed weeks\nC. 35 completed weeks\nD. 34 completed weeks\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The case involves gestational hypertension (formerly PIH) diagnosed at 32 weeks with BP in the non-severe range (150/100 mm Hg) that remains controlled without proteinuria, end-organ effects, or other complications. Current ACOG and RCOG guidelines therefore allow expectant management until 37 0/7 weeks, at which point delivery is indicated to avoid progression to preeclampsia while minimizing risks of late-preterm birth. Earlier delivery (options C or D) is reserved for severe-range hypertension or superimposed complications; delivery at term (option A) is not appropriate once the 37-week threshold is reached.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":273,"output_tokens":126},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":0.0001176,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_554","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A drug X was given continuous intravenous infusion at 1.6 mg/min. The clearance of the drug is 640 mL/min. With a half-life of 1.8 hours, what would be the steady state plasma concentration of drug?\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.002 mg/mL\nB. 0.004 trig/mL\nC. 2.88 mg/mL\nD. 3.55 mg/mL\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The steady-state plasma concentration (C_ss) during a continuous IV infusion is given by the formula: C_ss = Rate of infusion / Clearance.  \nHere, the infusion rate is 1.6 mg/min and clearance is 640 mL/min (or 0.64 L/min), so C_ss = 1.6 / 640 = 0.0025 mg/mL, which is closest to 0.002 mg/mL.  \nNote that option B contains a typo (\"trig/mL\"), making it invalid.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":160,"output_tokens":121}},"cost":9.34e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1612","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If the distribution of intraocular pressure (IOP) seen in 100 glaucoma patients has an average 30 mm with an SD of 1, what is the lower limit of the average that can be expected 95% of times -\n\nOptions: \nA. 28\nB. 26\nC. 32\nD. 25\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The question pertains to the range of values expected to cover 95% of observations from a distribution (poorly worded in the source, but this is the standard interpretation of such MCQs). With a reported mean of 30 and SD of 1, the elementary formula for the 95% limits on the data is therefore mean \\(\\pm\\) 2 SD. This immediately yields the lower bound \\(30-2=28\\).\n\n(The sample size of 100 is irrelevant to this calculation and functions only as a distractor; the SEM-based 95% CI around the mean would be far narrower and is not what the phrasing “95% of times” denotes.)\n\nThus the matching choice is A.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":253,"output_tokens":145},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":0.0001231,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1539","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: CLED media better than Macconkey media\n\nOptions: \nA. It stimulates growth of Staph and Candida as it is non selective\nB. Inhibits swarming of proteus\nC. Differentiates between Lactose fermenter and non-lactose fermenters\nD. Sodium taurocholate is used as selective agent.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"CLED (Cystine Lactose Electrolyte Deficient) media is specifically designed to prevent the swarming of *Proteus* species, which can otherwise overgrow and interfere with the isolation of other urinary pathogens. Unlike MacConkey agar, which supports swarming, CLED inhibits this phenomenon without being overly selective. This makes it superior for urine culture, particularly for accurate colony counting.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":135,"output_tokens":88}},"cost":7.035e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_605","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Sending the parents outside the operatory and threatening the child that they won't be back until he stops crying-is an example of which of the following behavior management techniques:\n\nOptions: \nA. Omission\nB. Negative reinforcement\nC. Positive reinforcement\nD. Modelling\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The described technique involves removing the parents (a stimulus) to increase the likelihood of the desired behavior (stopping crying), which aligns with negative reinforcement—where an aversive or unpleasant condition is removed to reinforce behavior.\n\nThis is not omission (which involves withholding a reward), positive reinforcement (adding a desirable stimulus), or modelling (demonstrating behavior for imitation).\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":119,"output_tokens":79}},"cost":6.287e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1016","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which is not an obvious advantage of high pressure oxygen through cannula:\n\nOptions: \nA. Bypassing nasopharyngeal dead space\nB. Decreases need for intubation\nC. PEEP\nD. Hot and Humidification of air\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"High pressure oxygen via nasal cannula, such as high-flow nasal cannula (HFNC), provides several benefits including dead space washout, some degree of PEEP, and improved comfort with humidification. However, \"hot and humidification of air\" is not an inherent *advantage* in terms of physiological outcome like the others—it's a feature to improve tolerance, not a direct therapeutic benefit. The most accurate answer reflecting a non-obvious or less direct advantage is therefore D.\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":118,"output_tokens":104}},"cost":7.774e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2209","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The logical explanation for the unique anticariogenic property of most silicate cements is:\n\nOptions: \nA. The reduction in enamel solubility due to fluoride uptake by enamel\nB. That beryllium flux is used in silicates\nC. That silicates show very little leakage at the margins of the restoration\nD. Due to the high silica content\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The anticariogenic property of silicate cements is primarily attributed to the release of fluoride, which is taken up by the surrounding tooth structure, thereby reducing enamel solubility and increasing resistance to caries. Option A correctly identifies this mechanism. The other options are either irrelevant (B, D) or not directly related to anticariogenic effects (C).\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":139,"output_tokens":77}},"cost":6.427e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1198","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following is not a function of guiding plane?\n\nOptions: \nA. Provide one path of insertion and removal of the restoration\nB. Provide stabilizing characteristics against horizontal rotation of denture\nC. Eliminate detrimental strain to abutment teeth during placing or removing restoration\nD. Engage the abutment tooth in such a manner as to resist displacement of restoration away from basal seat\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The guiding plane helps control the path of insertion and removal, enhances denture stability, and reduces strain on abutment teeth during placement or removal. However, resisting displacement of the restoration away from the basal seat is primarily the function of a retentive clasp, not the guiding plane. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":145,"output_tokens":71}},"cost":6.145e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1809","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Stress breakers are not used in partial denture construction because:\n\nOptions: \nA. They are expensive\nB. Increase the vertical dimension\nC. They are difficult to design and fabricate\nD. Harmful effect on the abutment\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Stress breakers are not used in partial denture construction because they can transmit harmful, uncontrolled forces to the abutment teeth, potentially causing damage or loosening. Modern prosthodontic principles favor stress-distributing designs rather than stress-breaking mechanisms to protect abutment teeth. The correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":114,"output_tokens":70}},"cost":5.682e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_877","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: When it is made up of same steel, size 55, which will be more prone to fracture:\n\nOptions: \nA. Triangular reamer\nB. Rhomboid cross section file\nC. Square cross section file\nD. Headstrom file\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Endodontic instruments of identical size and material differ in fracture susceptibility primarily due to cross-sectional design and manufacturing method. Triangular (reamer) and square/rhomboid (K-type file) geometries retain a relatively robust central core, distributing torsional and flexural stresses evenly. In contrast, the Hedstrom (H-type) file is machined from a round blank, producing deep flutes with sharp internal angles and minimal core thickness; these act as stress concentrators, markedly lowering resistance to cyclic fatigue and torsional failure.\n\nThus the most fracture-prone instrument is the Hedstrom file.\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":237,"output_tokens":118},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":0.00010640000000000001,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1841","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Repeated fracture of a porcelain fused to metal restoration is primarily due to\n\nOptions: \nA. Occlusal trauma\nB. Inadequately designed framework\nC. Improper firing schedule\nD. Failure to use metal conditioner\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Repeated fracture of a porcelain fused to metal restoration is most commonly due to an inadequately designed framework, which fails to properly support the porcelain under functional loads. A weak or improper framework design can lead to flexing and stress concentration, promoting porcelain fracture. \n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":112,"output_tokens":57}},"cost":4.876e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1446","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Sequential arrangement question on JVP. Staing with \"a\" wave. A-First hea sound B-T wave C-R wave D-Rapid ejection phase\n\nOptions: \nA. A,B,C,D\nB. A,C,D,B\nC. C,A,D,B\nD. D,C,B,A\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The \"a\" wave of the jugular venous pressure (JVP) corresponds to atrial contraction, which occurs just before the first heart sound (S1). S1 coincides with the R wave on the ECG, followed by the rapid ejection phase of ventricular systole. The T wave occurs last, representing ventricular repolarization.\n\nThus, the correct sequence is: a wave → first heart sound (A) → R wave (C) → rapid ejection phase (D) → T wave (B).\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":128,"output_tokens":115}},"cost":8.564e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1914","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A properly designed rest on lingual surface of a canine is preferred to a rest on incisal surface because:\n\nOptions: \nA. Less Leverage is exerted against the tooth by Lingual rest\nB. Enamel is thicker on lingual surface\nC. Visibility and access is better on lingual surface\nD. The cingulum of canine produces a naturalsurface for recess\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"A lingual rest on a canine is preferred because the cingulum provides a natural, strong area for rest placement, allowing for a more favorable distribution of forces and minimizing stress on the tooth. This design takes advantage of the tooth's anatomy, reducing the risk of fracture or displacement. The incisal edge, in contrast, is more prone to damage and does not offer the same structural support.\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":144,"output_tokens":85}},"cost":6.972e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_777","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a village, despite of health education for oral cancer, people don't follow instructions even after referral with persuasive reminders, people are still reluctant. It best fits under which model:\n\nOptions: \nA. Trans-theoretical model\nB. Health belief model\nC. Social compliance\nD. Public health model\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The scenario describes individuals who are aware of the risks and have been encouraged to act but still fail to change their behavior, which aligns with the Health Belief Model's focus on perceived barriers, benefits, and susceptibility influencing health actions. Despite education and reminders, the lack of action suggests that personal beliefs about the disease and prevention are not aligned with taking action. This is best explained by the Health Belief Model.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":126,"output_tokens":88}},"cost":6.918e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_208","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following does not require 5'capping?\n\nOptions: \nA. tRNA of alanine\nB. mRNA for histone\nC. U6 snRNA\nD. siRNA\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The 5' cap is typically added to RNA polymerase II transcripts, such as mRNA and most snRNAs, but not to all small RNAs. U6 snRNA is transcribed by RNA polymerase III and has a gamma-monomethyl cap, not the standard 7-methylguanosine cap. However, siRNA and tRNAs do not undergo 5' capping at all, but among the options, tRNA of alanine is clearly processed without any capping.\n\nU6 snRNA (option C) is known to have a different capping mechanism, but siRNA (option D) is double-stranded and does not receive a 5' cap. Still, the most accurate answer is that tRNA is never capped, but the question may target U6 snRNA as an exception to standard capping.\n\nActually, siRNA is not capped and is processed from Dicer cleavage, lacking 5' capping entirely. Among these, siRNA definitively does not require 5' capping.\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":106,"output_tokens":217}},"cost":0.00014398,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_326","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: When a dentist says that \" I cannot fix your teeth if you do not open your mouth wide:\" He is employing:\n\nOptions: \nA. Problem ownership.\nB. Voice control\nC. Tolerance.\nD. Flexibility.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The quoted statement is a classic example of problem ownership in pediatric dentistry behavior guidance: the dentist uses an \"I-message\" to place responsibility for cooperation on the child, thereby motivating the child to open wider so treatment can proceed.  \n\nThis differs from voice control (which relies on altered tone/volume rather than the semantic content of the message) and has no relation to the vague notions of tolerance or flexibility.  \n\nThus the correct choice is A.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":229,"output_tokens":93},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":9.23e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_298","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following is having Maximum buffering capacity\n\nOptions: \nA. Histidine\nB. Cysteine\nC. Tyrosine\nD. Arginine\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The amino acid with the maximum buffering capacity is histidine because its side chain has a pKa value (~6.0) close to physiological pH (7.4), allowing it to effectively donate or accept protons. This makes histidine particularly efficient at buffering changes in pH in biological systems. \n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":99,"output_tokens":65}},"cost":5.187e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_423","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Sensitivity in gingival area of class II light cured composite restoration after 2 months is due to:\n\nOptions: \nA. Improper cavity preparation at gingival margin\nB. Curing from occlusal area only\nC. Addition of resin in multiple increments\nD. Curing from buccal and lingual aspect\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Sensitivity in the gingival area of a Class II light-cured composite restoration after two months is often due to inadequate polymerization of the resin at the gingival margin. Curing only from the occlusal area (option B) may result in insufficient light penetration to properly cure the deep gingival regions, leading to incomplete polymerization and subsequent microleakage or sensitivity. Therefore, the most likely cause is:\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":153,"output_tokens":112}},"cost":8.709000000000001e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_515","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Thirty-eight children consumed eatables procured from a single source at a picnic party. Twenty children developed abdominal cramps followed by vomiting and watery diarrhea 6-10 hours after the party. The most likely etiology for the outbreak is:\n\nOptions: \nA. Rotavirus infection\nB. Enterotoxigenic E.coli infection\nC. Staphylococcal toxin\nD. Clostridium perfringens infection\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The scenario describes a point-source foodborne outbreak with onset of cramps, vomiting, and watery diarrhea at 6–10 h. This timing and symptom cluster align with Clostridium perfringens type-A enterotoxin (produced in vivo after spore ingestion), whose median incubation is 8–12 h and whose dominant features are cramps plus watery diarrhea.  \n\nStaphylococcal pre-formed toxin typically produces illness in <6 h with vomiting predominating; rotavirus and ETEC have incubation periods of 1–3 days and are not classic picnic-food pathogens.  \n\nThus the single most likely etiology is D.\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":263,"output_tokens":123},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":0.00011410000000000001,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_663","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following structures is not of ectodermal origin:\n\nOptions: \nA. Hunter-schreger bands\nB. Enamel spindles\nC. Enamel tufts\nD. Enamel lamellae\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Enamel derives from ectoderm (via ameloblasts of the enamel organ), whereas dentin and odontoblast processes derive from ectomesenchyme. Hunter-Schreger bands, enamel tufts, and enamel lamellae are all intrinsic enamel features and therefore ectodermal. Enamel spindles, by contrast, are terminal extensions of odontoblast processes that cross the dentino-enamel junction and are consequently mesodermal/ectomesenchymal in origin.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":228,"output_tokens":93},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":9.21e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_133","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The necrotising pressure areas, undergoing bone resorption and endosteal bone formation\n\nOptions: \nA. Juvenile periodontitis\nB. Occlusal trauma\nC. Chronic suppurative periodontitis\nD. ANUG\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The described process of necrotizing pressure areas with bone resorption and endosteal bone formation is most consistent with occlusal trauma, where excessive force leads to localized bone changes, including resorption and reactive bone formation.\n\nThis pathophysiological response is characteristic of chronic mechanical stress on the periodontium, which aligns with option B.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":114,"output_tokens":74}},"cost":5.9220000000000006e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2223","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A woman comes with postdated pregnancy at 42 weeks. The initial evaluation would be:\n\nOptions: \nA. Induction of labour\nB. Review of previous menstrual history\nC. Cesarean section\nD. USG\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Postdated pregnancy (here at 42 weeks) first requires confirmation that the dates are accurate before any management decision such as induction or cesarean. This is achieved by reviewing the menstrual history (LMP, cycle regularity, prior dating scans) to exclude dating error, which is the most common reason for an apparently prolonged gestation. Only after dates are verified would further tests (USG for liquor/fetal well-being) or interventions be considered.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":230,"output_tokens":91},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":9.15e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_59","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Increase in height of mandible with increase in interdental spaces in elderly man\n\nOptions: \nA. Hyperpituitarism\nB. Hyperthyroidism\nC. Hypopituitarism\nD. Hyperparathyroidism\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The described mandibular changes (increased vertical height with tooth spacing) are a classic feature of acromegaly due to excess growth hormone after epiphyseal closure. This corresponds to hyperpituitarism (typically from a pituitary adenoma). The other options produce either reduced growth, generalized bone resorption, or unrelated metabolic effects and do not match the presentation.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":228,"output_tokens":73},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":8.21e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1179","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A new method of measuring Haemoglobin levels has been developed. Ten successive readings of a single sample are as follows: 9.4, 10.4, 9.6, 9.1, 10.8, 12.1, 10.1, 9.8, 9.2, 9.5. But the Haemoglobin measured by standard calorimetry was 10.2. Therefore the given method has\n\nOptions: \nA. Low validity, low reliability\nB. High validity, low reliability\nC. High validity, high reliability\nD. Low validity, high reliability\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The method shows low reliability because the readings vary widely (e.g., from 9.1 to 12.1), indicating poor consistency. However, the average of the readings is close to the true value (10.2), suggesting reasonable validity. Therefore, the method has low reliability but moderate to high validity.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":200,"output_tokens":72}},"cost":6.919999999999999e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1716","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Mass Drug Administration is not helpful for\n\nOptions: \nA. Lymphatic Filariasis\nB. Vitamin A Deficiency\nC. Worm infestation\nD. Scabies\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Mass Drug Administration (MDA) refers to population-level delivery of medicines (typically antiparasitic agents) as a core WHO strategy for several neglected tropical diseases and related conditions. It is a standard intervention for lymphatic filariasis (annual albendazole + DEC/ivermectin), soil-transmitted helminths (periodic albendazole/mebendazole deworming campaigns), and vitamin A deficiency (high-dose retinol supplementation rounds). Scabies is not addressed by routine MDA programs; management remains focused on case detection, topical acaricides, and contact treatment rather than blanket population dosing.\n\nThus the single option for which MDA is not an indicated or helpful strategy is D.\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":219,"output_tokens":138},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":0.0001128,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1431","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The probable reasons for a high incidence of dental caries in the teenage population relates most directly to:\n\nOptions: \nA. Rapid growth\nB. Frequency of sucrose intake\nC. Negligence in visiting the dentist\nD. Carelessness in oral hygiene habits\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The high incidence of dental caries in teenagers is primarily linked to dietary habits, especially frequent consumption of sugary foods and drinks. Sucrose promotes the growth of cariogenic bacteria, which produce acid that demineralizes tooth enamel. Therefore, the most direct reason is the frequency of sucrose intake.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":144,"output_tokens":85}},"cost":6.972e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2754","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Coefficient of thermal expansion of which of following is most similar to that of tooth?\n\nOptions: \nA. Gold inlay\nB. Acrylic resin\nC. Silicate cement\nD. Gold foil\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The coefficient of thermal expansion (CTE) of enamel is approximately 11–12 \\(\\times 10^{-6}/^\\circ\\)C (dentin slightly lower). Among the listed restoratives, only silicate cement has a CTE value in this narrow range (\\(\\approx 10 \\times 10^{-6}/^\\circ\\)C); gold alloys are modestly higher (\\(\\approx 14\\)), while acrylic resin is dramatically higher (\\(\\approx 70–90\\)). Consequently, silicate cement is the material whose dimensional change with temperature most closely matches that of tooth structure.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":225,"output_tokens":118},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":0.000104,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1923","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which one of the following is NOT a socio-economic indicator?\n\nOptions: \nA. Literacy rate\nB. Life expectancy at birth\nC. Housing\nD. Family size\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The question asks which option is NOT a socio-economic indicator. Socio-economic indicators typically measure economic and social well-being, such as literacy rate (education), life expectancy (health), and housing (living standards). Family size, while related to social structure, is more of a demographic characteristic than a socio-economic indicator.\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":100,"output_tokens":69}},"cost":5.4399999999999994e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2482","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: During laparoscopic inguinal hernia repair a tacker was accidently placed below and lateral to the ilio-pubic tract. Postoperatively the patient complained of pain and soreness in the thigh. This is due to the involvement of:\n\nOptions: \nA. Lateral cutaneous nerve of thigh\nB. llioinguinal nerve\nC. Genital branch of genitofemoral nerve\nD. Obturator nerve\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The pain in the thigh following misplaced tacker placement below and lateral to the ilio-pubic tract is most likely due to injury to the lateral cutaneous nerve of the thigh, which passes near this region and supplies sensation to the lateral thigh.\n\nThis nerve is vulnerable during laparoscopic hernia repair, especially when fixation is done close to the anterior superior iliac spine and inguinal ligament.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":154,"output_tokens":87}},"cost":7.222e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1186","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following change can be done in insulin structure so that there is least change in the function of insulin:\n\nOptions: \nA. Interchange of A1 & A4\nB. Interchange of B29 and B30\nC. Interchange of A5 & A6\nD. Breaking disulphide linkages\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The function of insulin is highly dependent on its three-dimensional structure, particularly the disulfide linkages and key residues in the A and B chains. Interchanging B29 and B30 (both located at the C-terminus of the B chain) has been shown to have minimal impact on activity, as seen in insulin analogs like insulin lispro, where this swap is used clinically. In contrast, breaking disulfide bonds or altering residues near the N-terminus of the A chain (A1, A4, A5, A6) would significantly disrupt structure and function.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":134,"output_tokens":127}},"cost":9.362000000000002e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_568","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: It is likely that cell mediated immune reactions (delayed\nhypersensitivity) occur in periodontitis because subjects with periodontitis have\n\nOptions: \nA. High levels of histamine in involved gingival tissue\nB. IgG antibodies reactive with plaque bacterial antigens\nC. Ttymphocytes sensitized to bacterial plaque antigens\nD. High Levels of collagenase in gingival fluids\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Cell-mediated immunity, particularly delayed hypersensitivity, involves T lymphocytes rather than antibodies or histamine release. In periodontitis, T lymphocytes sensitized to bacterial plaque antigens have been found in affected tissues, indicating a role for cellular immune responses. This supports the involvement of T cells in the immunopathology of the disease.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":146,"output_tokens":72}},"cost":6.217999999999999e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2302","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A patient complains of looseness of dentures within two to four hours of insertion. The most likely cause is:\n\nOptions: \nA. Psychological\nB. Adaptive unresponsiveness\nC. Deflective occlusion\nD. Unretentive denture\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The most likely cause of denture looseness a few hours after insertion is an unretentive denture, which fails to maintain proper fit due to inadequate adaptation to the underlying tissues. Over time, as saliva accumulates or minor tissue changes occur, the lack of retention becomes more apparent. Psychological factors or occlusal issues like deflective occlusion may contribute to discomfort but are less likely to cause progressive looseness.\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":117,"output_tokens":91}},"cost":6.981e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_733","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Following bilateral mandibular fracture in the canine region, the following muscles will tend to pull the mandible back:\n\nOptions: \nA. Genioglossus and anterior belly of digastric\nB. Genioglossus and mylohyoid\nC. Genioglossus and thyrohyoid\nD. Genioglossus and masseter\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The bilateral canine-region fractures isolate an anterior mandibular fragment whose posterior displacement is driven by muscles whose fibers run postero-inferiorly from genial tubercles or mental fossae. Genioglossus originates at the genial tubercles and passes backward; its contraction therefore retracts the fragment. The anterior bellies of the digastric likewise run postero-inferiorly from the mental fossae to the hyoid; with the hyoid fixed they exert a downward-and-backward vector on the same fragment.  \n\nMylohyoid, thyrohyoid and masseter attach either more posteriorly or exert opposing vectors and therefore cannot contribute to the described displacement.  \n\nThus the only pair that produces the observed posterior pull is option A.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":258,"output_tokens":149},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":0.0001261,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2494","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following doesn't occur in 5' to 3' direction?\n\nOptions: \nA. DNA repair\nB. DNA replication\nC. RNA editing\nD. Transcription\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"All nucleic acid polymerization processes (DNA replication, transcription, and most forms of DNA repair that rely on DNA polymerases) proceed exclusively 5′→3′ because of the chemistry of phosphodiester-bond formation. RNA editing, by contrast, is a post-transcriptional covalent modification (base deamination, insertion/deletion, etc.) performed by enzymes such as ADARs or editosomes; it does not involve directional chain elongation and therefore lacks an inherent 5′→3′ polarity.\n\nThus the process that does not occur in the 5′→3′ direction is RNA editing.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":222,"output_tokens":124},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":0.0001064,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_459","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Renal osteodystrophy differs from nutritional and genetic form of osteomaLacia in having:\n\nOptions: \nA. Hypocalcemia\nB. Hypercalcemia\nC. Hypophosphatemia\nD. Hyperphosphatemia\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Renal osteodystrophy is typically associated with chronic kidney disease, leading to impaired phosphate excretion and reduced activation of vitamin D. This results in hyperphosphatemia and secondary hyperparathyroidism, distinguishing it from nutritional and genetic osteomalacia, which are usually linked to vitamin D deficiency and present with hypophosphatemia. Therefore, the correct answer is hyperphosphatemia.\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":115,"output_tokens":88}},"cost":6.775e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1704","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a survey of sleep apnea scores among 10 people, the highest sample of 58 was entered by mistake as 85. This will affect the result as:\n\nOptions: \nA. Increased mean, decreased median\nB. Increased mean, increased median\nC. Increased mean. no change in median\nD. No change in mean, increased median.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The incorrect entry of 85 instead of 58 increases the sum of the data, which will increase the mean. The median, however, is the middle value when data is ordered and is less sensitive to extreme values, especially in a small sample of 10; unless the error shifts the middle values, the median remains unchanged. Therefore, the mean increases but the median stays the same.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":139,"output_tokens":87}},"cost":7.026999999999999e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2301","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Cell membrane of a cell is freely permeable to three ions X, Y and Z. At resting membrane potential, the respective equilibrium potentials of Xand Y are -30mV and -40 mV.What will happen to the membrane potential if a drug is infused which can block the permeability of Z?\n\nOptions: \nA. Depolarisation\nB. Hyperpolarization\nC. No change\nD. Hyperpolarization following repolarization\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The resting membrane potential (RMP) is a permeability-weighted average of the equilibrium potentials of all open ions. With free permeability to X, Y and Z, RMP lies between Ex, Ey and Ez. Blocking permeability to Z removes its contribution, so RMP must shift toward the average of the only remaining values (Ex = −30 mV, Ey = −40 mV). Because both of those values are less negative than a typical RMP, the shift is depolarizing.\n\nThus the correct choice is A.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":273,"output_tokens":109},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":0.0001091,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_477","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: On rubber dam application gingiva is seen protruding out of margins, it can be seen due to?\n\nOptions: \nA. Edematous gingival tissues\nB. Holes paced too far apart\nC. Using a light-weight dam\nD. Holes placed too close together\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Gingival tissue protruding through the margins of a rubber dam typically occurs when the holes are punched too close together, causing the dam to stretch excessively and impinge on the gingiva, leading to tissue protrusion. This improper hole placement reduces the space for each tooth, increasing pressure on the surrounding tissues. \n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":122,"output_tokens":68}},"cost":5.6659999999999996e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_48","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following type of failure may occur, if the coefficient of thermal expansion of ceramic is much lower than that of metal?\n\nOptions: \nA. Cohesive failure of ceramic\nB. Adhesive failure of metal ceramic bond\nC. Cohesive failure of metal\nD. Cohesive failure of metal ceramic bond\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The coefficient of thermal expansion (CTE) mismatch is evaluated upon cooling after firing. When ceramic CTE is much lower than metal CTE, the metal contracts more, placing the ceramic under substantial compression. Because dental ceramics are brittle and weak in tension (and can develop surface tensile stresses from the mismatch), this commonly produces cracking or fracture within the ceramic itself (cohesive failure) rather than at the interface.\n\nThus the most likely outcome among the given choices is option A.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":249,"output_tokens":96},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":9.78e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1772","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: 3 weeks after insertion of distal extension partial denture, the patient reports to the dental clinic with complaint of sensitivity to chewing pressure. The most probable reason would be:\n\nOptions: \nA. Improper occlusion\nB. Abrasion of tooth by clasp\nC. Wearing off the cement base\nD. Passive retentive arm\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The question concerns a distal extension RPD (Kennedy Class I/II), where the prosthesis is tooth-and-tissue supported and therefore settles under function. Any residual occlusal discrepancy that was not eliminated at insertion will become symptomatic once the denture has seated fully, typically within a few weeks, producing precisely the complaint of sensitivity to chewing pressure.  \n\nThe remaining options are implausible on temporal or mechanistic grounds: clasp abrasion (B) requires months of wear, loss of a cement base (C) is not mentioned, and a passive retentive arm (D) would produce loss of retention rather than pain.  \n\nThus the most probable cause is improper occlusion.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":251,"output_tokens":134},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":0.0001172,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1029","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In leukemia patient, post extraction bleeding doesn't stop because of:\n\nOptions: \nA. Increased leukocyte count\nB. Increased Ca+ level in blood\nC. Platelet disorder\nD. Deficiency of clotting factors\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"In leukemia patients, post-extraction bleeding often persists due to impaired platelet function or low platelet count, which is common in the disease. Platelet disorders prevent effective clot formation at the extraction site. While other factors may contribute, platelet dysfunction is the most direct cause.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":132,"output_tokens":82}},"cost":6.636e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_248","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Wave patterns of EEF, ECG and EMG are depicted below. The B pattern belongs to (Figure was not provided in the exam):\n\nOptions: \nA. NREM sleep\nB. REM sleep\nC. Wakefulness\nD. Quiet wakefulness\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Without the figure, it is not possible to definitively determine which wave pattern corresponds to B. However, in typical neurophysiological contexts, if B shows irregular, low-amplitude waves with rapid eye movements, it would most likely represent REM sleep. Therefore, based on common pattern associations:\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":117,"output_tokens":63}},"cost":5.3009999999999996e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_53","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following is most effective for gluconeogenesis in starvation?\n\nOptions: \nA. Acetyl Co-A stimulation of pyruvate carboxylase\nB. Fructose-1, 6-biphosphate stimulation of phosphofructokinase-1\nC. Citrate stimulation of acetyl carboxylase\nD. Fructose-2, 6-biphosphate stimulation of phosphofructokinase-2\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"During starvation, gluconeogenesis is upregulated to maintain blood glucose levels, and acetyl Co-A activation of pyruvate carboxylase is a key regulatory step that channels pyruvate toward glucose production. Acetyl Co-A, derived from fatty acid oxidation, stimulates pyruvate carboxylase, promoting the conversion of pyruvate to oxaloacetate, a critical entry point into gluconeogenesis. The other options either promote glycolysis or are not directly relevant to gluconeogenesis during starvation.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":156,"output_tokens":115}},"cost":8.928e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1287","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Asymptomatic hep B is common in 2-3% normal population, but there is increased risk of transmission into hepatocellular carcinoma. Why?\n\nOptions: \nA. Inability to induce inflammation to remove the organism\nB. High level of transaminases\nC. High rate of proliferation of virus\nD. Integration of viral DNA with host DNA\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The correct answer is \\boxed{D}. Integration of viral DNA with host DNA can disrupt tumor suppressor genes or promote genomic instability, leading to an increased risk of hepatocellular carcinoma. This process occurs even in asymptomatic individuals, explaining the cancer risk despite lack of symptoms.","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":138,"output_tokens":57}},"cost":5.214e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_511","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A lateral sliding flap done on a tooth with roots denuded for 6 years will show\n\nOptions: \nA. PDL fibres attached to cementum\nB. PDL fibres attached to dentin\nC. Epithelium adjacent to previously denuded root surface\nD. Co adaptation to the remaining fibres\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"After 6 years of root surface denudation, the denuded root surface is unlikely to re-establish normal periodontal ligament (PDL) attachment. Instead, a long junctional epithelium typically forms, with epithelium migrating and adhering to the previously exposed root surface. Therefore, a lateral sliding flap would most likely show epithelium adjacent to the previously denuded root surface.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":131,"output_tokens":87}},"cost":6.923e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_355","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In examining the edentulous mouth of an aged patient wearing complete maxillary denture against six mandibular teeth, the dentist will see:\n\nOptions: \nA. Cystic degeneration of the foramina of the anterior palatine nerve\nB. Loss of osseous structure in the anterior maxilla\nC. Flabby tissue in the posterior region\nD. Decrease interocclusal distance\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The scenario describes combination syndrome (Kelly syndrome), in which a maxillary complete denture opposes mandibular anterior teeth only. This produces excessive anterior occlusal loading that resorbs the premaxillary ridge, producing the osseous loss cited in option B. Options A and C describe unrelated or anatomically incorrect sequelae, while D is an effect of posterior bite collapse rather than the primary finding.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":261,"output_tokens":81},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":9.27e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1816","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Child is Evasive and dawdling, what could be the child's mother behavior:\n\nOptions: \nA. Overprotective mother.\nB. Authoritarian mother.\nC. Rejecting mother.\nD. Underaffectionate mother.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The question pertains to links between specific maternal attitudes and resulting child behaviors in developmental psychology. A rejecting mother tends to produce insecurity and avoidance in the child, manifesting as evasive (withdrawn/avoidant) behavior and dawdling (passive resistance or delay tactics). This does not align as closely with overprotective (produces dependency), authoritarian (produces compliance or rebellion), or underaffectionate (overlaps with rejecting but is less directly tied to these exact behaviors) styles.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":230,"output_tokens":100},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":9.6e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1662","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: GPCR that does not act through opening of potassium channels is?\n\nOptions: \nA. Muscarinic M2 receptor\nB. Dopamine D2 receptor\nC. Serotonin 5 HT1 receptor\nD. Angiotensin 1 receptor\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The angiotensin 1 receptor (AT1 receptor) is a GPCR that primarily acts through the Gq pathway, leading to IP3 and DAG production and calcium release, rather than opening potassium channels. In contrast, Muscarinic M2, Dopamine D2, and Serotonin 5-HT1 receptors are Gi-coupled and typically cause potassium channel opening leading to hyperpolarization. Therefore, the correct answer is the receptor that does not use this mechanism.\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":116,"output_tokens":103}},"cost":7.688e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_720","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 60-year-old has got severe bulla and target lesion which erythema around halo and genital lesions:\n\nOptions: \nA. Stevens Jhonson syndrome\nB. Herpes zoster\nC. Herpes simplex\nD. Herpangina\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The presence of severe bullae, target lesions with erythematous halos, and genital involvement in a 60-year-old is most consistent with Stevens-Johnson syndrome (SJS), which is a mucocutaneous reaction often triggered by medications or infections. Target lesions and bullae are hallmark features of SJS, and genital mucosal involvement is common. Herpes zoster and herpes simplex typically present with grouped vesicles on an erythematous base, not target lesions, and herpangina primarily affects the oropharynx without genital lesions.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":118,"output_tokens":122}},"cost":8.854e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1610","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Insulin resistance is seen in liver disease because of-\n\nOptions: \nA. Decreased secretion of insulin\nB. Hepatic steatosis\nC. Hepatocytedysfunction\nD. Low 'C'peptide level\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Insulin resistance in liver disease is primarily due to hepatocyte dysfunction, which impairs insulin signaling and glucose metabolism in the liver. The liver plays a key role in insulin clearance and glucose regulation, and damaged hepatocytes fail to respond properly to insulin. This makes hepatocyte dysfunction the most direct cause among the options.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":112,"output_tokens":69}},"cost":5.596e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1697","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In uncontrolled diabetes mellitus, elevated triglyceride and VLDL levels are seen due to:\n\nOptions: \nA. Increased activity of lipoprotein lipase and decreased activity of hormone sensitive lipase\nB. Increased activity of hormone sensitive lipase and decreased activity of lipoprotein lipase\nC. Increase in peripheral LDL receptors\nD. Increased activity of hepatic lipase\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"In uncontrolled diabetes mellitus, insulin deficiency leads to increased activity of hormone-sensitive lipase in adipose tissue, causing elevated free fatty acid release into the liver. This promotes hepatic synthesis of triglycerides and VLDL, while low insulin also reduces lipoprotein lipase activity, impairing triglyceride clearance. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":175,"output_tokens":98}},"cost":8.155e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1269","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Vascular event of inflammation in order-a) delayed prolonged- leukocytes mediated injuryb) immediate transient - mast cell activation lead to release of histamine bradykininc) immediate prolonged- direct endothelial injury by bacterial toxind) Somewhat delayed prolonged- sun exposure /heat stroke lead to mild endothelial injury\n\nOptions: \nA. ABCD\nB. DCBA\nC. ACDB\nD. BDCA\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The sequence of vascular events in inflammation begins with immediate transient vasodilation due to mast cell activation (B), followed by immediate prolonged due to direct endothelial injury (C), then somewhat delayed prolonged from mild injury like heat (D), and finally delayed prolonged leukocyte-mediated injury (A). Thus, the correct order is B → C → D → A.\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":150,"output_tokens":77}},"cost":6.57e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2687","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The least effect on the prognosis of a periodontal disease is\n\nOptions: \nA. Suppuration from the pocket\nB. Furcation involvement\nC. Alveolar bone loss\nD. Co-operation and motivation of the patient\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The least effect on the prognosis of periodontal disease is suppuration from the pocket, as it is a sign of active infection but does not independently determine long-term outcomes like structural damage or patient behavior. Factors such as furcation involvement, alveolar bone loss, and patient cooperation significantly influence treatment success and disease progression. Suppuration can be managed with therapy and does not carry the same prognostic weight as the other factors.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":113,"output_tokens":93}},"cost":7.049e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_476","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following event has little or no significance?\n\nOptions: \nA. Mandibular incisor erupting before mandibular molar\nB. Mandibular canine erupting before mandibular premolar\nC. Mandibular 2nd premolar erupting before mandibular 2nd molar\nD. Maxillary premolar and canine erupting before maxillary 2nd molar\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The question concerns which tooth-eruption sequence deviation carries negligible diagnostic or occlusal importance. In the mandible the second premolar normally erupts before the second molar; reversal of this order therefore produces no clinically meaningful effect on arch length or intercuspation. By contrast, sequences A, B and D each alter the leeway space or molar–premolar relationship and can precipitate crowding, impaction or Class-II molar drift, giving them clear clinical weight.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":257,"output_tokens":96},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":9.94e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2268","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: 3 year old girl having delayed milestones, playing with\nherself, difficulty in learning is likely to be suffering from\n\nOptions: \nA. Mental retardation\nB. Autism\nC. Specific Learning Disorder\nD. ADHD\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The child's delayed milestones, self-focused behavior (playing with herself), and difficulty in learning are hallmark features of autism spectrum disorder. While mental retardation (now termed intellectual disability) and specific learning disorder can involve learning difficulties, the social and behavioral patterns point more strongly to autism. ADHD typically does not present with delayed milestones or solitary play in the same way.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":112,"output_tokens":77}},"cost":6.076e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_557","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A G2 P1+0+0 diabetic mother present at 32 weeks pregnancy, there is history of full term fetal demise in last pregnancy. Her vitals are stable, sugar is controlled and fetus is stable. Which among the following will be the most appropriate management?\n\nOptions: \nA. To induce at 38 weeks\nB. To induce at 40 weeks\nC. Cesarean section at 38 weeks\nD. To wait for spontaneous delivery\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"In a G2 P1+0+0 diabetic mother with a history of prior fetal demise, current pregnancy at 32 weeks, and well-controlled diabetes, delivery is typically recommended earlier than term to reduce the risk of stillbirth. Current guidelines suggest delivery around 38–39 weeks for well-controlled diabetic pregnancies, especially with prior adverse outcomes. Induction of labor at 38 weeks is preferred over cesarean if the cervix is favorable and the fetus is stable.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":162,"output_tokens":104}},"cost":8.346e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_797","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the best management of the case shown?\n\nOptions: \nA. Dapsone plus steroids\nB. Stop smoking and screen for cancer\nC. Vitamin supplements\nD. Antifungals for oral candidiasis\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The question appears to refer to a clinical case, likely involving oral lesions or a condition associated with smoking and possible malignancy, such as leukoplakia or oral potentially malignant disorders. The most appropriate initial management in such cases is smoking cessation and cancer screening to rule out or prevent progression to malignancy. \n\nTherefore, the best answer is \\boxed{B}.","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":110,"output_tokens":73}},"cost":5.8099999999999996e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1041","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which is best method to assess fetal damage in a diabetes mother in 1st trimester is:\n\nOptions: \nA. Blood sugar estimation\nB. Urine ketone assay\nC. Amniocentesis to see level of sugar in amniotic fluid\nD. Glycosylated Hb\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The best method to assess fetal damage risk in a diabetic mother during the first trimester is glycosylated Hb (HbA1c), as it reflects long-term glycemic control over the preceding 2–3 months, which is critical for fetal organ development. Poor control during this period increases the risk of congenital anomalies. Blood sugar estimation and urine ketones reflect only immediate status, and amniocentesis is not used in the first trimester for this purpose.\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":127,"output_tokens":105}},"cost":7.951e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1194","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: To assess outcome from labour, cost, time\n\nOptions: \nA. Cost benefit\nB. Cost Effectiveness\nC. Cost utility\nD. Risk Benefit\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"To assess outcomes from labor in terms of cost, time, and effectiveness, the most appropriate method is cost-effectiveness analysis, which compares the relative costs and outcomes (effects) of different interventions. It is commonly used when the outcomes are measured in natural units (e.g., time saved, labor hours reduced). This makes cost-effectiveness the best fit among the options.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":97,"output_tokens":80}},"cost":6.0610000000000004e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1326","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which is the best index for burden of disease?\n\nOptions: \nA. Case fatality rate\nB. Morbidity data\nC. Dependency ratio\nD. Disability adjusted life years\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The best index for measuring the burden of disease is Disability Adjusted Life Years (DALYs), as it accounts for both premature death and time lived with disability. It provides a comprehensive measure of health loss across populations. \n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":120,"output_tokens":64}},"cost":5.4e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1479","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following drugs is least efficacious in the treatment of temporal lobe epilepsy?\n\nOptions: \nA. Phenobarbitone\nB. Phenytoin sodium\nC. Primidone\nD. Carbamazepine\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Temporal lobe epilepsy involves focal (partial) seizures, for which first-line agents include carbamazepine (which blocks voltage-gated Na channels and is especially effective in the temporal lobe) and phenytoin (likewise a Na-channel blocker with established efficacy). Both primidone and its active metabolite phenobarbital also possess proven antiseizure activity against partial seizures, although they are generally regarded as second-line because of greater sedation. Phenobarbital, however, shows the lowest relative efficacy among the listed options for this seizure type and is rarely chosen when the goal is optimal seizure control rather than cost or availability.\n\nThus the drug with the least efficacy is phenobarbitone.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":229,"output_tokens":135},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":0.0001133,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1514","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 50 year male presented with high BP of 160/100 mm Hg and hea rate of 120/min. CECT is shown below. Which is best management of this condition?\n\nOptions: \nA. Surgical repair\nB. LMW heparin\nC. Beta blocker\nD. Vitamin K inhibitors\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The patient presents with severe hypertension and tachycardia, which in the context of a CECT (contrast-enhanced computed tomography) likely suggests an acute aortic condition such as aortic dissection. Beta-blockers are the first-line treatment to reduce shear stress on the aortic wall by controlling heart rate and blood pressure. Therefore, the best initial management is a beta blocker.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":137,"output_tokens":84}},"cost":6.821e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1547","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In fracture of atrophic mandible with bone loss, what is the best treatment modality?\n\nOptions: \nA. Bone grafting and load bearing\nB. Bone grafting and load sharing\nC. Semi-rigid fixation\nD. IMF with open reduction\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Atrophic edentulous mandibles lack sufficient bone stock or buttressing contacts to share functional loads, so any fracture with segmental bone loss requires autogenous grafting plus a rigid reconstruction plate (load-bearing osteosynthesis) that spans the defect and bears 100 % of the masticatory forces until the graft incorporates.  \nLoad-sharing miniplates, semi-rigid fixation, or IMF alone cannot provide the necessary stability in this setting and risk non-union or plate fracture.  \nHence option A is the only modality that simultaneously restores bone volume and achieves absolute rigid fixation.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":234,"output_tokens":115},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":0.00010430000000000001,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_1861","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Routine examination of a 17 years old asymptomatic boy reveals sho PR interval, and delta wave on ECG. The least effective measure for the boy would be:\n\nOptions: \nA. Hotter monitoring\nB. Treadmill stress test\nC. Beta blocker\nD. Reassurance\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The ECG findings (short PR interval + delta wave) indicate asymptomatic WPW/pre-excitation due to an accessory pathway. Noninvasive risk stratification with Holter monitoring or treadmill testing is indicated to assess abrupt loss of pre-excitation (implying a long refractory period and low risk of sudden death). Beta-blockers are contraindicated, as AV-nodal blockade can preferentially enhance accessory-pathway conduction and precipitate malignant arrhythmias if AF occurs; thus they are the least appropriate action.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":242,"output_tokens":99},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":9.79e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2010","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of these is the best study to evaluate effect and outcome?\n\nOptions: \nA. Clinical trial\nB. Coho\nC. Case control study\nD. Cross sectional study\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The best study design to evaluate the effect and outcome of an intervention is a clinical trial, as it involves controlled testing of treatments in human participants. Clinical trials allow for causal inferences due to randomization and control groups. \n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":120,"output_tokens":68}},"cost":5.64e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2065","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following is the least important prognostic factor in congenital diaphragmatic hernia ?\n\nOptions: \nA. Pulmonary Hypertension\nB. Delay in emergent surgery\nC. Size of defect\nD. Gestational age at diagnosis\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The modern management of CDH prioritizes physiologic stabilization (including management of pulmonary hypertension) before repair, so intentionally delaying surgery is not an adverse prognostic factor and may even be beneficial. By contrast, pulmonary hypertension, defect size (as a surrogate for the degree of pulmonary hypoplasia), and earlier gestational age at diagnosis are all well-validated predictors of survival and morbidity. Therefore, among the listed options, delay in emergent surgery is the least important prognostic factor.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":229,"output_tokens":94},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":9.28e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2296","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of these is the most reliable method for monitoring fluid resuscitation?\n\nOptions: \nA. Urine output\nB. CVP\nC. Pulse rate\nD. Blood pressure\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The most reliable method for monitoring fluid resuscitation among the options is urine output, as it reflects renal perfusion and overall tissue perfusion. While CVP (central venous pressure) and blood pressure can be useful, they are less reliable due to variability and delayed responses. Pulse rate can be influenced by many non-volume factors and is not specific.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":102,"output_tokens":76}},"cost":5.886e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2425","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 29-year-old, 4 months pregnant primigravida has history of juvenile myoclonic epilepsy. She has been regularly taking sodium valproate and now presents requesting for an opinion for a change in her anti-epileptic treatment. What would you sugeets her?\n\nOptions: \nA. Immediately taper off valproate and sta lamotrigine\nB. Switch to carbamazepine\nC. Continue valproate and serial drug monitoring in blood\nD. Add lamotrigine to valproate\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Valproate is associated with a high risk of congenital malformations and neurodevelopmental disorders when used during pregnancy, especially in the first trimester, and should be avoided if possible. Lamotrigine is considered a safer alternative for use in pregnancy and is often the preferred agent for women with epilepsy who are pregnant or planning pregnancy. Therefore, the best approach is to gradually switch from valproate to lamotrigine under close supervision.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":177,"output_tokens":97}},"cost":8.121e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"MedMCQA_2467","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following can be used to delay preterm contractions of uterus with best neurological outcome for the fetus?\n\nOptions: \nA. Mgso4\nB. Nifidipine\nC. Ritodrine\nD. Isoxprine\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"MgSO4 is administered as a tocolytic in threatened preterm labor before 32 weeks and simultaneously confers fetal neuroprotection by reducing the incidence of cerebral palsy and intraventricular hemorrhage. The other agents (nifedipine, ritodrine, isoxsuprine) can suppress uterine contractions but lack this neuroprotective effect. Therefore the single agent that satisfies both requirements in the question is MgSO4.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":234,"output_tokens":84},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":8.88e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Vehicles_120","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What kind of train was Stepney, a train on the Bluebell Railway notable for his appearance in \"The Railway Series\"?\n\nOptions: \nA. LB&SCR A1X\nB. LB&SCR J1\nC. LB&SCR E2\nD. LB&SCR D1\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Stepney was an LB&SCR A1X class locomotive, a rebuilt version of the original A1 class, famously known for its appearances in \"The Railway Series\" by Rev. W. Awdry. It has been preserved and is operational on the Bluebell Railway. \n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":124,"output_tokens":63}},"cost":5.392e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Vehicles_3704","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What nickname was given to Air Canada Flight 143 after it ran out of fuel and glided to safety in 1983?\n\nOptions: \nA. Gimli Glider\nB. Gimli Microlight\nC. Gimli Superb\nD. Gimli Chaser\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The nickname \"Gimli Glider\" was given to Air Canada Flight 143 after it ran out of fuel mid-flight and successfully glided to an emergency landing at a former airbase in Gimli, Manitoba. The incident occurred in 1983 and became famous for the skillful handling by the flight crew. The correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":125,"output_tokens":78}},"cost":6.305e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Vehicles_1602","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following collision avoidance systems helps airplanes avoid colliding with each other?\n\nOptions: \nA. TCAS\nB. TAWS\nC. GPWS\nD. OCAS\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The correct answer is A. TCAS (Traffic Alert and Collision Avoidance System) is specifically designed to detect nearby aircraft and provide resolution advisories to pilots to avoid mid-air collisions. TAWS and GPWS are terrain awareness systems, and OCAS is not a standard aviation system. \n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":102,"output_tokens":63}},"cost":5.1059999999999996e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Vehicles_3934","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The Japanese Shinkansen beat the French TGV's speed record for fastest electric rail train.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The French TGV holds the official world speed record for wheeled electric rail trains (574.8 km/h on conventional track in 2007). The Shinkansen's highest conventional-rail speed is lower (around 443 km/h), and its faster maglev runs use a non-rail technology outside the category referenced in the statement. Therefore the claim that the Shinkansen beat the TGV record is false.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":214,"output_tokens":88},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":8.68e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Vehicles_3397","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The difference between the lengths of a Boeing 777-300ER and an Airbus A350-1000 is closest to:\n\nOptions: \nA. 10m \nB. 100m\nC. 1m\nD. 0.1m\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The Boeing 777-300ER is approximately 73.9 meters long, while the Airbus A350-1000 is about 73.8 meters long. The difference in length is only about 0.1 meters. Therefore, the closest difference is 0.1m.\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":128,"output_tokens":74}},"cost":6.104e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Vehicles_4026","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Arriva is owned by the Deutsche Bahn.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Arriva is a multinational public transport company that was acquired by Deutsche Bahn in 2010. Therefore, it is correct that Arriva is owned by Deutsche Bahn. \n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":84,"output_tokens":43}},"cost":3.672e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Vehicles_991","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In 1993 Swedish car manufacturer Saab experimented with replacing the steering wheel with a joystick in a Saab 9000.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"In 1993, Saab did experiment with alternative control systems, including a joystick, as part of its \"Saab Magic Eye\" concept in the Saab 9000. This was intended to improve ergonomics and safety, although it never reached production. Therefore, the statement is accurate.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":117,"output_tokens":72}},"cost":5.840999999999999e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Vehicles_3396","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In 2014, over 6 million General Motors vehicles were recalled due to what critical flaw?\n\nOptions: \nA. Faulty brake pads\nB. Faulty ignition switch\nC. Breaking fuel lines\nD. Malfunctioning gas pedal\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The correct answer is B. Faulty ignition switch. In 2014, General Motors recalled over 6 million vehicles due to a defect in the ignition switch that could unexpectedly turn off the engine, disabling critical safety systems like airbags. This flaw was linked to numerous accidents, injuries, and fatalities. \n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":116,"output_tokens":70}},"cost":5.7079999999999996e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Vehicles_645","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What part of an automobile engine uses lobes to open and close intake and exhaust valves, and allows an air/fuel mixture into the engine?\n\nOptions: \nA. Drive shaft\nB. Piston\nC. Camshaft\nD. Crankshaft\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The camshaft uses lobes to open and close the intake and exhaust valves, allowing the air/fuel mixture into the engine and exhaust gases out. It is precisely timed with the crankshaft to ensure proper engine operation. \n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":116,"output_tokens":51}},"cost":4.5679999999999996e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Vehicles_2541","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What UK Train does NOT go over 125MPH?\n\nOptions: \nA. Javelin\nB. Class 43\nC. Sprinter\nD. Pendolino\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The Sprinter family (Classes 150–159) consists of regional DMUs with a design top speed of 75 mph (rarely 90 mph in service). By contrast, the Class 43 HST, Class 395 Javelin, and Class 390 Pendolino are all cleared for 125 mph (or higher) operation on UK infrastructure. Therefore only the Sprinter fails to exceed 125 mph.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":220,"output_tokens":87},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":8.75e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Vehicles_471","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The snowmobile was invented by Canadian Joseph-Armand Bombardier in 1937.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The statement is correct, as Joseph-Armand Bombardier (a Canadian inventor from Quebec) is widely credited with developing and patenting the first practical snowmobile, known as the B7, in 1937. While earlier prototypes existed in other countries, Bombardier’s version is recognized as the foundational design that led to modern snowmobiles.  \n\nThus, the most likely correct choice is A.  \n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":213,"output_tokens":86},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":8.56e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Vehicles_673","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The Chevrolet Corvette has always been made exclusively with V8 engines only.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The statement is false because the Chevrolet Corvette has not always been made exclusively with V8 engines. Starting with the 2020 model year, Chevrolet introduced the C8 Corvette with an available turbocharged V6 engine in its E-Ray hybrid variant. Additionally, there were earlier experimental or special edition models that deviated from the traditional V8.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":88,"output_tokens":75}},"cost":5.644e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Vehicles_2597","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What are the cylinder-like parts that pump up and down within the engine?\n\nOptions: \nA. Leaf Springs\nB. Pistons\nC. ABS\nD. Radiators\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The cylinder-like parts that move up and down inside an engine are responsible for compressing fuel and air and converting combustion energy into motion. These components are known as pistons. Leaf springs, ABS, and radiators serve entirely different functions unrelated to this motion.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":99,"output_tokens":57}},"cost":4.7069999999999995e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Vehicles_2719","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following countries has officially banned the civilian use of dash cams in cars?\n\nOptions: \nA. Austria\nB. United States\nC. South Korea\nD. Czechia\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Austria has strict privacy laws that restrict the use of dash cams by civilians, as they can record people without consent in public spaces, which violates data protection regulations. While other countries may have restrictions, Austria is known for officially banning civilian dash cam use. \n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":102,"output_tokens":57}},"cost":4.7459999999999996e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Vehicles_3718","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What do the 4 Rings in Audi's Logo represent?\n\nOptions: \nA. Main cities vital to Audi\nB. States in which Audi makes the most sales\nC. Previously independent automobile manufacturers\nD. Countries in which Audi makes the most sales\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The four rings in Audi's logo represent four previously independent automobile manufacturers that merged to form Auto Union, the predecessor of Audi. These companies were Audi, DKW, Horch, and Wanderer. The logo symbolizes their unity and collaboration.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":115,"output_tokens":55}},"cost":4.795e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Vehicles_601","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The General Motors EV1 was the first street-legal production electric vehicle.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The General Motors EV1, introduced in 1996, was one of the first mass-produced electric vehicles designed specifically for consumer use and was indeed street-legal. While there were earlier electric vehicles, the EV1 is widely recognized as the first modern, purpose-built, street-legal production EV by a major automaker. Therefore, the statement is accurate.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":89,"output_tokens":79}},"cost":5.897e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Vehicles_509","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Ferrari has never made a V10 engine for any of its cars.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Ferrari has indeed produced V10 engines, most notably in the Ferrari F10 (2010 Formula 1 car) and the road-going Ferrari 458 Italia, which features a 4.5L V10 engine. Therefore, the statement that Ferrari has never made a V10 engine is incorrect.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":89,"output_tokens":75}},"cost":5.657e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Vehicles_2548","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Volkswagen's legendary VR6 engine has cylinders positioned at what degree angle?\n\nOptions: \nA. 15 Degree\nB. 45 Degree\nC. 90 Degree\nD. 30 Degree\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The Volkswagen VR6 engine features a narrow-angle V-configuration where the cylinders are positioned at a 15-degree angle, allowing for a compact design that fits in engines bays typically meant for inline-four engines. This unique layout combines the benefits of a V-engine with the space efficiency of a straight engine. \n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":108,"output_tokens":68}},"cost":5.484e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Vehicles_132","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: When BMW was established in 1916, it was producing automobiles.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"BMW was established in 1916, but initially it produced aircraft engines, not automobiles. The company began manufacturing automobiles much later, with its first car introduced in the 1920s. Therefore, the statement is false.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":90,"output_tokens":55}},"cost":4.47e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Vehicles_3234","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which Variable Valve Timing technology is used by BMW?\n\nOptions: \nA. VANOS\nB. MultiAir\nC. VVT-iw\nD. VVEL\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"BMW uses VANOS as its Variable Valve Timing technology. VANOS adjusts the timing of the intake and exhaust valves to optimize engine performance and efficiency. \n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":98,"output_tokens":35}},"cost":3.374e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Vehicles_2087","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: BMW M GmbH is a subsidiary of BMW AG that focuses on car performance.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"BMW M GmbH, originally known as BMW Motorsport GmbH, is indeed a subsidiary of BMW AG dedicated to developing high-performance variants of BMW vehicles. It is responsible for models such as the M3, M5, and X5 M, which are engineered for enhanced power, handling, and sporty aesthetics. Therefore, the statement is accurate.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":89,"output_tokens":75}},"cost":5.657e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Vehicles_1743","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following passenger jets is the longest?\n\nOptions: \nA. Boeing 787-10\nB. Airbus A330-200\nC. Airbus A350-1000\nD. Boeing 747-8\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The Boeing 747-8 is the longest passenger jet among the options listed, with a length of approximately 76.4 meters. All other options are significantly shorter: the Boeing 787-10 is about 68.3 meters, the A330-200 is 59 meters, and the A350-1000 is 73.8 meters. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":117,"output_tokens":78}},"cost":6.201e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Vehicles_1879","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which Audi does not use Haldex based all wheel drive system?\n\nOptions: \nA. Audi TT\nB. Audi S3\nC. Audi A3\nD. Audi A8\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The Audi A8 uses a permanent all-wheel drive system based on a Torsen center differential, not the Haldex system used in transverse-engine platforms. In contrast, the Audi TT, S3, and A3 (in most configurations) utilize the Haldex-based quattro system. Therefore, the correct answer is the model that differs in drivetrain layout.\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":103,"output_tokens":81}},"cost":6.199000000000001e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Vehicles_3606","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How much horsepower is produced by the SD40-2 Locomotive?\n\nOptions: \nA. 2,190\nB. 2,578\nC. 3,000\nD. 3,200\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The EMD SD40-2 is a diesel-electric locomotive model whose 16-cylinder 645E3 prime mover is factory-rated at 3,000 hp (2,240 kW). This rating is unchanged from the original SD40 and is confirmed across EMD specification sheets, operator manuals, and standard railfan references. The other listed values correspond to different locomotive models or mis-remembered figures and do not apply to the SD40-2.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":229,"output_tokens":96},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":9.38e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Vehicles_279","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: When was Cadillac founded?\n\nOptions: \nA. 1985\nB. 1898\nC. 1964\nD. 1902\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Cadillac was founded in 1902, making it one of the oldest American luxury automobile brands. It was established by Henry Leland and named after Antoine de la Mothe Cadillac, the founder of Detroit. \n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":103,"output_tokens":50}},"cost":4.339e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Vehicles_3158","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which country has the international vehicle registration letter 'A'?\n\nOptions: \nA. Australia\nB. Austria\nC. Armenia\nD. Afghanistan\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The international vehicle registration letter 'A' stands for Austria. This code is used on vehicle license plates to identify the country of registration internationally. \n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":94,"output_tokens":34}},"cost":3.2619999999999996e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Vehicles_3245","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The LS3 engine is how many cubic inches?\n\nOptions: \nA. 376\nB. 346\nC. 427\nD. 364\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The LS3 engine is a General Motors small-block V8 with a displacement of 6.2 liters, which converts to approximately 376 cubic inches. This engine is commonly found in vehicles like the Chevrolet Corvette and Camaro. \n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":104,"output_tokens":54}},"cost":4.592e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Vehicles_3076","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What country was the Trabant 601 manufactured in?\n\nOptions: \nA. Soviet Union\nB. Hungary\nC. East Germany\nD. France\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The Trabant 601 was a compact car produced by VEB Sachsenring Automobilwerke in Zwickau, which was located in East Germany. It became an iconic vehicle of the former German Democratic Republic (GDR). \n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":97,"output_tokens":55}},"cost":4.5610000000000005e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Vehicles_872","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What model was the sports car gifted to Yuri Gagarin by the French government in 1965?\n\nOptions: \nA. AC Cobra\nB. Porsche 911\nC. Matra Djet\nD. Alpine A110\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The sports car gifted to Yuri Gagarin by the French government in 1965 was the Matra Djet. Matra, a French company, produced the Djet as one of the earliest mid-engined production cars, and it was presented as a diplomatic gift. \n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":117,"output_tokens":64}},"cost":5.361e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Vehicles_1329","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The LS2 engine is how many cubic inches?\n\nOptions: \nA. 364\nB. 346\nC. 402\nD. 376\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The LS2 engine is a General Motors small-block V8 that has a displacement of 6.0 liters, which converts to approximately 364 cubic inches. This engine was introduced in the early 2000s and used in various Chevrolet and GMC vehicles. \n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":104,"output_tokens":62}},"cost":5.0719999999999996e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Vehicles_1753","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The LS7 engine is how many cubic inches?\n\nOptions: \nA. 364\nB. 346\nC. 427\nD. 376\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The LS7 engine is a 7.0-liter V8 engine produced by General Motors, which translates to approximately 427 cubic inches. This engine was notably used in the Chevrolet Corvette Z06. \n\n\\boxe