put_tokens":133},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":0.00026710000000000004,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"ChessInstruct_119","prompt":"You are given a question about chess moves. Analyze the context carefully and provide the correct move.\n\nContext:\nGiven some set of chess moves, write the best possible move\n\nQuestion:\n{{\"moves\": [\"e2e4\", \"c7c5\", \"g1f3\", \"e7e6\", \"d2d4\", \"c5d4\", \"f3d4\", \"g8f6\", \"b1c3\", \"b8c6\", \"d4c6\", \"b7c6\", \"e4e5\", \"f6d5\", \"c3e4\", \"d8c7\", \"f2f4\", \"c6c5\", \"c2c4\", \"d5b4\", \"a2a3\", \"b4c6\", \"f1d3\", \"c6d4\", \"e1g1\", \"a7a5\", \"c1e3\", \"c8b7\", \"e4c3\", \"f8e7\", \"c3b5\", \"c7b6\", \"d1h5\"]}}\n\nInstructions:\n- State the correct chess move clearly.\n- Format your final answer as \\boxed{X}, where X is the move in standard coordinate notation (e.g., a2a3).\n- Keep your explanation or reasoning within 2–3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The given move sequence reaches a nonstandard but sharp Sicilian-style position in which White has just played Qh5 (attacking the loose h7-pawn and eyeing a possible invasion on f7). Black’s knight on d4 is ideally placed to deliver a forcing intermediate check by jumping to f3; the check compels the king to move (or the queen to be interposed) while simultaneously opening the long diagonal for the bishop on b7 and gaining a decisive tempo. All other candidate replies (…g6, …h6, …d5, etc.) allow White to maintain the initiative or regain material, whereas …Nf3 leaves Black with a decisive advantage.\n\n\\boxed{d4f3}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":420,"output_tokens":143},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":0.00015549999999999999,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"ChessInstruct_126","prompt":"You are given a question about chess moves. Analyze the context carefully and provide the correct move.\n\nContext:\nGiven some set of chess moves, write the best possible move\n\nQuestion:\n{{\"moves\": [\"e2e4\", \"c7c5\", \"g1f3\", \"d7d6\", \"d2d4\", \"c5d4\", \"d1d4\", \"b8c6\", \"d4e3\", \"g8f6\", \"b1c3\", \"g7g6\", \"h2h3\", \"f8g7\", \"f1e2\", \"c8e6\", \"e1g1\", \"a8c8\", \"f1d1\", \"e8g8\", \"a2a3\", \"f8e8\", \"c3d5\", \"e6d7\", \"c1d2\", \"f6d5\", \"e4d5\", \"c6e5\", \"f3e5\", \"g7e5\", \"e3b3\", \"d8b6\", \"b3b6\", \"a7b6\", \"c2c3\", \"d7a4\", \"d1c1\", \"c8c5\", \"e2f3\", \"c5a5\"]}}\n\nInstructions:\n- State the correct chess move clearly.\n- Format your final answer as \\boxed{X}, where X is the move in standard coordinate notation (e.g., a2a3).\n- Keep your explanation or reasoning within 2–3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The given sequence ends after Black's 20th move (...Ra5). In the resulting position, White's b-pawn remains on its starting square while Black's rook on a5 and bishop on a4 are both vulnerable along the queenside. Advancing the pawn with b2b4 therefore gains a tempo by attacking the rook; the same advance also restricts the bishop and opens lines for White's rook on c1. No other candidate (c3-c4, Bf3-e4, etc.) yields comparable material or positional gains.\n\n\\boxed{b2b4}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":462,"output_tokens":117},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":0.0001509,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"ChessInstruct_141","prompt":"You are given a question about chess moves. Analyze the context carefully and provide the correct move.\n\nContext:\nGiven some set of chess moves, write the best possible move\n\nQuestion:\n{{\"moves\": [\"d2d4\", \"d7d5\", \"c2c4\", \"c7c6\", \"e2e3\", \"g8f6\", \"f1e2\", \"e7e6\", \"g1f3\", \"f8e7\", \"e1g1\", \"b7b6\", \"b1c3\", \"e8g8\", \"b2b3\", \"c8b7\", \"c1b2\", \"b8d7\", \"a1c1\", \"a8c8\", \"h2h3\", \"f6e4\", \"e2d3\", \"f7f5\", \"c3e2\", \"e7d6\", \"f3e5\", \"e4f6\", \"e2f4\", \"d8e7\", \"d1e2\", \"f8d8\", \"c1c2\", \"c6c5\", \"f1c1\", \"c8c7\", \"c4d5\", \"f6d5\", \"f4d5\", \"b7d5\", \"e5c4\", \"d5c4\",