estions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following films was Don Bluth both the writer, director, and producer for?\n\nOptions: \nA. Anastasia\nB. The Land Before Time\nC. All Dogs Go To Heaven\nD. Titan A.E.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Don Bluth was the director and producer of *Anastasia*, but not the writer. He co-directed *The Land Before Time* and was a producer on *All Dogs Go to Heaven*, but did not serve in all three roles for those films. He was the writer, director, and producer for *Titan A.E.*, making D the correct answer.\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":111,"output_tokens":79}},"cost":6.183e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Entertainment: Cartoon & Animations_3210","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Nutcracker Suite was one of the musical pieces featured in Disney's 1940's film Fantasia.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The Nutcracker Suite was indeed featured in Disney's 1940 film *Fantasia*. It is one of the eight segments in the film, set to Tchaikovsky's music and visually depicting dancing flowers, insects, and fairies. \n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":110,"output_tokens":57}},"cost":4.85e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Entertainment: Cartoon & Animations_2826","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In \"Avatar: The Last Airbender\", which element does Aang begin to learn after being defrosted?\n\nOptions: \nA. Earth\nB. Water\nC. Fire\nD. Air\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Aang is the Avatar and was born an Airbender, so he already mastered airbending before being frozen. After being defrosted, the next element he begins to learn is waterbending, starting with Katara as his teacher. \n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":106,"output_tokens":57}},"cost":4.798e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Entertainment: Cartoon & Animations_675","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What town was \"Springfield\" from \"The Simpsons\" originally named after?\n\nOptions: \nA. Springfield, Illinois\nB. Springfield, Oregon\nC. Springfield, Missouri\nD. Springfield, Massachusetts\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The fictional town of Springfield in \"The Simpsons\" was inspired by Springfield, Oregon. Matt Groening, the creator of the show, named it after the town of Springfield, Oregon, which he recalled from the TV show \"Father Knows Best.\" This fact was confirmed by Groening himself in various interviews.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":106,"output_tokens":68}},"cost":5.4579999999999996e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Entertainment: Cartoon & Animations_3681","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How many episodes were in season five of Samurai Jack?\n\nOptions: \nA. 13\nB. 11\nC. 12\nD. 10\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Samurai Jack originally ran for four seasons on Cartoon Network (2001–2004). Its fifth season was the 2017 Adult Swim revival, which consisted of exactly ten half-hour episodes (aired weekly from March to May 2017 and concluding with the series finale “CI”). This count matches option D and rules out the higher episode totals listed in A–C.\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":218,"output_tokens":79},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":8.31e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Entertainment: Cartoon & Animations_835","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In The Simpsons, which war did Seymour Skinner serve in the USA Army as a Green Beret?\n\nOptions: \nA. World War 2\nB. Cold War\nC. Vietnam War\nD. World War 1\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Seymour Skinner, a character from The Simpsons, is depicted as a veteran who served in the Vietnam War. This is referenced multiple times throughout the series, including flashbacks and stories about his time as a prisoner of war. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":110,"output_tokens":59}},"cost":4.97e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Entertainment: Cartoon & Animations_1448","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: When did the last episode of \"Futurama\" air before returning in 2023?\n\nOptions: \nA. September 4, 2013\nB. March 28, 1999\nC. November 4, 2021\nD. December 25, 2010\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The original run of *Futurama* ended in 2003, after which four direct-to-DVD films aired in 2007–2009. The series was then revived for two additional seasons on Comedy Central that concluded with the episode “Meanwhile,” broadcast on 4 September 2013. The 2023 Hulu revival therefore follows directly after that 2013 finale, making option A the correct date.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":246,"output_tokens":88},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":9.32e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Entertainment: Cartoon & Animations_2146","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In \"My Little Pony: Friendship is Magic\", which of these ponies represents the quality of honesty?\n\nOptions: \nA. Rarity\nB. Pinkie Pie\nC. Twilight Sparkle\nD. Applejack\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Applejack is the pony who represents the Element of Honesty in \"My Little Pony: Friendship is Magic.\" She is known for her truthful nature and strong moral character. \n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":108,"output_tokens":40}},"cost":3.804e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Entertainme