 questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What are the Three Virtues of Bionicle?\n\nOptions: \nA. Work, Play, Live\nB. Forge, Build, Fight\nC. Unity, Duty, Destiny\nD. Build, Play, Change\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The Three Virtues of Bionicle are central themes in the Bionicle storyline, representing the core principles that guide the characters. These virtues are explicitly stated as Unity, Duty, and Destiny throughout the lore. \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \\boxed{C}.","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":109,"output_tokens":56}},"cost":4.7770000000000005e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Entertainment: Comics_3416","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Who was the inspiration for Cuthbert Calculus in the Tintin series?\n\nOptions: \nA. Will Morris\nB. Jacques Piccard\nC. J. Cecil Maby\nD. Auguste Picard\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The character Professor Cuthbert Calculus in the Tintin series was inspired by the Swiss physicist Auguste Piccard, a real-life scientist known for his work in high-altitude balloon flights and deep-sea exploration. Hergé, the creator of Tintin, modeled Calculus's appearance and eccentric personality on Piccard. \n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":109,"output_tokens":74}},"cost":5.857e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Entertainment: Comics_2958","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In \"Homestuck\" the \"Kingdom of Darkness\" is also known as?\n\nOptions: \nA. Derse\nB. Prospit\nC. Skaia\nD. The Medium\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"In \"Homestuck,\" the \"Kingdom of Darkness\" is associated with the moon Derse, which contrasts with Prospit, the \"Kingdom of Light.\" Derse is where dream selves often appear and is linked to darker, more chaotic forces in the game's mechanics. \n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":106,"output_tokens":65}},"cost":5.278e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Entertainment: Comics_324","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In Bionicle, who was formerly a Av-Matoran and is now the Toa of Light?\n\nOptions: \nA. Vakama\nB. Takua\nC. Tahu\nD. Jaller\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Takua was originally an Av-Matoran and later became the Toa of Light, playing a central role in the Bionicle story. He is known for his journey from a chronicler to a heroic Toa. \n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":109,"output_tokens":53}},"cost":4.597e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Entertainment: Comics_2349","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following rings from the DC Comics' \"Lantern Corps\" are classified as Parasitic?\n\nOptions: \nA. Indigo (Compassion)\nB. White (Life)\nC. Yellow (Fear)\nD. Green (Willpower)\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The parasitic rings in the DC Comics' Lantern Corps are those that forcibly bond to their hosts, impairing their free will. Among the options, the Indigo Ring of Compassion is known to be parasitic, as it often chooses unwilling hosts and alters their emotions. \n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":116,"output_tokens":62}},"cost":5.2279999999999994e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Entertainment: Comics_3437","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In what Homestuck Update was [S] Game Over released?\n\nOptions: \nA. October 25th, 2014\nB. April 8th, 2012\nC. August 28th, 2003\nD. April 13th, 2009\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The question asks for the release date of the Homestuck flash animation known as [S] Game Over (the climactic fight sequence resulting in multiple character deaths during Act 6).  \n\nHomestuck began on April 13, 2009 (eliminating option D) and the other listed dates correspond to unrelated milestones (e.g., early MSPA material or earlier flashes such as Cascade).  \n\nThe correct date for [S] Game Over is therefore October 25, 2014.  \n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":245,"output_tokens":105},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":0.0001015,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Entertainment: Comics_3801","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the real name of the \"Master Of Magnetism\" Magneto?\n\nOptions: \nA. Pietro Maximoff\nB. Johann Schmidt\nC. Charles Xavier\nD. Max Eisenhardt\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The real name of Magneto, also known as the \"Master of Magnetism,\" is Max Eisenhardt. This name reflects his canonical backstory in Marvel Comics, where he is a Holocaust survivor with the ability to control magnetic fields. Pietro Maximoff is Quicksilver, Johann Schmidt is Red Skull, and Charles Xavier is Professor X.\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":118,"output_tokens":85}},"cost":6.633999999999999e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Entertainment: Comics_3201","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the Hellboy universe, who founded the BPRD?\n\nOptions: \nA. Benjamin Daimio\nB. Kate Corrigan\nC. Trevor Bruttenholm\nD. Johann Kraus\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The BPRD (Bureau for Paranormal Research and Defense) was founded by Professor Trevor Bruttenholm, a key figure in the Hellboy universe and Hellboy's adoptive father. He established the organization to investigate and combat supernatural threats. \n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":106,"output_tokens":57}},"cost":4.798e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Entertainment: Comics_3181","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the webcomic \"Ava's Demon\", what sin is \"Nevy Nervine\" based off of? \n\nOptions: \nA. Sloth\nB. Wrath \nC. Envy \nD. Lust\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Nevy Nervine from \"Ava's Demon\" embodies the sin of Envy, as her character is deeply tied to feelings of jealousy and resentment, especially toward the protagonist Ava. Her motivations and emotional arc center around wanting what Ava has, both in terms of relationships and identity. \n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":110,"output_tokens":65}},"cost":5.33e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Entertainment: Comics_4013","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the comic book \"Archie\", Betty is friends with Veronica because she is rich.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The statement oversimplifies the relationship between Betty and Veronica in the \"Archie\" comic books. While Veronica is indeed wealthy, their friendship is based on more than just money—they are core members of the same social group and have a complex, sometimes competitive, but enduring bond. The idea that Betty is friends with Veronica solely because she is rich is inaccurate.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":92,"output_tokens":78}},"cost":5.876e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Entertainment: Comics_309