tions given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In \"Star Trek Nemesis\", why was Praetor Shinzon created?\n\nOptions: \nA. To replace Picard as a Romulan Agent\nB. To destroy the Enterprise\nC. To steal the Enterprise\nD. To become Picard's friend \n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Praetor Shinzon was created as a clone of Captain Jean-Luc Picard in order to infiltrate and eventually replace him, serving Romulan interests. His creation was part of a secret Romulan plan to use him as a biological weapon and agent. Therefore, the most accurate answer is that he was created to replace Picard as a Romulan agent.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":117,"output_tokens":79}},"cost":6.261e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Entertainment: Film_2506","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the correct phrase for the Latin saying \"Romanes Eunt Domus\" in Monty Python's Life of Brian?\n\nOptions: \nA. Romani Ite Domum\nB. Romans Go Home\nC. Roxani Ite Domum\nD. Tomate Ite Domum\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The phrase \"Romanes Eunt Domus\" is a humorous, incorrect Latin sentence from Monty Python's Life of Brian, meant to mock poor language instruction. The correct Latin translation of \"Romans Go Home\" would be \"Romani Ite Domum.\" This is both grammatically accurate and referenced in the film for comedic effect.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":125,"output_tokens":75}},"cost":6.125e-05,"accuracy":null},{