lgun\", how many \"sisters\" did Accelerator have to kill to achieve the rumored level 6?\n\nOptions: \nA. 10,000\nB. 20,000\nC. 128\nD. 5,000\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"In \"A Certain Scientific Railgun\", the Sisters Project involved creating clones of Misaka Mikoto, and Accelerator was tasked with fighting them to achieve Level 6. He was required to kill 20,000 Sisters, though the project was stopped before he could complete the final battle. \n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":130,"output_tokens":67}},"cost":5.709999999999999e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Entertainment: Japanese Anime & Manga_3268","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In Pokémon, Ash's Pikachu refuses to go into a pokeball.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Ash's Pikachu is famously known for preferring to stay outside of its Poké Ball and is often seen riding on Ash's shoulder. This trait is established early in the Pokémon anime series and remains consistent throughout the show. Therefore, the statement is accurate.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":103,"output_tokens":72}},"cost":5.658999999999999e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Entertainment: Japanese Anime & Manga_147","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In \"One Piece\", who confirms the existence of the legendary treasure, One Piece?\n\nOptions: \nA. Edward \"Whitebeard\" Newgate\nB. Silvers Rayleigh\nC. Former Marine Fleet Admiral Sengoku\nD. Pirate King Gol D Roger\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"D. Pirate King Gol D Roger is the one who confirms the existence of the legendary treasure, One Piece, by announcing it before his execution, which sets off the Great Pirate Era. He directly states that the treasure is real and is located at the end of the Grand Line. This proclamation inspires countless pirates to set sail in search of it.\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":119,"output_tokens":75}},"cost":6.047e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Entertainment: Japanese Anime & Manga_19","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In \"Highschool DxD\", what is the name of the item some humans are born with?\n\nOptions: \nA. Sacred Gear\nB. Hallowed Relic\nC. Imperial Arm\nD. Blessed Artifact\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"In \"Highschool DxD,\" the item that some humans are born with is called a Sacred Gear. These are powerful artifacts granted to chosen individuals, often granting them unique and potent abilities. \n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":108,"output_tokens":45}},"cost":4.104e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Entertainment: Japanese Anime & Manga_1431","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options 