 or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The statement is true based on documented details from Roald Dahl’s early drafts and editorial process for the 1964 novel. Publisher Knopf (via editor Virginia Kirkus) explicitly requested the change from a Black protagonist to a white one before publication, citing market concerns at the time. This is corroborated in biographies and interviews with Dahl’s estate, distinct from the separate (and later revised) racial issues with the Oompa-Loompas.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":212,"output_tokens":92},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":8.840000000000001e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_740","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What was the first ever entry written for the SCP Foundation collaborative writing project?\n\nOptions: \nA. SCP-173\nB. SCP-999\nC. SCP-1459\nD. SCP-001\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The first ever entry written for the SCP Foundation collaborative writing project was SCP-173. It was posted on the 4chan forum in 2007 and became the foundational piece for the entire SCP universe. This entry established the tone and format for future SCP articles.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":114,"output_tokens":63}},"cost":5.2619999999999994e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_769","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the \"Harry Potter\" series, what is Headmaster Dumbledore's ful