ect letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The Lies of Locke Lamora is set in a world whose dominant tongue is Therin (with Throne Therin as its archaic liturgical form). Within the text, Locke’s assumed surname is explicitly glossed by other characters as the Throne Therin word for “shadow,” underscoring his role as an unseen thief. None of the other offered glosses (justice, chaos, thievery) appear in the novel’s onomastic explanations.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":225,"output_tokens":92},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":9.1e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_1420","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the title of the first Sherlock Holmes book by Arthur Conan Doyle?\n\nOptions: \nA. The Sign of the Four\nB. A Study in Scarlet\nC. The Doings of Raffles Haw\nD. A Case of Identity\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The first Sherlock Holmes book written by Arthur Conan Doyle is \"A Study in Scarlet,\" published in 1887. It introduces the characters of Sherlock Holmes and Dr. Watson. The other options are either later Holmes stories or unrelated works.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":113,"output_tokens":55}},"cost":4.7690000000000006e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_1487","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is Hermione Granger's middle name?\n\nOptions: \nA. Jo\nB. Jane\nC. Jean\nD. Emma\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Hermione Granger's middle name is Jean, as confirmed by author J.K. Rowling in interviews and supplementary material. The name is often cited in official Harry Potter resources and fan references approved by Rowling. \n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":91,"output_tokens":49}},"cost":4.1229999999999997e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_1523","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which Russian author wrote the epic novel War and Peace?\n\nOptions: \nA. Vladimir Nabokov\nB. Fyodor Dostoyevsky\nC. Alexander Pushkin\nD. Leo Tolstoy\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Leo Tolstoy is the author of the epic novel *War and Peace*, which was published in the 1860s and is considered one of the greatest works of world literature. The other authors listed, while also significant in Russian literature, did not write this particular novel. \n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":108,"output_tokens":65}},"cost":5.304e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_1580","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the book \"The Martian\", how long was Mark Watney trapped on Mars (in Sols)?\n\nOptions: \nA. 401 Days\nB. 324 Days\nC. 549 Days\nD. 765 Days\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The novel tracks Watney’s ordeal in Martian sols (each ~24 h 39 m). The narrative opens on Sol 6 after the storm and ends with his rescue on Sol 549, a span explicitly confirmed in the text and author’s notes. The other listed figures correspond to Earth-day equivalents or unrelated intervals and are therefore incorrect.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":232,"output_tokens":72},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":8.24e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_1586","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The title of Adolf Hitler's autobiography \"Mein Kampf\" is what when translated to English?\n\nOptions: \nA. My Hatred\nB. My Sadness\nC. My Struggle\nD. My Desire\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The title \"Mein Kampf\" translates directly from German to English as \"My Struggle.\" This reflects the autobiographical and ideological nature of Adolf Hitler's book, outlining his political beliefs and life experiences. \n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":122,"output_tokens":60}},"cost":5.186e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_1688","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the fourth book of the Old Testament?\n\nOptions: \nA. Exodus\nB. Genesis\nC. Leviticus\nD. Numbers\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, wh