ed throughout the books and official sources.  \n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":91,"output_tokens":53}},"cost":4.363e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_2004","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Who wrote the novel 'Fear And Loathing In Las Vegas'?\n\nOptions: \nA. William S. Burroughs\nB. Hunter S. Thompson\nC. F. Scott Fitzgerald\nD. Henry Miller\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The novel *Fear and Loathing in Las Vegas* was written by Hunter S. Thompson, a pioneer of gonzo journalism. It was first published in 1971 and is based on his own experiences covering events in Las Vegas. The correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":108,"output_tokens":60}},"cost":5.004e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_2065","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How many books are in the Chronicles of Narnia series?\n\nOptions: \nA. 5\nB. 8\nC. 7\nD. 6\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The Chronicles of Narnia series consists of seven books, written by C.S. Lewis. The series includes classics such as *The Lion, the Witch and the Wardrobe* and *The Voyage of the Dawn Treader*. \n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":99,"output_tokens":52}},"cost":4.407e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_2131","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which fictional English county was the setting for Thomas Hardy's novels?\n\nOptions: \nA. Barsetshire\nB. Wessex\nC. Fulchester\nD. Ambridge\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Thomas Hardy's novels are famously set in a fictional region he called Wessex, which is based on the south and southwest of England. This imaginative landscape appears in works like *Tess of the d'Urbervilles* and *Far from the Madding Crowd*. The other options are fictional counties from different literary or radio contexts.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":100,"output_tokens":73}},"cost":5.679999999999999e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_2138","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What was the name of Captain Nemo's submarine in \"20,000 Leagues Under the Sea\"?\n\nOptions: \nA. The Nautilus\nB. The Neptune\nC. The Atlantis\nD. The Poseidon  \n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The correct answer is A. The Nautilus is the name of Captain Nemo's submarine in Jules Verne's novel \"20,000 Leagues Under the Sea.\" It is a fictional submarine powered by electricity and is central to the story's exploration of the ocean depths. \n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":112,"output_tokens":66}},"cost":5.416e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenT