n/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"In \"The Hobbit,\" Bard, a man from Lake-town, kills the dragon Smaug using a black arrow. Bilbo Baggins discovers Smaug's weak spot during their encounter, which helps Bard in the final attack. Frodo and Gandalf do not kill Smaug.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":103,"output_tokens":67}},"cost":5.3589999999999993e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_3000","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The \"Berenstein Bears\" is the correct spelling of the educational children's book series' name.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The correct spelling of the children's book series is \"Berenstain Bears,\" not \"Berenstein Bears.\" The name is often misremembered due to a phenomenon known as the Mandela effect. \n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":95,"output_tokens":48}},"cost":4.115e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_3056","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: \"Green Eggs And Ham\" is a book by which author?\n\nOptions: \nA. Dr. Seuss\nB. Beatrix Potter\nC. A.A. Milne\nD. Roald Dahl\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"\"Green Eggs and Ham\" is a classic children's book known for its playful rhymes and whimsical illustrations, characteristic of Dr. Seuss's style. The author, whose real name is Theodor Seuss Geisel, wrote and illustrated the book under the pen name Dr. Seuss. It was published in 1960 and remains one of his most popular works.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":106,"output_tokens":83}},"cost":6.358e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_3106","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: By what nickname is Jack Dawkins known in the Charles Dickens novel, 'Oliver Twist'?\n\nOptions: \nA. The Artful Dodger\nB. Fagin\nC. Bull’s-eye\nD. Mr. Fang\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Jack Dawkins is a character in Charles Dickens' *Oliver Twist* who is famously known for his skill in pickpocketing and cleverness. He is commonly referred to by his nickname, \"The Artful Dodger,\" which reflects his cunning and agility. Fagin is the leader of the gang, Bull’s-eye is Bill Sikes’s dog, and Mr. Fang is a magistrate.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":112,"output_tokens":88}},"cost":6.735999999999999e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_3157","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In The Lies of Locke Lamora, what title is Locke known by in the criminal world?\n\nOptions: \nA. The Thorn of the Marrows\nB. The Thorn of Camorr\nC. The Thorn of Emberlain\nD. The Rose of the Marrows\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"In *The Lies of Locke Lamora*, Locke is known by a title that reflects his cunning and impact on the criminal underworld of Camorr. The correct title associated with him is \"The Thorn of Camorr,\" symbolizing how he pricks and disrupts the established powers. \n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":119,"output_tokens":63}},"cost":5.3269999999999996e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_3339","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The book \"The Little Prince\" was written by...\n\nOptions: \nA. Jane Austen\nB. Antoine de Saint-Exupéry\nC. F. Scott Fitzgerald\nD. Miguel de Cervantes Saavedra\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The book \"The Little Prince\" was written by Antoine de Saint-Exupéry, a French aviator and author. It was first published in 1943 and has since become one of the most beloved and translated books in the world. The other authors listed wrote different famous works but not this one.\n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":112,"output_tokens":71}},"cost":5.716e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_3354","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Where does the book \"The Silence of the Lambs\" get its title from?\n\nOptions: \nA. The villain's favourite meal\nB. The main character's trauma in childhood\nC. The relation it has with killing the innocents\nD. The voice of innocent people being shut by the powerful\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The title \"The Silence of the Lambs\" refers to the protagonist Clarice Starling's traumatic memory of hearing lambs being slaughtered as a child, symbolizing her desire to protect the innocent and stop their suffering. This connects directly to her motivation and emotional drive throughout the story. \n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":126,"output_tokens":63}},"cost":5.418e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_3456","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the Harry Potter universe, who does Draco Malfoy end up marrying?\n\nOptions: \nA. Astoria Greengrass\nB. Pansy Parkinson\nC. Hermione Granger\nD. Millicent Bulstrode\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Draco Malfoy marries Astoria Greengrass in the Harry Potter universe, as confirmed by J.K. Rowling in post-series interviews and writings. Astoria is the younger sister of Daphne Greengrass, a fellow Slytherin student. This makes option A the correct answer.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":112,"output_tokens":68}},"cost":5.536e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_3490","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the name of the town in which Lily and James Potter are buried?\n\nOptions: \nA. Ottery St. Catchpole\nB. Godric's Hollow\nC. Hogsmeade\nD. Little Hangleton\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Lily and James Potter are buried in Godric's Hollow, the village where they lived before their deaths. This location is significant as it is also the birthplace of Harry Potter and the final resting place of other notable figures like Ignotus Peverell. \n\n\\boxed{B}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":112,"output_tokens":60}},"cost":5.0560000000000004e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_3516","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In Alice in Wonderland, what is the name of Alice's kitten?\n\nOptions: \nA. Heath\nB. Oscar\nC. Dinah\nD. Smokey\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"In *Alice's Adventures in Wonderland* by Lewis Carroll, Alice's kitten is named Dinah, who is mentioned frequently in the story as her beloved pet. The other options—Heath, Oscar, and Smokey—are not characters from the book. \n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":99,"output_tokens":59}},"cost":4.827e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_3520","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the Lord of the Rings, who is the father of the dwarf Gimli?\n\nOptions: \nA. Dwalin\nB. Thorin Oakenshield\nC. Bombur\nD. Gloin\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The father of Gimli in The Lord of the Rings is Gloin, one of the dwarves who accompanied Thorin Oakenshield in *The Hobbit*. This is confirmed in both *The Hobbit* and *The Lord of the Rings*. \n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":108,"output_tokens":59}},"cost":4.944e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_3570","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the Magic: The Gathering universe, the Fallen Empires expansion takes place on which continent?\n\nOptions: \nA. Sarpadia\nB. Shiv\nC. Terisiare\nD. Otaria\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Fallen Empires is an early MTG expansion whose flavor text and world-building explicitly place its events (the collapse of elven, dwarven, orcish, and thrull civilizations) on the continent of Sarpadia, a landmass on Dominaria.  \nBy contrast, Terisiare hosts the Brothers’ War / Antiquities / Ice Age cycle, Shiv is the volcanic region tied to the Viashino and later Weatherlight stories, and Otaria is the setting of the Odyssey / Onslaught blocks.  \nThus the only option that matches the canonical location is A.\n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":227,"output_tokens":121},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":0.0001059,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_3586","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which author co-wrote \"The Communist Manifesto\" alongside Karl Marx?\n\nOptions: \nA. Paul Lafargue\nB. Robert Owen\nC. Friedrich Engels\nD. Alexander Kerensky\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Friedrich Engels co-wrote \"The Communist Manifesto\" with Karl Marx in 1848. The pamphlet was commissioned by the Communist League and is one of the most influential political documents in history. Engels and Marx collaborated closely on many works, with Engels providing both intellectual and financial support.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":106,"output_tokens":70}},"cost":5.578e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_3621","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What's the second book in George R. R. Martin's 'A Song of Ice and Fire' series?\n\nOptions: \nA. A Storm of Swords\nB. A Feast for Crows\nC. A Clash of Kings\nD. A Dance with Dragons\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The second book in George R. R. Martin's 'A Song of Ice and Fire' series is \"A Clash of Kings.\" The series follows the order: *A Game of Thrones*, *A Clash of Kings*, *A Storm of Swords*, *A Feast for Crows*, and *A Dance with Dragons*. Therefore, the correct answer is C.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":118,"output_tokens":79}},"cost":6.274e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_3687","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Who was the author of the 1954 novel, \"Lord of the Flies\"?\n\nOptions: \nA. Hunter Fox\nB. F. Scott Fitzgerald\nC. William Golding\nD. Stephen King\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The author of the 1954 novel \"Lord of the Flies\" is William Golding. This novel is a classic of British literature, exploring themes of civilization and savagery through the story of a group of boys stranded on an island. The correct answer is C.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":109,"output_tokens":64}},"cost":5.257e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_3816","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: According to The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy book, the answer to life, the universe and everything else is...\n\nOptions: \nA. Loving everyone around you\nB. Chocolate\nC. 42\nD. Death\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The correct answer is based on a famous plot point in *The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy* by Douglas Adams, where a supercomputer named Deep Thought calculates the Answer to the Ultimate Question of Life, the Universe, and Everything. After much anticipation, the answer revealed is simply \"42.\" This humorous and absurd result is central to the book's satire of the search for meaning.\n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":112,"output_tokens":86}},"cost":6.616e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_3845","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The book \"Fahrenheit 451\" was written by whom?\n\nOptions: \nA. Stephen King\nB. R. L. Stine\nC. Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart\nD. Ray Bradbury\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The book \"Fahrenheit 451\" is a well-known dystopian novel about censorship and a future society where books are banned and burned. It was written by Ray Bradbury, a prominent American author of science fiction and fantasy literature. The other options are incorrect: Stephen King and R. L. Stine are authors of horror and children's books, respectively, and Mozart was a composer.\n\n\\boxed{D}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":109,"output_tokens":87}},"cost":6.636999999999999e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_3886","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What book series published by Jim Butcher follows a wizard in modern day Chicago?\n\nOptions: \nA. A Hat in Time\nB. The Cinder Spires\nC. The Dresden Files\nD. My Life as a Teenage Wizard\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The book series that follows a wizard in modern-day Chicago is The Dresden Files by Jim Butcher. This series features Harry Dresden, a wizard who works as a private investigator. \n\n\\boxed{C}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":112,"output_tokens":42}},"cost":3.976e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"OpenTDB_Entertainment: Books_3907","prompt":"Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What was the last message of the Dolphins in \"The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy\"?\n\nOptions: \nA. \"So long, and thanks for all the fish.\"\nB. \"Land of the brave.\"\nC. \"The answer is 42.\"\nD. \"Goodbye cruel world!\"\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The dolphins in \"The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy\" left Earth just before its destruction and were known for their intelligence and appreciation of humanity. Their final message, as revealed in the story, was a humorous and poignant farewell. The correct answer is: \n\n\\boxed{A}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":126,"output_tokens":60}},"cost":5.2379999999999997e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"QANTA_Literature_1195","prompt":"Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A popular conspiracy theory held by tax protesters is that some parties in court cases do not actually exist since they are identified exclusively through the use of this technique.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The question pertains to a fringe legal theory (popular among \"sovereign citizens\" and tax protesters) holding that a court's use of stylized typography creates a fictitious corporate entity rather than referring to a natural person. This is the basis for the so-called \"strawman\" argument, in which only the all-caps version of a name is thought to appear in court filings, contracts, etc. Consequently, the technique in question is the rendering of names in all capital letters.\n\n\\boxed{ALL CAPS names (strawman theory)\n}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":211,"output_tokens":110},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":9.72e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"QANTA_Literature_1203","prompt":"Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Seven brothers with this last name all fought at Edgehill, and one of them, John, surrendered Chester to the Parliamentarians.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The query pertains to a notable episode from the English Civil War. The 1642 Battle of Edgehill is recorded as having been attended by seven royalist brothers of the same family, one of whom (John) later became governor of Chester and surrendered the city to Parliament in February 1646. Contemporary sources and later histories identify that family as the Byrons of Newstead (Sir John Byron’s seven sons).\n\nThus the required surname is Byron.\n\n\\boxed{Byron}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":206,"output_tokens":96},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":8.92e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"QANTA_Literature_1052","prompt":"Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Lord Howard helped secure this son of a tailor a seat in Parliament.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The question is a historical clue identifying a British MP. Samuel Pepys’s father was a London tailor, and Pepys himself sat in Parliament for Castle Rising (1673) and later Bramber. Contemporary records show that Lord Henry Howard (later 6th Duke of Norfolk) used his family interest to secure the Castle Rising seat for Pepys.\n\nThus the person referenced is Samuel Pepys.\n\n\\boxed{Samuel Pepys}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":194,"output_tokens":87},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":8.23e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"QANTA_Literature_620","prompt":"Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: One member of this title group asserts that all militaries must be \"the finest in the world\" although navies are measured by tonnage.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The phrasing of the query is characteristic of a quizbowl-style clue, which points to a group sharing an identical proper name (i.e., a “title group”). Both states that bear that name routinely issue propaganda or official statements claiming to field “the strongest/finest military in the world,” yet objective naval rankings are performed by aggregate tonnage—a metric that separates the two claimants. The only polity pair that satisfies every element of the clue is therefore the two Koreas.\n\n\\boxed{the (two) Koreas}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":208,"output_tokens":104},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":9.36e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"QANTA_Literature_1239","prompt":"Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This food, which pejoratively gave its name to Taiwan's millennial generation, was reclaimed as a badge of honor a ter a 2008 student protest.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The 2008 Wild Strawberry Student Movement protested restrictions on freedom of assembly and explicitly adopted the “strawberry” label that had been used to disparage Taiwan’s millennials (seen as fragile like the fruit). By turning the epithet into the name of their movement, participants reclaimed it as a positive symbol of youthful activism. Consequently, the food referenced in the clue is the strawberry.\n\n\\boxed{strawberry (gen./movement)\n}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":212,"output_tokens":89},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":8.69e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"QANTA_Literature_782","prompt":"Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Giles Allen sued the owners of this location for transporting a building from his land to this place while he was on vacation.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Giles Allen sued the owners of the Globe Theatre for dismantling the Theatre in Shoreditch and transporting its materials to build the Globe on the South Bank of the Thames while he was away. He was the landlord and claimed the structure was his property. The most common answer to this question is the Globe Theatre.\n\n\\boxed{Globe Theatre}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":83,"output_tokens":71}},"cost":5.339e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"QANTA_Literature_435","prompt":"Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Michel Foucault coined the term \"noso-politics\" in an essay which discusses the integration of public and private administration of this profession during the 18th century.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Michel Foucault used the term \"noso-politics\" to describe the political and administrative management of disease, particularly in the context of medicine and public health. He discussed how the administration of health became intertwined with state power during the 18th century, blurring lines between public and private medical practices. The profession in question is medicine.\n\n\\boxed{medicine}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":95,"output_tokens":77}},"cost":5.855e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"QANTA_Literature_1345","prompt":"Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This playwright was translated and  rst introduced to the U.S. by an actor who later became a Hollywood star playing Dr. Fu Manchu and Charlie Chan.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The actor in question is Warner Oland, who originated the film roles of Dr. Fu Manchu and Charlie Chan. Because Oland was Swedish-American, the playwright he first translated into English and introduced to U.S. stages had to be Swedish; the only major dramatist who fits the chronology and facts is August Strindberg (whose works Oland rendered in the 1910s). No other European playwright of the era matches both the translator’s identity and the “first introduced to the U.S.” claim.\n\n\\boxed{August Strindberg}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":212,"output_tokens":112},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":9.84e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"QANTA_Literature_1067","prompt":"Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A form of one of these events in African-American tradition provides the title for Yaa Gyasi's (JAH-see's)  \n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The clue refers to Yaa Gyasi's 2016 debut novel whose title is a single word, \"Homegoing.\" In African-American tradition a \"homegoing\" (or home-going) service is a celebratory funeral rite marking the deceased's passage to the afterlife; therefore the category being defined by the clue is funerals.\n\n\\boxed{funerals (homegoings)}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":207,"output_tokens":76},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":7.94e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"QANTA_Literature_1128","prompt":"Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: After a writer from  Wallpaper  magazine described this language as \"one of the ugliest\" in the world, billionaire Johann Rupert pulled several ads in response.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The language in question is Afrikaans. Johann Rupert, a prominent South African businessman, withdrew advertising from Wallpaper magazine after it insulted Afrikaans by calling it \"one of the ugliest\" languages. This sparked national outrage in South Africa, leading to the ad boycott.\n\n\\boxed{Afrikaans}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":91,"output_tokens":64}},"cost":5.023e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"QANTA_Literature_1073","prompt":"Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A theatrical director named Felix stars in Margaret Atwood's 2016 adaptation of this play,  Hag-Seed .\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The question appears to be asking for the play that Margaret Atwood's *Hag-Seed* is an adaptation of. *Hag-Seed* is a modern retelling of William Shakespeare's *The Tempest*. Therefore, the correct answer is *The Tempest*.\n\n\\boxed{The Tempest}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":85,"output_tokens":65}},"cost":5.005e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"QANTA_Literature_795","prompt":"Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An analogue of this figure is said to be the only one of the giant race of the jentillak (JEN-tee-lahk) to survive the arrival of Christianity.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The clue describes Olentzero, the last surviving member of the jentillak (a race of Basque giants said to have vanished with the arrival of Christianity). Olentzero is a folkloric Christmas gift-bringer whose role and attributes are directly analogous to those of the modern Santa Claus/Father Christmas figure.  \n\nThus the referent of “this figure” is Santa Claus.  \n\n\\boxed{Santa Claus}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":218,"output_tokens":84},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":8.56e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"QANTA_Literature_50","prompt":"Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Meisei University in Tokyo houses a copy of this document through which a bullet has penetrated half the pages.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The clue describes a multi-page historical book (not a single-sheet parchment such as Magna Carta) that is known to contain a bullet hole passing through roughly the first half of its leaves. Meisei University’s rare-book collection includes one of the surviving copies of the 42-line Gutenberg Bible; that exemplar still bears the documented bullet hole, which is believed to have occurred during 20th-century conflict. No other widely referenced document matches both the physical detail and the stated institutional provenance.\n\n\\boxed{Gutenberg Bible}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":201,"output_tokens":102},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":9.12e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"QANTA_Literature_1440","prompt":"Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In The Old Curiosity Shop, Nell and her grandfather are taken in by a man of this profession named Mr. Marton.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The novel in question is Dickens's *The Old Curiosity Shop*. After fleeing Quilp and enduring various hardships on the road, Nell and her grandfather are given shelter in a rural village by its kindly schoolmaster, Mr. Marton, who also employs Nell as an assistant. Thus the profession referenced is schoolmaster (or, equivalently, teacher).\n\n\\boxed{schoolmaster (teacher)}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":205,"output_tokens":77},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":7.95e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"QANTA_Literature_1801","prompt":"Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A polio epidemic strikes a summer camp in this state in a 2010 novel whose author claimed it to be his last.  \n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The clue describes Philip Roth’s 2010 novel *Nemesis*, which the author publicly stated would be his last. In the book a polio outbreak reaches the boys’ summer camp at which the protagonist is working; that camp is located in the Poconos. The Poconos lie in Pennsylvania, so the state referenced by the clue is Pennsylvania.\n\n\\boxed{Pennsylvania}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":206,"output_tokens":77},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":7.970000000000001e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"QANTA_Literature_980","prompt":"Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: To worship a god represented by these animals, a character recites nonsense lineages such as \"\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The query provides an incomplete clue describing a fictional religious practice (nonsense genealogies recited to honor a deity whose form or avatars are the animals in question). This is a recognizable reference to the feline cult in Neil Gaiman’s Sandman story “A Dream of a Thousand Cats,” where cats worship a great feline goddess and intone absurd ancestral lists. Hence the animals are cats.\n\n\\boxed{cats (Gaiman's Sandman)}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":198,"output_tokens":87},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":8.31e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"QANTA_Literature_1692","prompt":"Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In this work, \"Knot Taps\" are shown graf ti-ing buildings with the outlines of lovers embracing as if vaporized by the blast at Hiroshima.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The work described is *Watchmen* by Alan Moore and Dave Gibbons, in which the character Rorschach mentions \"Knot Taps\" graffiti depicting embracing figures reminiscent of the Hiroshima shadows. This imagery symbolizes the ever-present threat of nuclear annihilation. The correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{Watchmen}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":92,"output_tokens":66}},"cost":5.156e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"QANTA_Literature_1524","prompt":"Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The centrality of these concepts in Europe began with a translation and commentary written \"in the vulgar language\" by Lodovico Castelvetro.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The question refers to the translation and commentary by Lodovico Castelvetro on Aristotle's *Poetics*, which was highly influential in spreading classical dramatic theory in Renaissance Europe. Castelvetro's work was written in Italian (the \"vulgar language\") rather than Latin, making it accessible to a broader audience. This helped establish the centrality of concepts like the unities of time, place, and action in European literary theory.\n\n\\boxed{Aristotle's Poetics}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":89,"output_tokens":101}},"cost":7.217e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"QANTA_Literature_1185","prompt":"Please 