\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In 2016, the golden lantern-like cap of a 123-floor \"World Tower\" in this city was finished.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The clue describes the completion of the distinctive golden crown on Lotte World Tower (also styled as a “lantern”), a 123-floor skyscraper whose structural topping-out occurred in December 2016.  \nThe building’s official name contains the phrase “World Tower,” directly matching the quoted wording in the question.  \nNo other 123-story tower finished a comparable lantern-like cap in that year, confirming the city as Seoul.\n\n\\boxed{Seoul}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":205,"output_tokens":91},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":8.65e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"QANTA_Geography_686","prompt":"Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: It's not Georgia, but a festival with the slogan \"Give Peach a Chance\" is held in this state's city of Ruston.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The festival with the slogan \"Give Peach a Chance\" is held in Ruston, Louisiana, not Georgia. This annual event celebrates local culture and music, playing on the word \"peach\" humorously despite Louisiana not being known for peaches like Georgia. The correct answer is Louisiana.\n\n\\boxed{Louisiana}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":87,"output_tokens":65}},"cost":5.031e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"QANTA_Geography_830","prompt":"Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Anthropologists like Georg Steindorff investigated traditional homosexual behavior in a town in one of these natural features.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The question refers to anthropologist Georg Steindorff's work in Egypt, where he studied traditional social behaviors, including same-sex relationships, in communities along the Nile River. The \"natural feature\" in question is therefore a river. \n\n\\boxed{river}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":81,"output_tokens":54}},"cost":4.2930000000000004e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"QANTA_Geography_856","prompt":"Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A massive 2,000-year-old system for growing this crop was built by the Igorot  (ego-ROTE)  inhabitants of the Ifugao  \n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The massive 2,000-year-old system built by the Igorot people of the Ifugao is for growing rice. This system is known as the Ifugao Rice Terraces, often called the \"Eighth Wonder of the World.\" These terraces were carved into mountain slopes to cultivate rice using sophisticated irrigation methods.\n\n\\boxed{rice}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":95,"output_tokens":73}},"cost":5.6149999999999996e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"QANTA_Geography_863","prompt":"Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: One of these places in Stockholm is supposedly haunted by the Silverpilen, or \"Silver Arrow\", and features a huge fresco depicting a timeline of human civilization at Rissen.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The clue describes a category of locations in Stockholm linked by two distinctive features: the urban legend of the ghost train Silverpilen (which is said to appear only at abandoned or little-used stops on the tunnelbana network) and the large historical fresco at Rissne station. Both details unambiguously identify the Stockholm metro (T-bana) stations as the common set. Hence the answer to the “one of these places” prompt is the Stockholm metro stations themselves.\n\n\\boxed{Stockholm metro stations (T-bana)}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":215,"output_tokens":105},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":9.55e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"QANTA_Geography_917","prompt":"Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In this country, the office of the newspaper  Respublika  was firebombed in 2002 shortly after a decapitated dog was hung from that building with the note \"There will be no next time.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The incident involving the firebombing of the Respublika newspaper office and the decapitated dog occurred in Kazakhstan. This was in response to the newspaper's critical reporting and alleged insults toward the president. The country is known for suppressing press freedom, and this event highlighted the dangers faced by journalists there.\n\n\\boxed{Kazakhstan}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":108,"output_tokens":70}},"cost":5.604e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"QANTA_Geography_939","prompt":"Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An organization based in this European city awards the Wateler Prize and was established after Andrew White convinced Andrew Carnegie to fund a palace.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The organization referred to is the Permanent Court of Arbitration, which is based in The Hague, Netherlands. The Carnegie Foundation, funded by Andrew Carnegie and established through the efforts of Andrew White, built the Peace Palace in The Hague to house this institution. The Wateler Peace Prize is awarded annually by a Dutch foundation based in The Hague.\n\n\\boxed{The Hague}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":85,"output_tokens":74}},"cost":5.5450000000000006e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"QANTA_Geography_954","prompt":"Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The brother of a ruler of this country died while defending that ruler's residence of Dasman Palace.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The country in question is Kuwait. The brother of Emir Jaber Al-Ahmad Al-Sabah, Sheikh Faisal Al-Sabah, died while defending Dasman Palace during the Iraqi invasion in 1990. \n\n\\boxed{Kuwait}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":79,"output_tokens":56}},"cost":4.3870000000000005e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"QANTA_Geography_968","prompt":"Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This city contains a set of nine kinetic art sculptures depicting the Muses by Troy Pillow located at the corners of the namesake intersection of its 9th and 9th neighborhood.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The city described is Salt Lake City, Utah, where the \"9th & 9th\" neighborhood features a series of kinetic art sculptures of the Muses by artist Troy Pillow, installed at the intersection of 9th South and 9th East.\n\nThese sculptures are part of a public art initiative to enhance the cultural vibrancy of the area.\n\n\\boxed{Salt Lake City}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":96,"output_tokens":79}},"cost":5.988e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"QANTA_Geography_986","prompt":"Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: It was revealed in 2016 that this man corrected the author's factual inaccuracies about the speed of a boat in  The Story of a Shipwrecked Sailor  and a rifle in  Chronicle of a Death Foretold  while serving as an unofficial copy-editor for his friend Gabriel García\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The query is a reference to a 2016 revelation (from letters and interviews published after García Márquez's death) about an unofficial proofreader who fixed specific technical details in two of the author's early works. The individual in question was Germán Vargas Cantillo, a member of the Barranquilla Group and lifelong friend of García Márquez who routinely performed this service. (Álvaro Mutis and Plinio Apuleyo Mendoza were also close friends but did not perform the copy-editing role described.)\n\n\\boxed{Germán Vargas Cantillo}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":240,"output_tokens":109},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":0.0001025,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"QANTA_Geography_1013","prompt":"Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Massive parades of jeeps called  yipao  honor this country's farmers and are held in cities like Armenia and Calarcá.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The \"yipao\" parades are a cultural tradition in Colombia, where decorated jeeps are showcased to honor coffee farmers. These parades are especially prominent in the Colombian Coffee-Growing Axis, including cities like Armenia and Calarcá. The correct answer is Colombia.\n\n\\boxed{Colombia}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":88,"output_tokens":63}},"cost":4.9239999999999996e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"QANTA_Geography_1023","prompt":"Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This city was the site of the so-called \"Trefa  (TRAY-fuh)  \n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The Trefa Banquet of 1883 was held to celebrate the first graduating class of Hebrew Union College. The serving of non-kosher (trefa) dishes at the event in Cincinnati offended traditionalist rabbis and helped trigger the eventual split between Reform and Conservative branches of American Judaism. Because the college itself was located in Cincinnati, that city is the site referenced by the clue.\n\n\\boxed{Cincinnati}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":201,"output_tokens":84},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":8.219999999999999e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"QANTA_Geography_1100","prompt":"Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A building in this city contains an installation called  Fiori di Como  that consists of more than 2,000 Dale Chihuly-blown glass flowers.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The installation \"Fiori di Como\" by Dale Chihuly is located in Las Vegas. It is situated in the Bellagio Hotel and Casino, where it adorns the lobby with its vibrant, hand-blown glass flowers. \n\n\\boxed{Las Vegas}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":94,"output_tokens":56}},"cost":4.5820000000000005e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"QANTA_Geography_1116","prompt":"Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A locomotive passes by one of these animals in a notable diamond-shaped postage stamp from the short-lived Tuvan People's Republic.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The clue describes a specific philatelic curiosity: the Tuvan People's Republic (1921–1944) produced a series of diamond-shaped stamps, one of which depicts a steam locomotive passing a camel. Because the question is phrased in the “one of these animals” style typical of quiz-bowl or crossword clues, the expected referent is simply the animal shown on that stamp—camels. No other animal appears in the well-documented Tuva locomotive scene, confirming the answer.\n\n\\boxed{camels}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":204,"output_tokens":103},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":9.23e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"QANTA_Geography_1148","prompt":"Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The Vitousek lab uses a four-million-year chronosequence in this region to understand the successional dynamics of nutrient cycling.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The Vitousek lab studies nutrient cycling using a four-million-year chronosequence in Hawaii.\n\nThis long-term ecological research focuses on how soil nutrients and ecosystems change over time on volcanic landscapes.\n\n\\boxed{Hawaii}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":85,"output_tokens":45}},"cost":3.805e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"QANTA_Geography_1192","prompt":"Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This city is home to a UFO-shaped ice cream parlor called Coppelia, which was founded by a world leader.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The city described is Havana, Cuba. Coppelia is a famous UFO-shaped ice cream parlor founded in 1966 and named after a ballet, inspired by revolutionary leader Che Guevara's interest in making ice cream accessible to all Cubans. It is often associated with the Cuban Revolution's leaders, though not directly founded by Fidel Castro.\n\n\\boxed{Havana}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":83,"output_tokens":79}},"cost":5.8190000000000004e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"QANTA_Geography_1211","prompt":"Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Long tracking shots of this desert are coupled with audio of  lm scholar Lotte Eisner reading from the Popol Vuh in Werner Herzog's early documentary Fata Morgana.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The clue describes a key sequence from Werner Herzog's 1971 experimental documentary *Fata Morgana*. That film consists almost entirely of extended tracking shots across the dunes and salt flats of the Sahara (primarily in southern Algeria and Morocco), over which Lotte Eisner recites passages from the Popol Vuh. No other desert is featured in the picture, so the referent is unambiguously the Sahara.\n\n\\boxed{Sahara (desert)}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":216,"output_tokens":88},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":8.72e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"QANTA_Geography_1252","prompt":"Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: n an e5fort to revitalize a town in this state, sculptor Gary Gre5f placed massive metal statues of pheasants, grasshoppers, and deer along its so called \"Enchanted Highway.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The Enchanted Highway is a stretch of road in North Dakota featuring large metal sculptures created by artist Gary Greff to revitalize the area. These sculptures include pheasants, grasshoppers, and deer, among other whimsical figures. The state is North Dakota.\n\n\\boxed{North Dakota}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":105,"output_tokens":63}},"cost":5.145e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"QANTA_Geography_1334","prompt":"Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In this city in the 1930s, the meteorologist Wilhelm Gustlo f organized a local Nazi party before being shot by the young Jew David Frankfurter, an event described in Gunter Grass's novel Crabwalk.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The city referred to is Königsberg, where Wilhelm Gustloff founded the Swiss branch of the Nazi Party and was later assassinated by David Frankfurter in 1936. This event is depicted in Günter Grass's novel *Crabwalk*. Königsberg is now the Russian city of Kaliningrad, but in the 1930s, it was part of Germany.\n\n\\boxed{Königsberg}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":107,"output_tokens":91}},"cost":6.851e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"QANTA_Geography_1335","prompt":"Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Emmeline Pankhurst's daughter Sylvia was invited to live in this city in 1956 a ter supporting an anticolonial movement in the 1930s and 1940s.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"Sylvia Pankhurst was invited to live in Addis Ababa, Ethiopia, in 1956 after her long-standing support for the Ethiopian resistance against Italian colonization in the 1930s and 1940s. She was a passionate anti-colonial activist and developed strong ties with Emperor Haile Selassie. Her contributions were recognized by the Ethiopian government, which invited her to reside in the capital.\n\n\\boxed{Addis Ababa}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":104,"output_tokens":100}},"cost":7.352e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"QANTA_Geography_1356","prompt":"Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: One of this province's \"ten strange wonders\" is a food with an infamously complex name that requires 58 strokes to write.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The food in question is \"biángbiáng miàn,\" a type of Chinese noodle known for the complexity of the character \"biáng,\" which requires 58 strokes to write. This dish is associated with Shaanxi province, famous for its unique local cuisine and cultural quirks. \n\n\\boxed{Shaanxi}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":88,"output_tokens":69}},"cost":5.2839999999999996e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"QANTA_Geography_1407","prompt":"Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Local legend holds that Muhammad safely landed in this country at a cove called the Prophet's Hole.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The question refers to the first Hijra (flight of persecuted early Muslims from Mecca), who sailed across the Red Sea to safety in the Aksumite kingdom. Historical and local tradition places their landing at a coastal inlet on the territory of the modern state of Eritrea, which is still known as the “Prophet’s Hole.” (Ethiopia is sometimes mentioned because of the ancient kingdom’s extent, but the Red-Sea littoral in question lies in present-day Eritrea.)\n\n\\boxed{Eritrea}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":200,"output_tokens":100},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":9e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"QANTA_Geography_1414","prompt":"Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Rotoscoped archival footage of an event that took place in this city is interspersed with eyewitness interviews in a 2016 Kevin Maitland documentary.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The 2016 Kevin Maitland documentary refers to *The Birth of a Nation*, which includes rotoscoped archival footage and interviews related to the 1913 premiere of D.W. Griffith’s film in Los Angeles. The event in question—the controversial release and reception of the original *Birth of a Nation*—took place in Los Angeles. \n\n\\boxed{Los Angeles}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":94,"output_tokens":82}},"cost":6.141999999999999e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"QANTA_Geography_1448","prompt":"Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This peninsula will eventually be connected to the mainland by the planned Parallel Thimble Shoal Tunnel.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The clue refers to a planned expansion of the Chesapeake Bay Bridge-Tunnel (CBBT) in Hampton Roads, Virginia. The existing CBBT already links the Virginia mainland (near Virginia Beach) to the southern tip of the Eastern Shore via the Thimble Shoal Tunnel and other segments; the parallel tunnel simply adds a second bore for capacity and safety. Thus the peninsula in question is the Eastern Shore of Virginia (the southern portion of the Delmarva Peninsula).\n\n\\boxed{Eastern Shore (VA)}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":200,"output_tokens":103},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":9.15e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"QANTA_Geography_1516","prompt":"Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Before directing the London Fire Brigade, James Braidwood organized the  rst modern municipal  re brigade in this city, where he helped  ght an 1824 \"Great Fire\" that destroyed the studio of caricaturist John Kay.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"James Braidwood organized the first modern municipal fire brigade in Edinburgh, where he helped fight the 1824 \"Great Fire\" that destroyed the studio of caricaturist John Kay. He later went on to lead the London Fire Brigade. The correct answer is Edinburgh.\n\n\\boxed{Edinburgh}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":122,"output_tokens":71}},"cost":5.846e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"QANTA_Geography_1555","prompt":"Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Welsh immigrants to this region founded a settlement called Y Wladfa (oh lad-vah).\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The Welsh settlement known as Y Wladfa (founded in 1865) was established by immigrants in the Chubut Valley of Argentina. This area lies within the broader geographic and cultural region of Patagonia. The name and history are unique to that location and are not associated with Welsh colonies elsewhere.\n\n\\boxed{Patagonia (Chubut, Arg.)}\n\n}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":199,"output_tokens":75},"model_used":"x-ai/grok-4.3"},"cost":7.73e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"QANTA_Geography_1657","prompt":"Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Bally Manufacturing's attempt to corner this city's leisure industry in the 1970s hit a snag when preservationists objected to its planned demolition of the MarlboroughÂ–Blenheim Hotel.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The city in question is Atlantic City, where Bally Manufacturing planned to build a casino in the 1970s but faced opposition due to the proposed demolition of the historic Marlborough–Blenheim Hotel. Preservationists argued for the protection of the architecturally significant structure, which delayed Bally's plans. This event was part of the larger transformation of Atlantic City into a gambling hub.\n\n\\boxed{Atlantic City}","success":true,"token_usage":{"input_tokens":101,"output_tokens":86}},"cost":6.473e-05,"accuracy":null},{"global index":"QANTA_Geography_1707","prompt":"Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: On April 23, lovers in the four provinces of this region celebrate a holiday in which men give women roses in exchange for books.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.","prediction":"grok-4-1-fast-reasoning","generated_result":{"generated_answer":"The holiday described is the Catalan celebration of Sant Jordi (St. George's Day) on April 23, which features the traditional